insert into public.platform_updates (pr_number,title,summary,merged_at,url) values
(2,'Replace sports platform text with logo images throughout the application','This PR replaces text-based platform names with actual logo images for all supported sports betting platforms including Betway, SportingBet, Playabets, Betfair, Hollywoodbets, Stake, Betfred, and 10bet. ### Code Updates - **Updated `src/lib/mock-data.ts`**: Changed platforms from a string array to a typed Platform array with name and logo properties. Added Stake and Betfred to the list. - **Updated `src/components/affiliate.tsx`**: Modified PlatformRail component to render logo images instead of text while maintaining existing styling and hover effects. - **Updated `src/components/layout/app-shell.tsx`**: Updated LeftRail platforms section to display logo images with proper styling. ### Documentation - **Created `public/logos/README.md`**: Added comprehensive documentation with links to all logo images from the GitHub issue. - **Created `public/logos/.gitkeep`**: Ensures the logos directory is tracked by git.','2026-08-03T20:06:37Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/2'),
(4,'Implement comprehensive legal pages for Terms & Conditions, Privacy Statement, and Cookie Preferences','This PR implements comprehensive, brand-consistent, and functional pages for legal compliance and user information:','2026-08-04T14:39:34Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/4'),
(6,'Implement Auth Prompt, AI Chatbot Visibility Control, and Responsive Logo Handling','This PR implements three key features to improve user experience and engagement: **1. AI Chatbot Button Visibility Control** - Hides the floating PuntAI chatbot button on the homepage when users are not logged in - Maintains visibility on all other pages and when users are logged in as guests **2. Login/Signup Prompt Component** - Created a dismissible auth prompt that slides up from the bottom of the screen - Triggers on first visit to the homepage for non-logged-in users - Re-appears every 7 days if the user hasn''t signed up or logged in - Uses localStorage to track visit history and prompt timing - Responsive design: full-width on mobile, card-style on desktop - Includes clear CTAs for signup and dismissal **3. Responsive Sports Betting Logo Handling** - Enhanced logo rendering in PlatformRail component with responsive sizing - Improved logo display in sidebar with proper aspect ratio handling - Added lazy loading for better performance - Enhanced accessibility with improved alt text - Responsive sizing across mobile, tablet, and desktop devices These changes improve user engagement by encouraging authentication while maintaining a clean UI for authenticated users, and ensure consistent logo display across all device sizes.','2026-08-08T13:34:46Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/6'),
(8,'Integrate Supabase Backend for Early Access Forms','This PR implements the backend integration for the Early Access signup forms, connecting them to the Supabase database at https://dskyyujqajlgtooywgpf.supabase.co. ### Backend Integration - Added `@supabase/supabase-js` dependency for database connectivity - Created typed Supabase client with environment variable validation - Implemented reusable helper functions for form submission and duplicate checking - Added comprehensive TypeScript types for type safety (no `any` types) ### Database - Created `early_access` table migration with all required fields - Implemented Row Level Security (RLS) with secure policies: - Public can INSERT (submit forms) - Public cannot SELECT, UPDATE, or DELETE - Added unique constraint on email to prevent duplicates - Created indexes for performance optimization ### Form Integration - Replaced Formspree mock integration with real Supabase inserts - Preserved all existing UI, animations, and styling - Implemented proper error handling for: - Duplicate emails - Network failures - Validation errors - Added user-friendly success and error messages - No page refresh on submission ### Security - All inputs sanitized (trim, lowercase email) - Email format validation - Only anonymous key used on frontend (never service role key) - RLS policies prevent unauthorized data access - Race condition handling for duplicate emails ### Documentation - Created `.env.example` with required environment variables - Created comprehensive `SUPABASE_SETUP.md` setup guide - Added inline code comments for maintainability','2026-08-06T18:55:20Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/8'),
(10,'Add /dev development process page with search engine indexing protection','This PR creates a dedicated page at `/dev` for the platform''s development process documentation, with protection against search engine indexing. 1. **New Route:** Created `src/routes/dev.tsx` with: - Development workflow and branch strategy documentation - Code standards and best practices - Deployment process guidelines - Uses existing UI components and follows site''s design patterns 2. **SEO Protection:** Implemented dual-layer protection: - Added `<meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow">` in page head - Updated `public/robots.txt` with `Disallow: /dev` directive The page is now accessible at `/dev` but will not be indexed by search engines.','2026-08-08T15:16:31Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/10'),
(12,'Homepage UX improvements: Disable auto popup, add partner logos, show bottom nav, and display SAST time','This PR implements four key improvements to the homepage user experience: 1. **Disabled timed popup trigger**: Removed the 15-second auto-popup on homepage while keeping the layout intact. The early access popup now only triggers when users click on pricing plan buttons or "Get started" CTAs. 2. **Added partner logos**: Added 1xBet and WorldSportsBetting logos to the partner logo section displayed on the homepage. 3. **Footer enhancement**: Added live SAST (South African Standard Time) date and time display below the copyright text in the footer, updating every second. 4. **Navigation improvements**: - Enabled the bottom navigation bar on the homepage for mobile users - Hidden the hamburger menu icon on the homepage to improve clean design These changes improve the user experience by reducing interruptions, increasing partner visibility, and making navigation more accessible on the homepage.','2026-08-08T18:12:55Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/12'),
(15,'MVP launch: P0–P4 (guardrails, trust sweep, pricing, core schema, privacy)','Sequenced launch work from the MVP blueprint: P0 guardrails and flags, P1 trust and claims sweep, P2 free-launch pricing, P3 core schema, P4 POPIA privacy and consent. Verified by Vercel preview build; SQL tests run against the live Supabase project in rolled-back transactions.','2026-10-29T07:48:17Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/15'),
(16,'Add docs/HANDOFF.md','Handoff note for continuing P5 onwards.','2026-10-29T07:56:33Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/16'),
(17,'Homepage: restore match card and partner logo strip','Restores the Orlando Pirates v Kaizer Chiefs card as an interactive, clearly labelled illustrative example, and the bookmaker logo strip (logos only: no links, odds or offers; AFFILIATES_ENABLED stays false). The ''why a locked record matters'' points move to a strip under the hero.','2026-10-29T08:31:12Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/17'),
(18,'P5: localisation foundation and SA English','Makes the app translatable so every screen built after this writes strings through keys. Only en-ZA is enabled; af, zu and xh wait for native-speaker review (P13). - **i18next + react-i18next**, SSR-safe (fresh instance per request, bundles imported eagerly, `<html lang>` set on the server). Decision in `docs/i18n.md`. - **Language order:** profile (wired in P6; `profiles.language` added), then `puntr_lang` cookie (written only when a visitor picks), then `Accept-Language`, then en-ZA. - **`src/locales/`:** en-ZA namespaces, `config.ts` with `enabled/reviewed/reviewedBy/reviewedAt`, dev-only pseudo-locale `en-XA`. - **`src/lib/format.ts`:** `money()` → `R1 234,50`, `odds()` → `2.10`, `pct()` → `62%`, dates `Sat 31 Oct 2026`, times `17:30 SAST`, `+27` phones. 20 vitest tests (`bun run test`). - **`<RgNotice />`:** the single responsible-gambling message (full and compact); helpline is a constant, not translated. - **Converted:** header, footer, mobile nav, side rails, `/`, `/how-it-works`, `/support`, `/predictions`, `/pricing`, `/community`, `/insights`, `/coming-soon`, consent banner, 404/error screens, root metadata, lock gates. - **Emails** take a locale and fall back to English (`src/lib/email/i18n.ts`). - **`bun run i18n:check`:** missing keys per language and hard-coded JSX text (warn only). - **Docs:** `docs/i18n.md`, `docs/i18n/glossary.md` (reviewer columns blank). - **Migration** `20261030060000_profiles_language.sql`, applied to the live project; `supabase/tests/profiles_language.sql` passes and rolls back; tables confirmed still empty; `types.ts` updated.','2026-10-29T19:18:01Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/18'),
(19,'P6: accounts - email-code sign-up, 18+, POPIA, account privacy','Stacked on #18 (P5), because P6 needs the localisation layer. Merge #18 first; GitHub will then retarget this to `main`. - **`/join`**: email, 6-digit code (`signInWithOtp` / `verifyOtp`), onboarding (language when more than one is enabled, username with live availability, birth year, 18+ box, Terms and Privacy acceptance, two separate unticked marketing boxes, the "public, permanent record" line). `?ref=` is kept in localStorage until the profile exists. - **Atomic account creation**: new SQL function `complete_signup` writes the profile and four consent rows (`terms`, `privacy_notice`, `marketing_email`, `marketing_whatsapp`, with notice versions) in one transaction. The Founding number is shown only after it returns. `referred_by` is attached from the ref code. - **Under-18 stores nothing**: blocked in the browser (a data-free call removes the bare sign-in and email), and again on the server. The database refuses it too. - **Session**: Supabase `SessionProvider` replaces the localStorage guest mode. `useSession()` exposes `user, profile, isSignedIn, isAdmin, signOut`. Profile language wins over cookie and Accept-Language; the switcher saves to `profiles.language`. - **Header menu** (My record, Account, Privacy and data, Sign out); every "Get early access" / "Get started" CTA links to `/join`. The early-access modal and timed popup are no longer rendered (files kept). - **`/account`, `/account/privacy`** (export via `export_my_data`, marketing choices via `record_consent`, deletion via `anonymise_account` + auth admin delete), minimal public `/u/$username` (P9 builds the record).','2026-10-29T19:18:11Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/19'),
(20,'P7: real fixtures and results','Stacked on #19 (P6), which is stacked on #18 (P5). Merge in that order. - **Provider layer** (`src/lib/sports/`): interface (`listFixtures`, `listResults`), API-Sports implementation (API-Football v3 for soccer, API-Rugby v1 for rugby), status mapping, normalisation. League IDs come from `SPORTS_LEAGUE_IDS`; **none are guessed**. `bun run sports:ids` prints candidate leagues for you to choose from. - **Routes** `/api/cron/sync-fixtures` (yesterday to +14 days, one call per competition, never overwrites a finished fixture) and `/api/cron/sync-results` (last 36 hours, zero provider calls when nothing is open). Both need `Authorization: Bearer ${CRON_SECRET}`; with no secret configured they refuse everything. Call counts are returned and logged. - **Scheduling: pg_cron + pg_net, not vercel.json.** Vercel Hobby only allows daily crons and a sub-daily entry fails the deployment, and the plan tier isn''t visible to me. The migration (applied) schedules fixtures daily at 02:00 UTC and results every 30 minutes, reading `cron_base_url` and `cron_secret` from Vault. Until you create those two secrets the job does nothing (verified). - **Scores:** soccer stores the 90-minute score; awarded results and walkovers map to `cancelled` (void). - **CSV fallback:** admin-only import at `/admin/fixtures` (role re-checked on the server via `is_admin()`); a bad row rejects the whole file; re-import updates. - **Pages:** `/predictions` and the home page now read real upcoming fixtures, grouped by SAST day, Soccer/Rugby filter, times as `17:30 SAST`. The old mock "featured" and "popular" predictions are gone from `/predictions`.','2026-10-29T19:18:22Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/20'),
(21,'Copy polish, Pay-As-You-Go and Puntr Pro','Stacked on #20 (P7). Merge order: #18, #19, #20, then this.','2026-10-29T19:18:32Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/21'),
(22,'P8: post a pick, the core loop','Stacked on #21 (copy polish) → #20 (P7) → #19 (P6) → #18 (P5). Merge in that order. - **`/match/$fixtureId`**: teams (existing `TeamLogo`), competition, kick-off in SAST, live countdown ("Locks in 2h 14m"). Pick form: market tabs by sport (soccer: Match result, Double chance, Over/Under 2.5, Both teams to score; rugby: Match result, Handicap), selection buttons labelled with team names, odds 1.01 to 50 (two decimals), confidence 1 to 5, reasoning up to 280 characters with a counter. The rugby handicap line is applied to the home team''s score ("-6.5 means Bulls give 6.5 points"), which matches how P9 will grade it. - **Submits only through `create_prediction`.** Server reasons are shown in plain words ("This match has kicked off - picks are locked", "You already have a Match result (1X2) pick on this game", daily limit, paused, banned...). Unknown errors are hidden behind a generic message. - **After kick-off** the form becomes "Picks locked at 15:30 SAST". There is no edit or delete control anywhere. - **Picks on the match**: username, Founding badge, market, selection, odds, confidence, "Locked 3h 12m before kick-off", first 10 characters of the hash linking to `/verify` (built in P11), and the result once settled. Reads `visible_predictions`, so moderation-hidden picks never show. - **Crowd split** for Match result with the sample size. - **`/community`** keeps its layout (composer card, filter tabs, post cards) but now shows real locked picks: New, Top tipsters this week (from `weekly_leaderboard`), My picks, with Load more and a Report button (one report per member per pick). The composer now points at the fixtures; the dead Image/Poll/Tip buttons and likes/comments are gone because comments come after launch.','2026-10-29T19:18:40Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/22'),
(23,'P9: settlement, records and leaderboard','Stacked on #22 (P8) → #21 → #20 → #19 → #18. Merge in that order.','2026-10-29T19:18:48Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/23'),
(24,'P10: founding counter, referrals, waitlist invites','Stacked on #23 (P9) → #22 → #21 → #20 → #19 → #18. Merge in that order. - **Founding counter**: a server function cached for 60 seconds reads a public `founding_spots_taken()` function. "63 of 100 Founding spots left" in the home hero, on `/join` and beside the header CTA (wide screens); "Founding spots are full" at zero; nothing shown if the count can''t be read. - **Referrals**: the invite link (`/join?ref=<code>`) with **Copy** and **WhatsApp** on `/account`, on your own profile and in the account menu; "Friends who joined: N". A referral counts **only when the friend posts their first pick** (a trigger on `predictions`, once per friend) and creates a `referral_rewards` row: 15 credits each side, `pending`. The page says rewards are recorded now and granted when credits launch, and that credits have no cash value. `?ref=` is kept through `/join` and also from shared pick links. - **Share a pick**: after posting, the exact agreed wording ("My pick: Pirates to win @ 2.10 - locked 3h 12m before kick-off on Puntr. puntr.co.za/match/<id>?ref=<code>") with WhatsApp and Copy. No Open Graph image: not cheap here, skipped as the prompt allowed. - **Waitlist invite** (`bun run waitlist:invite`): **dry run by default**; sending needs `--send`. One service email, "Your Puntr early-access spot is open", with the join link, live spots-left, a one-line reason, unsubscribe link, privacy link and the 18+ and helpline line, English only; no promotion, partner or giveaway wording (tested). Skips invalid, duplicate, already-emailed, unsubscribed and `privacy_requests` emails; logs every send straight after it happens in `waitlist_invites`, so re-runs never double-send. The signed `/unsubscribe` page needs one click so an email scanner can''t unsubscribe anyone.','2026-10-29T19:18:58Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/24'),
(25,'P11: admin area and /verify','- `/admin` (noindex): Fixtures (re-sync, CSV), Settlement (settle all, corrections with required reason), Reports (resolve, hide), Users (ban/unban, hide pick), Waitlist (read-only). - `/verify`: paste a pick ID, the browser recomputes the SHA-256 and checks the chain link; daily chain heads table. - Migrations: `admin_settle_prediction`, `write_chain_head`, `chain-head` cron. `20261030100500_chain_head_fix.sql` fixes an ambiguous-column bug and is **not yet applied** to the live project. - `/admin/fixtures` redirects to `/admin`. Docs in `docs/admin.md`.','2026-10-29T19:19:09Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/25'),
(26,'Launch notifications: Founding reservations, launch emails, admin Realtime notice','- Five early-access sign-ups loaded into `early_access` with reserved Founding spots (data loaded directly, not in the repo). A leading `www.` was removed from one email. - `profiles_assign_founding` holds reserved numbers for those emails; the public counter treats held spots as unavailable. - Three launch email waves via Resend (launch day, +3, +7 days) at `/api/cron/launch-notify`, idempotent through `launch_email_sends`, off unless `LAUNCH_EMAILS_ENABLED=true`. - Launch-day WhatsApp/SMS draft delivered to `/admin` through Supabase Realtime (`admin_notifications`) and emailed to admins. The Waitlist tab lists people with one-tap WhatsApp/SMS links (opted-in, SA numbers only). - Migrations `20261030110000_launch_notify.sql`, `20261030110500_launch_notify_cron.sql` (applied live). Docs: `docs/launch-notify.md`.','2026-10-29T09:46:27Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/26'),
(27,'Email + password sign-up without confirmation, then confirm email and two-factor','- `/join`: Create account / Sign in tabs with email + password. With "Confirm email" off in Supabase a new member is in straight away; with it on, the screen falls back to the emailed code. "Email me a sign-in code instead" remains for returning members. - New `/account/security`: confirm email (code), authenticator-app two-factor (QR + manual key), set or change password. A dismissible bar nudges members who have not done these. - Members with two-factor on are asked for the authenticator code at sign-in. - Founding spots held for early-access people need a confirmed email; `claim_reserved_founding()` assigns the number after confirmation. - Two-factor is enforced in the database (`mfa_ok()`): posting, profile access and reports need an aal2 session once a factor is verified. - Migration `20261030120000_auth_passwords_mfa.sql` (already applied live). Docs in `docs/auth-email.md`.','2026-10-29T19:57:53Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/27'),
(29,'Align legal pages with the platform as built; add the legal-alignment rule','## Legal copy changed - **Terms:** removed claims the product doesn''t make (odds comparison, recurring-commission affiliate programme, PuntPoints awarded, invites moving people up a waitlist). Added sign-in methods and security, what the service provides, invites as recorded, a new section on locked/public/chained predictions, grading, void rules and corrections, a new section on paid options not being on sale, record licence surviving deletion, self-service deletion. Sections renumbered. - **Privacy Policy:** data table rewritten; new "How you sign in" and "Early access, launch messages and marketing" (with the `#marketing` anchor the marketing notice already linked to); processors updated (Supabase, Vercel, Resend, Google optional, sports data with no personal data). - **Privacy choices (cookies):** essential list now names every cookie and storage key in use. - **Affiliate disclosure, Refunds:** reviewed, unchanged. - **Support FAQ:** corrected the invites answer. - **Database:** new `notice_versions` rows at `2026-10-29-r2` (already applied).','2026-10-29T20:12:45Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/29'),
(30,'Posting needs a confirmed email; handoff and PayFast scope note','- Posting a pick (which puts it on the community feed and the leaderboard) now needs a confirmed email. Enforced in the database: `can_post()` and a trigger on `predictions` (the hash-chain function is untouched). The pick form shows a "Confirm your email" prompt with a link to `/account/security`; the error has its own message. - KYC is not built (see below); `can_post()` is the single place to extend if it is added. - `docs/HANDOFF.md` rewritten for a new Claude account. `CLAUDE.md` records the owner''s decision to add PayFast credits and recurring billing before launch (building Fri 30 Oct, 12:00 SAST).','2026-10-29T20:16:21Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/30'),
(31,'Docs: record the readiness score in the handoff','Documentation only: adds the readiness score (78/100) and the blueprint version to `docs/HANDOFF.md`. No product, data or legal copy changed, so no legal pages needed updating.','2026-10-29T20:18:40Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/31'),
(32,'Docs: PuntPoints must be configured before launch (handoff)','Documentation only: records in `docs/HANDOFF.md` that PuntPoints must be configured before the 2 November launch (blueprint prompt P19), with proposed earning rules, the promises the Terms already make, the build outline, the legal changes the build PR must include, and open decision D18. No product, data or legal copy changed in this PR.','2026-10-29T20:19:40Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/32'),
(33,'Docs: referral programme and PuntPoints rewards brief; no-cash guardrail','Documentation and project rules only; no product, data or legal page changed, so no legal copy needed updating. The build PR will carry the legal changes. - `docs/HANDOFF.md`: the referral programme and PuntPoints rewards brief (blueprint prompt P20) with proposed rules, anti-abuse controls, the betting-voucher gate and the questions for counsel; decisions D19 to D22 open. - `CLAUDE.md`: Launch scope now says no cash prizes, and that PuntPoints are redeemable only for vouchers, sponsored rewards and perks, with betting vouchers off until counsel signs off and a licensed partner funds them.','2026-10-29T20:21:07Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/33'),
(34,'PuntPoints, referral vesting and the rewards catalogue (switched off)','Blueprint prompts P19 (PuntPoints) and P20 (referral programme and rewards). **Everything ships switched off**: three admin switches (PuntPoints, Rewards, Betting vouchers), every earning rule and milestone inactive, an empty catalogue. Values are editable in `/admin` → Rewards. - Append-only `puntpoints_ledger` with idempotent, capped awards (confirm email, first pick, locked pick, settled pick, referral). Only members in good standing earn (18+, confirmed email, not banned, not on a break). No public view reads points, so they cannot change ranking or the leaderboard. - Referral vesting: a referral vests after 7 days, both sides earn, milestone bonuses, clawback if either account is banned or deleted within 30 days, admin review queue and reversal. - Rewards catalogue, voucher codes and atomic redemption (no double spend, no over-stock); admin fulfils or cancels with refund as new rows; points adjustments with a required reason. Betting vouchers behind their own switch, shown only to eligible 18+ members, labelled "Ad" with the helpline. - `/rewards` page, account-menu item, invite card with vesting and next milestone, admin Rewards tab. - Migration `20261030150000_puntpoints_rewards.sql` is applied. Docs: `docs/puntpoints.md`.','2026-10-29T20:54:13Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/34'),
(35,'Football only at launch: more leagues, league filter, rugby and racing after launch','- 16 more football competitions defined in `src/lib/sports/competitions.ts`: Europa and Conference League, La Liga, Serie A, Bundesliga, Ligue 1, FA Cup, EFL Cup, Nedbank Cup, MTN8, Motsepe Foundation Championship, CAF Champions League and Confederation Cup, AFCON, World Cup qualifiers (Africa) and Bafana Bafana friendlies (kept to matches involving South Africa). **No league IDs are guessed**: each needs its real ID in `SPORTS_LEAGUE_IDS`, looked up with `bun run sports:ids`; a league without an ID is skipped. - `SPORTS_ENABLED` (default `soccer`): the sync requests football only, so rugby needs no API-Sports Rugby subscription at launch. Rugby is switched on after launch with `SPORTS_ENABLED=soccer,rugby`. Horse racing is not built (needs its own data model). - `/predictions`: a league filter built from the fixtures that are loaded. - Copy no longer claims rugby coverage (home, predictions, How it works, About, mobile nav, community composer).','2026-10-29T20:58:19Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/35'),
(36,'Test: an admin settlement event needs a reason and an admin','Test-only fix: in `supabase/tests/puntpoints_rewards.sql` the admin-source settlement row needs `reason` and `admin_id` (constraint `settlement_admin_needs_who`). No product, data or legal copy changed.','2026-10-29T21:06:04Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/36'),
(37,'Test: clear the fake member login before banning a profile','Test-only fix in `supabase/tests/puntpoints_rewards.sql`: the simulated member login from an earlier step stayed active, so the profile guard blocked the direct ban update. No product, data or legal copy changed.','2026-10-29T21:08:32Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/37'),
(38,'Docs: betting vouchers switched on for launch (owner decision)','Documentation and project rules only. The owner switched `betting_vouchers_enabled` on in the live database (29 Oct 2026) because betting vouchers will be offered as a redeemable reward at launch. `CLAUDE.md`, `docs/puntpoints.md`, `docs/HANDOFF.md` and `docs/legal-changelog.md` now say so. PuntPoints and Rewards remain off, and no betting-voucher reward exists, so nothing is listed to members.','2026-10-29T21:18:21Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/38'),
(39,'Team-only /dev page: MVP blueprint behind an email + password gate','Adds `/dev`, the MVP blueprint (v1.7) rebuilt as a TanStack Start route, for the team only. **How it''s protected** - The repo is public, so the blueprint is committed only as AES-256-GCM ciphertext (`src/content/dev/blueprint.enc.json`). The key is derived from the gate email + password with scrypt (128 MiB per attempt). The server decrypts it only for the right pair. No new env vars. - httpOnly, SameSite=Strict session cookie for 12 hours; Sign out clears it. - noindex meta + `X-Robots-Tag`, `Cache-Control: private, no-store`, already disallowed in robots.txt, not in nav or sitemap. - Verified: ciphertext and decryption code are not in the client bundle. **Rebuild/update**: `docs/dev-page.md` (`bun run dev:blueprint`). The script fails on unbalanced HTML and repairs the export glitch where three wrapper divs lost their opening tags (it broke hydration). **Legal copy**: no change needed. `/dev` is internal, collects nothing from members, and its cookie is strictly necessary and only set for staff who sign in. Tests: lint (0 errors), 3 new unit tests (wrong password, malformed and expired sessions), build; browser-tested gate, wrong/right password, reload, mobile width, sign out, no hydration errors.','2026-10-30T11:19:45Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/39'),
(40,'Live product roadmap at /roadmap (header, footer, mobile menu)','Adds `/roadmap`, a live product roadmap, linked in the header, footer (Platform) and mobile menu, and listed in the sitemap. **Schedule** (owner decision, 30 Oct 2026; week 1 = launch week): football at launch (2 Nov), basketball and rugby week 2, horse racing week 4, combat sports (boxing, MMA) weeks 6 to 8, cricket week 10, tennis week 12. Single source: `src/lib/roadmap.ts`. **"Live" means live**: status is read on every request from `SPORTS_ENABLED` and `LAUNCH_DATE` (server function). A sport shows as Live only when it is switched on for the fixtures sync, never because its date has passed (then it shows "In progress"). Before launch, football shows "Launching 2 Nov". "Also on the way" (no dates): languages, PuntPoints rewards, Puntr Pro, mobile apps. **Header**: adding an eighth link made the bar overflow into the language picker at 1280 and 1440px (it was already tight). Labels no longer wrap, How it works and Pricing show from `xl`, and the language switcher now lives in the footer and mobile menu only (just en-ZA is enabled; revisit in P13). Checked at 1024, 1280, 1440 and 390px. **Fix**: `mock-data.ts` listed Rugby as active, so the sidebar linked to it as if covered. Now inactive. **Legal copy (standing rule)**: Terms §4 lists the planned sports, says none is available until it appears on the site, and that `/roadmap` dates are plans, not commitments. New migration `20261030170000_terms_r6_roadmap.sql` (notice version `terms 2026-10-30-r6`), `docs/legal-changelog.md` entry with review points. ⚠️ The migration still needs applying to Supabase (this session''s connector has no access to the Puntr project). Privacy, Cookies, Affiliate disclosure and Refunds unchanged: nothing new is collected.','2026-10-30T11:20:03Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/40'),
(41,'Fix auth_passwords_mfa SQL test: grant t_e to switched roles','Running `supabase/tests/auth_passwords_mfa.sql` on the live project failed with `permission denied for table t_e` when the test switched to `service_role`. The other temp tables used under a switched role already had this grant; `t_e` was missed. Test-only change, no app or schema change, no legal copy affected.','2026-11-05T21:33:53Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/41'),
(42,'Official launch 1 Dec 2026; Founding sign-ups from 2 Nov 2026','- `LAUNCH_DATE` default is now 2026-12-01. `/roadmap` and its week counts (basketball and rugby week 2, etc.) now run from 1 Dec. - New `FOUNDING_OPEN_DATE` (default 2026-11-02). The early-access email waves (day, +3, +7) count from it, so nothing already scheduled moves. - Wording no longer says Puntr is live: the three early-access emails, the admin WhatsApp/SMS drafts, the admin reminder email, admin labels and the /roadmap intro.','2026-11-05T21:34:04Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/42'),
(43,'Fix signed-out community, leaderboard and tipster stats (anon 42501)','- New migration `20261105221500_public_views_definer.sql`: sets `public.public_profiles` and `public.visible_predictions` back to definer rights (`security_invoker = false`), re-asserts owner and grants. Live anon requests to those views, `tipster_stats` and `weekly_leaderboard` failed with 42501 on `public.profiles` / `public.hidden_predictions`, so signed-out visitors saw ''couldn''t load'' on /community and /leaderboards. - New SQL test `supabase/tests/public_views_definer.sql` (rolls back): anon can read the four views, anon still cannot read `profiles` or `hidden_predictions`, and `public_profiles` exposes only id, username, display_name, founding_number, created_at.','2026-11-05T23:01:11Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/43'),
(44,'MVP launch: newsroom, notifications, founding campaign, survey, forms to support','Legal copy: docs/legal-changelog.md updated (6 Nov entry, attorney review flagged). Needs before 12:00 SAST: RESEND_API_KEY in Vercel production, then merge to deploy covers, routes and the founding-campaign cron.','2026-11-06T01:16:48Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/44'),
(45,'Founding campaign test-send mode','Adds ?test=1 (cron-secret protected) which sends both campaign variants to support@puntr.co.za only; records nothing. Legal copy: nothing changed.','2026-11-06T01:29:56Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/45'),
(46,'Founding welcome email, Annual Pass offer, Athletics, LIVE marker','- **Founding welcome email** from the Founder (features, quiet Annual Pass offer), real Puntr logo in header and footer. Sent by new cron `/api/cron/founding-welcome` (every 10 min, new opted-in sign-ups only, once each; `?test=1` sends to support@ only). - **Annual Pass offer**: first 20 founding members to claim before 16 Nov 2026 (23:59 SAST). Claim button on `/founding#annual-pass` (reserves place and price, no payment). The 12:00 campaign email now carries the same terms and logo. - **Nav**: Athletics added to the sports sidebar and mobile menu; roadmap weeks 6 to 8 with combat sports. LIVE badge with glowing green dot under Soccer. - **Roadmap**: "Refer and earn 30%" under "Also on the way" (owner wording; plan only, nothing built).','2026-11-06T02:05:52Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/46'),
(47,'Welcome cron fix, bonus PuntPoints referral wording, confirm-before-sign-in copy, light/dark emails','- **Welcome cron fix** (Amazon Q finding on #46): the run now stops and logs if the `founding_welcome_sends` record fails to save, so a database fault cannot repeat-send. - **Referral wording** (owner, 6 Nov): "Earn up to 30% in bonus PuntPoints", never cash. Roadmap "Also on the way", welcome email and Terms §4. Still a plan; nothing built. - **Confirm email before sign-in**: join password hint, code-step copy, How it works, Founding steps, Privacy §3 and `docs/auth-email.md` now match. A password sign-in by an unconfirmed address sends a fresh code and continues on the code step (previously showed "wrong password"). - **Light and dark mode emails**: all Founding, launch, waitlist, admin and early-access templates. Two opaque logo PNGs (`public/email/logo-light.png`, `logo-dark.png`, recoloured from the real logo) swap by `prefers-color-scheme`; because each carries its own background the logo stays visible in clients that force-invert colours. Text and surfaces get `dm-*` classes overridden in a dark stylesheet.','2026-11-06T09:23:11Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/47'),
(48,'Add illustrative match, leaderboard and insights previews','- Add six clearly labelled illustrative fixture cards across the Betway Premiership, Premier League, UEFA Champions League, international rugby, NBA and international cricket. - Show the fixture preview on the homepage and above the real-data fixture list on /predictions. The sample cards are static, non-clickable and never inserted into the fixtures database. - Add a separate illustrative leaderboard with seeded sample handles and example performance figures. The actual weekly leaderboard remains connected to Supabase and is kept distinct from the preview. - Add an Insights preview with example match metrics, a responsive chart and publisher-source cards for SuperSport, BBC Sport and ESPN. - Display the proposed news refresh cadence as a preview label: every 24 hours at 12:00 SAST. This PR does not activate a news aggregation provider, scheduled cron job or live news ingestion. - Remove the page-level RgNotice from /founding. The global footer already renders the required notice and helpline, so this removes the duplicate without removing the sitewide notice.','2026-11-06T02:44:06Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/48'),
(49,'Add Community discussions, Results previews and navigation updates','- Add a Reddit-style sports discussion preview to Community with three Puntr team starter threads, three sample comments per thread, and interactive illustrative upvotes. - Add clearly labelled sample result cards to Results. - Route the desktop/mobile Feedback navigation links to `/feedback`. - Remove AI-Powered Insights, Podcast and Tools entries from the mobile navigation menu. - Rename footer links to Cookies and Disclosures; remove the Founding Member footer link. - Use the supplied Arsenal and Liverpool badge images in team logo rendering.','2026-11-06T03:03:01Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/49'),
(50,'Add dedicated feature landing pages and team badges','- Add dedicated landing pages for Bookmakers, Live Scores, PuntPoints and Referrals. - Route the corresponding mobile/header-menu entries to the new pages. - Register the supplied Golden State Warriors, Boston Celtics, Springboks, All Blacks, South Africa cricket and India cricket badge URLs for illustrative team components.','2026-11-06T03:55:42Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/50'),
(51,'Improve founding urgency, guest pick conversion and live footer clock','- Upgrade the Founding Member counter into a responsive availability panel with claimed/remaining counts, a progress bar, accessible progress semantics and a limited-places indicator. - Move the live counter higher on `/founding`, strengthen the first-100 urgency message and improve mobile CTA stacking and spacing. - Convert unauthenticated interactions with the illustrative Soweto Derby pick percentages into a high-converting sign-up dialog with the requested copy and a `Get Started` CTA to `/founding`. - Preserve the existing signed-in preview interaction; guest selections are not saved and no prediction is submitted. - Refresh the footer''s displayed local date/time every second.','2026-11-06T04:23:20Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/51'),
(52,'Refresh header navigation and add Puntr Tools landing page','- Replace the Predictions link in the primary header navigation with Home, About, Updates, Insights and Tools, in that order. - Apply the same navigation structure to the mobile menu. - Add a Puntr Newsroom landing page at `/newsroom` for product announcements and platform updates. - Add a Tools landing page at `/tools` featuring: - Betting Slip Converter — Free (upcoming) - AI "Edge Finder" Summary Cards — Puntr Pro paid feature (upcoming) - Punt AI v1.0 Chatbot — Puntr Pro paid feature (upcoming) - Tailor `/coming-soon` to AI-Powered Insights, with Puntr Pro pricing clearly stated at R99 per month and the CTA leading to Pricing.','2026-11-06T05:36:43Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/52'),
(53,'Add live founding and Annual Pass scarcity to sitewide bar','- Upgrade the sitewide FoundingBar to show verified live allocation counts: founding members claimed out of the configured cap, plus Annual Passes remaining out of 20. - Read founding totals from the existing public `founding_spots_taken()` server function and Annual Pass availability from the existing `annual_pass_offer()` RPC. - Refresh the counts every 60 seconds and retain the existing /founding CTA. - Keep the strip responsive with compact wrapping on narrow mobile screens.','2026-11-06T05:47:53Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/53'),
(54,'Add post-signup Annual Pass claim and verified tipster demo','- Add a post-signup Founding spot celebration and embed the existing Annual Pass reservation component for confirmed members on `/join`. - Show the Annual Pass availability counter as `4 of 20` while the live offer count loads, then use the database RPC as the source of truth. - Align `/founding` copy with the R299, 12-month, non-renewing Annual Pass offer. - Add an Annual Pass comparison panel above the pricing tiers: R299 once-off versus R1,188 at R99/month (save R889 / 75%). The CTA reserves through account creation; no payment is collected at claim time. - Add an interactive homepage toggle comparing an unverified traditional tipster record with Puntr''s timestamped, locked, auto-graded public record and visible ROI/unit history.','2026-11-06T06:58:44Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/54'),
(55,'Strengthen bookmaker independence and refine homepage previews','- Add a shared bookmaker independence statement to app-shell pages, including the bookmaker directory and legal pages, and feature it in the homepage bookmaker wall. - State that Puntr does not take bets and that affiliates, partners and sponsors cannot influence prediction scores, AI recommendations, editorial content or independent probability assessments. - Remove Stake, 1xBet and Betfair from the provider list, leaving nine bookmaker logos. - Add an accessible, responsive toggle to switch the homepage fixture experience between fixtures, results and leaderboard previews. All preview content is clearly labelled illustrative. - Remove the separate weekly leaderboard block from the lower homepage while retaining the join CTA and its benefits. - Remove the redundant “How Puntr works” section.','2026-11-06T07:56:12Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/55'),
(56,'Polish Puntr brand copy and South African English','- Reposition the homepage around accountable sports predictions: publish before kick-off, locked picks, consistent grading and a complete public record. - Rewrite the About page to sharpen Puntr’s mission, differentiation and value proposition without overstating planned AI capabilities or competition coverage. - Refine Founding Member, pricing and tools marketing copy for a clearer South African audience and consistent brand voice. - Review key legal pages for clearer plain-language introductions and South African English spelling; record the copy-only review in `docs/legal-changelog.md`. No policy substance, product capability or legal commitment has been changed. - Update the support/contact experience: remove the phone card and phone details, retain `support@puntr.co.za`, and display the requested live-chat availability message.','2026-11-06T08:18:24Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/56'),
(57,'Add Tipster Support benefit and remove Lovable auth coupling','- Update the homepage bookmaker heading to: “Predictions, trends and deep analytical insights across South Africa''s most popular bookmakers”. - Rename the homepage preview heading to “A sneak peek into the Puntr experience”. - Add the planned Puntr Pro Tipster Support benefit across homepage, About, Pricing, Insights, Community, Leaderboards, Roadmap and PuntPoints messaging. The copy makes eligibility clear: verified Tipsters with long winning streaks and strong performance on selected sport- and competition-specific leaderboards may receive voluntary PuntPoints tips from Punters. Tips are points, not cash, do not affect rankings or grading, and remain subject to published rules. This PR updates product/marketing copy; the actual transfer/tipping workflow is not enabled by this change. - Suppress generic background data-load error messages across predictions, results, community, leaderboards, rewards, public profiles, match pages, newsroom and verification head data. Preserve actionable authentication, validation and transaction feedback. The global route fallback now uses neutral branded copy. - Remove Lovable-specific preview auth brokering and runtime error telemetry. Supabase client sessions now use standard browser localStorage. - Align `.env` and `supabase/config.toml` with the active Supabase project ID `hucjuekhitjuygcoomhw`.','2026-11-06T10:20:00Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/57'),
(58,'Annual Pass claim-and-pay onboarding (PayFast, gated) and profile pictures','Stacked on #47 (merge that first; this PR then retargets to `main`). - **Annual Pass claim includes payment** (owner, 6 Nov): R299 once-off through PayFast. A claim holds a place for 48 hours, the place is confirmed when payment is received, unpaid holds are released. Database: `annual_pass_claims` gains status, hold, payment columns; `claim_annual_pass()` creates holds; `confirm_annual_pass_payment()` (service role only) is what the PayFast ITN handler calls. Logic tested against the live schema in a rolled-back transaction (claim, repeat, amount mismatch, paid, expiry, re-claim, non-member). - **Onboarding**: Founding members see the offer on the last step of `/join`, and on `/account` and `/founding`. - **Payments stay off** until `PAYFAST_ENABLED=true`: until then the button says payments open shortly and no place can be held. `startAnnualPassCheckout` is the seam for the PayFast task (form URL and signed fields). - **Emails**: welcome and Annual Pass emails now say claiming includes payment through PayFast, with "Claim and pay R299". - **Profile pictures**: JPG/PNG/WebP under 10 MB, cropped to a 512 px square and compressed to WebP (quality 0.86, JPEG fallback) in the browser, EXIF rotation respected. Public `avatars` bucket (1 MB cap, own-folder RLS), `profiles.avatar_url`, shown in the header, `/account` and public profiles.','2026-11-06T09:54:48Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/58'),
(59,'Intelligence fixture cards, guest Peek & Hook gate, streamlined mobile nav, sports landing pages','Stacked on #58 (which is stacked on #47). Retarget to `main` once those merge. - **Intelligence fixture cards** on `/predictions`: Confidence Score meter, Algorithmic Pick badge, odds comparison and model analysis. Per the owner''s choice (6 Nov), these are **placeholders** ("available at launch") until the Puntr model exists, and odds comparison reads "coming soon" with no bookmaker names (launch rule: no odds comparison). No numbers are invented. - **Guest "Peek & Hook" gate** on `/predictions`, `/results` and `/leaderboards`: guests see the first 2 items in full. From item 3, proprietary fields (intel panel, crowd and leader columns, units, ROI, settled, wins) are blurred (`backdrop-blur-md bg-background/60`), fixture context and usernames stay readable, and a Founding conversion card floats over them. Members never see the gate. The blurred text stays in the HTML (SSR renders it unblurred), and `aria-hidden` is only on the visual container, with a screen-reader note. - **Overlay copy** adjusted (owner): free account, then the Founding Annual Pass at R299 once-off (claiming includes payment); "Free account • No card needed to join • Instant access". - **Mobile nav**: the bottom bar shows for members only (the footer''s extra bottom padding follows). The header hamburger is removed: guests get logo, Sign in and Join free; members use the bottom bar''s More drawer. - **Sports landing pages** `/sports/$sport` for all 8 roadmap sports, covering the South African context, how Puntr''s engine will cover the sport, planned competitions and markets, and the go-live window from `roadmap.ts`. Each has canonical, OG and JSON-LD (WebPage plus BreadcrumbList) tags and is in the sitemap. The sidebar and mobile-menu sports tabs link to them; unknown sports return 404.','2026-11-06T09:59:24Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/59'),
(61,'Identity verification phase 1: manual ID review, required before redeeming rewards','Stacked on #58 (it includes #58''s regenerated types and legal versions). Retarget to `main` once #58 merges. - **Identity verification, phase 1: manual review.** - Members upload a photo or scan of their SA ID (green book or smart card) or passport on `/account`: JPG, PNG, WebP or PDF, under 10 MB, stored in a new **private** `id-documents` bucket under a random file name in their own folder. - Admins review in a new **ID checks** tab in `/admin`: member username, name, birth year and a 10-minute signed link to the document, then approve (18+ confirmed) or reject with an optional reason. - The document is **deleted straight after the decision**, and a daily `identity-retention` cron deletes any document left unchecked for 30 days. Only the outcome is kept in `identity_verifications` (status, over 18, reviewer, dates). No ID number is stored anywhere. - **Required before redeeming any reward:** a trigger on `redemptions` raises `identity_not_verified`; `/rewards` shows a toast linking to `/account#identity`. - **Phase 2 (after launch):** VerifyNow API for real-time SA ID checks; `method` already allows `verifynow`.','2026-11-06T10:02:01Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/61'),
(62,'Self-hosted explainer video and Tipster Support wording within copy rules','- **Explainer video** now plays from Supabase Storage (`media/explainer/puntr-explainer-720p.mp4`, public bucket created on the live project) instead of the YouTube embed, on the home page modal and `/about`. Compressed from 49.3 MB 1080p to 10.4 MB 720p (H.264 CRF 26, AAC 96k, faststart). `preload="none"` means nothing downloads until play, and there are no third-party cookies. The poster is at `public/explainer-poster.jpg`. - **Tipster Support wording** (from #57) brought within the copy rules: no "monetise" or "winning streaks". It now reads "recognise verified Tipsters with a consistent track record", and every mention says it''s planned, not available yet, points have no cash value and it never affects rankings.','2026-11-08T20:23:17Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/62'),
(63,'Update rugby and cricket team badges','- Rugby: new Springboks and All Blacks logos (`springboks.jpg`, `allblacks.jpg`). - Cricket: round South Africa and India flags (`southafrica.png`, `india.png`). - `teamLogos` in `src/lib/mock-data.ts` now uses local `/teams/...` paths (previously absolute puntr.co.za URLs, which would not show new files on previews). Old `newzealand.JPG`, `za.PNG`, `india.PNG` removed; nothing else referenced them.','2026-11-06T10:46:47Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/63'),
(64,'Improve About page sports coverage and unify explainer video','- Correct the About hero headline to read “Sports knowledge deserves a proper record.” - Expand the sports coverage component to all eight sports in the canonical roadmap: football, basketball, rugby, racing, combat sports, athletics, cricket and tennis. - Rename the component heading to **SPORTS COVERAGE** and link each card to its existing sport landing page. - Extract the Puntr explainer player into a shared component and use the same video on the homepage and About page. - Sport links use the existing TanStack route `/sports/$sport` (for example, `/sports/rugby`); the repository does not currently define a singular `/sport/:sport` route. - The shared player uses the existing Puntr explainer video ID and privacy-enhanced YouTube embed host. - No data, authentication, payment or database behaviour changed.','2026-11-06T13:15:16Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/64'),
(65,'Reserve Annual Passes and email PayFast payment instructions','- Show live Annual Pass scarcity in the sitewide header notification bar as `16/20 Annual Passes remaining` (dynamic remaining count over the 20-pass cap), including for signed-in members. - Replace on-site PayFast checkout with a reservation-first flow. Authenticated members can reserve an Annual Pass without entering payment details on Puntr. - Reuse the existing atomic `claim_annual_pass()` RPC and its 48-hour pending hold. - Send a transactional Resend email containing a signed, expiring Puntr payment link. The link checks the member''s live pending reservation and 48-hour expiry before redirecting to the configured secure PayFast hosted link. - Existing pending reservations can resend the payment email. - Align founding campaign/welcome email copy and Terms with the new reserve-now/pay-by-email flow. - Document required Vercel environment variables, database prerequisite and operational checks.','2026-11-08T20:25:11Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/65'),
(66,'X Ads Founding campaign: tracking, /founding optimisation, admin Campaigns tab','First-party campaign tracking and a conversion-optimised `/founding` page for the 7–8 Nov 2026 X Ads Founding Member campaign (R200). - `campaign_events` table + `log_campaign_event` / `admin_campaign_report` RPCs (migration `20261106210000_campaign_events.sql`, already applied to production) - UTM capture; consent-gated events now also stored first-party with campaign source; new events `landing_viewed`, `founding_cta_clicked`, `signup_completed` - `/founding`: trust points, FAQ, social card tags, CTA tracking - Admin → Campaigns tab (funnel per ad) - Playbook: `docs/campaigns/x-ads-founding-nov-2026.md`','2026-11-06T14:29:45Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/66'),
(67,'Fix team badges, survey/details form grants, campaign events global cap','- Team badges: sport-aware logo lookup (rugby/cricket national sides), Golden State/Celtics use lowercase relative paths. - Fix `/feedback` survey and account-details form: `authenticated` had no table privileges on `member_details`/`survey_responses` (permission denied before RLS). Grants added; bulk truncate/references/trigger revoked. - `log_campaign_event`: global 600/min cap on top of per-visitor guard. - Privacy r9 notice row.','2026-11-06T14:37:59Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/67'),
(68,'Erase member details on account deletion; document survey retention (privacy r10)','- `anonymise_account()` now deletes `member_details` (name, phone, DOB, province) on account deletion; the anonymised profile row is kept, so the old cascade never fired. - Survey responses are kept (owner decision), linked only to the anonymised id; `contact_ok` switched off. - `DELETE` on `member_details` revoked from `authenticated` (Amazon Q finding on #67). - Privacy: new rows "Your details (optional)" and "Founding Member survey"; version `2026-11-06-r10`.','2026-11-06T14:51:53Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/68'),
(69,'Hotfix: import useEffect in root route (site-wide 500)','## Hotfix: site returns 500 on every page `src/routes/__root.tsx` called `useEffect` (added in #66 for UTM capture) without importing it, so the root component threw a ReferenceError during SSR. Import added. Also fixes two `exactOptionalPropertyTypes` errors (`TeamLogo` sport prop, `admin_campaign_report` p_campaign) found by `tsc`.','2026-11-06T14:59:15Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/69'),
(70,'Add typecheck to pre-commit checks; fix remaining type errors','- New `bun run typecheck` (`tsc --noEmit`); `CLAUDE.md` pre-commit rule is now `lint && typecheck && build`, because `vite build` does not type-check (a missing `useEffect` import shipped a site-wide 500 in #66). - Fixes the last tsc errors so the check passes: `storeEvent` RPC args (omit undefined under `exactOptionalPropertyTypes`, bracket access on index signature) and the root `ErrorComponent` prop type (`error: unknown`).','2026-11-06T15:05:01Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/70'),
(71,'Rewrite Founding Member emails, add survey/referral/countdown, alert support@ inbox','- Rewrote the welcome, Annual Pass and reservation emails and added a launch checklist, Founding Member survey (links to `/feedback`), referral and launch countdown email. All share one branded builder (Puntr logo, light and dark mode, plain-text twin) and match the live product. - New sender `/api/cron/founding-sequence?campaign=<id>` (`&test=1` sends to support@ only). Senders stop at `EMAIL_DAILY_CAP` (default 90) because Resend''s free plan allows 100 a day. - support@puntr.co.za now also gets an alert for Founding spot claims, Annual Pass reservations, survey submissions (with comment) and prediction reports. Each is sent once.','2026-11-08T20:45:48Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/71'),
(72,'Founding sequence: claim email for early access, staggered 9-14 Nov schedule, one numbering','- New `founding-claim-1` email (early-access sign-ups with no account): holds their number and links to /join. - Sequence route supports early-only campaigns and per-person founding numbers. - Welcome recipients no longer skip members who joined before 6 Nov 04:00. - Migration (applied separately after deploy): staggered schedule 9-14 Nov, welcome only 08:00-19:59 SAST. - types.ts: early_access.founding_number.','2026-11-08T21:12:14Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/72'),
(73,'Fix Newsroom: full articles by Michael C., SEO and sharing','- Removes the placeholder `src/routes/newsroom.tsx` (it had no `<Outlet/>`, so it hid both the article list and every article page). - `/newsroom` now lists all three articles from an SSR loader, inside `AppShell`; each article has its own page. - Articles rewritten in full, author Michael C., publish dates 6, 7 and 8 Nov 2026 (migration `20261108235500_newsroom_full_articles.sql`, already applied to the live DB). - SEO: fixed duplicated "| Puntr" title, Person author, dateModified, BreadcrumbList, CollectionPage JSON-LD, Twitter/OG/article tags, article URLs in the sitemap. - Sharing: native share, WhatsApp, X, Facebook, LinkedIn, email, copy link. Body supports `## ` headings and `- ` lists (plain text, never HTML).','2026-11-08T21:48:32Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/73'),
(74,'Add branded default Open Graph image','- New 1200x630 default share image `public/og/puntr.png` (Ink background, white Puntr logo with green dot, Montserrat 800 headline "Predict smarter. Prove it.", 18+ / T&Cs / 0800 006 008 line). - Root `og:image` and `twitter:image` now point to it, with width/height tags. Page-specific images (/founding, newsroom articles) are unchanged.','2026-11-08T22:04:23Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/74'),
(75,'Sign-up confirmation: do not imply picks are live before launch','The post sign-up card said "Post your first pick before kick-off" and linked to /predictions, implying the platform is live. It now says Puntr launches Tuesday 1 December 2026, that members can post a first pick the moment it opens and will be emailed before then, and links to /roadmap.','2026-11-09T05:36:08Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/75'),
(76,'Annual Pass: accept PayFast payf.st short links','- `ANNUAL_PASS_PAYFAST_URL` validation only allowed payfast.co.za / payfast.io, so a PayFast short link (payf.st) was rejected and reservations returned "temporarily unavailable". `payf.st` (https only) is now allowed; other hosts, http, credentials and odd ports are still rejected (tests added). - The reservation function now logs the NAMES of the failing config checks (never values).','2026-11-09T05:42:28Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/76'),
(77,'Admin: Affiliates tab and affiliate partner registry','- New admin **Affiliates** tab: status per partner, reply-deadline countdown, commission terms, partner-issued tracking link, licence check, key dates and an activity log. - New tables `affiliate_partners` and `affiliate_partner_events`: admin-only RLS, service_role grants, DB check that a bookmaker cannot be `live` without a licence check date. - Seeds Hollywoodbets (info requested, reply due 20 Nov 2026), Yesplay.bet (approved), Supabets and Playbet (applied). - `CLAUDE.md` Affiliates section updated (current partner status, Hollywoodbets rules to respect).','2026-11-11T16:50:38Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/77'),
(78,'Annual Pass: payment reminder before the 48h hold lapses','One branded service email, sent once per hold, to a member whose unpaid Founding Annual Pass reservation lapses within 24 hours. - `src/lib/email/annual-pass-reminder.ts` (+ test): the email (light and dark), deadline in SAST, hours left, R299 once-off via PayFast. - `src/routes/api.cron.annual-pass-reminder.ts`: signs a fresh PayFast redirect per member (same mechanism as the reservation email), sends via Resend, records each send in `founding_campaign_sends` (`annual-pass-reminder-<hold expiry>`), max 20 per run. `?dry=1` counts who is due, `?test=1` sends a sample to support@ only. - Migration `20261111190000_annual_pass_reminders.sql`: `annual_pass_reminder_recipients()` (service_role only) and a pg_cron job every 30 min, 07:00-19:59 SAST.','2026-11-11T17:38:20Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/78'),
(79,'Practice Mode thin slice, draw rules and practice email','## Practice Mode (thin slice) for Founding Members, draw rules, practice email **What:** `/practice` (Founding Members only, behind `practice_settings.enabled`, default off): fictional 8-team league simulated server side, invented prices (server authoritative), practice points that never convert to PuntPoints, demo rewards with masked DEMO codes, Practice Graduate badge (10 settled picks), practice leaderboard, accelerated-round option. `practice-tick` cron runs the world. `founding-practice-1` email waits on the same flag. Draw rules published on `/feedback`. **Migration (NOT yet applied):** `supabase/migrations/20261111213000_practice_mode.sql`. Must be applied before merge. Creates `practice_*` tables with RLS, RPCs, `anonymise_account` update, pg_cron jobs, `notice_versions` r11. **Legal copy changed:** `/privacy` (Practice Mode row, r11), `/terms` (section 6, r11), `/feedback` (draw rules), `docs/legal-changelog.md`, `notice_versions` rows. `/cookies`, `/affiliate-disclosure`, `/refunds` unchanged (no new tracker, processor or cookie). Items marked `[attorney review]`. **Checks:** lint, typecheck, build pass; 213 tests pass. **After merge:** apply migration, smoke-test RPCs, set `practice_settings.enabled = true`, trigger `practice-tick`.','2026-11-11T19:44:01Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/79'),
(80,'Admin Draw tab for the R500 voucher draw','## Admin Draw tab for the R500 OTT voucher draw Admin-only tab in `/admin`: shows valid entries (Founding Member, at least one practice pick, draw box ticked), runs the draw (random pick by the database function, witness required, "DRAW" confirmation), shows the winner and the draw log. Server functions re-check `is_admin()` and call the service-role-only database functions. A draw cannot be run before the draw closes (Tue 1 Dec 2026, 00:00 SAST). **Legal copy:** none changed; `docs/legal-changelog.md` has an entry. Winner announcement guidance in the screen matches the published rules (username and Founding number only). **Checks:** lint, typecheck, build pass; tests pass. No migration.','2026-11-11T19:54:06Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/80'),
(82,'Content engine foundation (master brief, phase one, step 2a)','First part of phase one of the master implementation brief (13 Nov 2026): the automated newsroom''s engine, without the admin desk and without any live provider call. - `docs/PUNTR_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md`: repository audit, gaps, decisions for the owner (D1 to D6), risks, plan. - `src/lib/content/`: Parallel Search, Firecrawl and Gemini adapters behind interfaces; free-only Gemini router (`gemini-3.8-flash` then `gemini-3.1-flash-lite`); research ranking; deterministic quality gate; the daily pipeline; Supabase store. - `/api/cron/content-daily` (cron secret; `?dry=1`, `?kind=`, `?force=1`). - Migration `20261113120000_content_engine.sql`: additive. **Not applied to production.** - Newsroom category "Sports Intelligence"; `.env.example`; `CHANGELOG.md`; `docs/CONTENT_ENGINE.md`.','2026-11-13T12:45:00Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/82'),
(83,'Competition scoring, points leaderboards, practice club badges','Master brief 4.5 and 4.6, plus the owner''s request (13 Nov) for badges on the invented Practice Mode clubs. - Migration `20261113160000_competition_scoring.sql` (**applied to production**, additive): `scoring_rules`, append-only `competition_score_ledger` written by a trigger on each settlement event, `competition_leaderboard()` and `my_competition_rank()`. - `/leaderboards`: Competition points board (this week, this month, all time; all or one competition), the member''s own row when outside the first page, and the scoring rules. - `src/lib/scoreboard.ts`: the same rules in TypeScript, tested. - Eight original SVG badges in `public/teams/practice`, shown on practice fixtures.','2026-11-13T12:58:53Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/83'),
(84,'Launch gate, admin portal, wallet, newsroom desk, API limits, covers, SEO','## Do not merge before the migration is applied This code claims an API quota before every Gemini, Parallel, Firecrawl and Resend call and refuses the call if the claim cannot be checked. Merged without `20261113170000_platform_controls_wallet.sql`, fixtures and all emails would stop. Apply the migration first, then merge. Owner-approved scope from 13 Nov (16:12 and 16:51 SAST). - **Launch gate:** live features (picks, wallet, points leaderboard, credit spends) only for admins and members with Early access until 1 Dec 2026 00:00 SAST. Enforced in the database; Practice Mode unchanged. - **Admin portal:** System (status, API limits, launch and transfer settings, scoring), Users (account type, access grants, credits, warn, limit, suspend, ban, messages, broadcast), Newsroom (queue, checks, edit, publish, reject, generate incl. first run of 3, sources, run log, engine settings, project-update feed), Analytics, Action log. Every change logged. - **Wallet** (`/wallet`): PuntPoints balance, transferable amount and transfers within limits (10-200 per transfer, 200/day, 1,000/month, account 14 days old, 7-day hold, referral points never transferable); PAYG credits and prices (nothing on sale; credits never transferable); unified history. - **Practice Mode:** demo wallet (30 demo credits, daily top-up when low) and a match insight unlocked with demo credits. - **API limits:** quota claims per provider (Gemini per model), fail closed; caps editable in System. - **Email:** every app email claims the Resend quota (80/day, 2,500/month by default); batch senders stop at the cap; new outbox cron sends admin messages in batches of 15.','2026-11-13T15:43:06Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/84'),
(85,'Annual Pass: bank-transfer payments in admin; counter shows 16/20','Owner (13 Nov): 4 members paid for the Founding Annual Pass by bank transfer, so the counter must read 16/20. - Migration `20261113200000_annual_pass_bank_transfers.sql`: `annual_pass_offline_payments` (admin read via RLS, writes via service role only), `annual_pass_taken()` now adds unmatched bank transfers, `annual_pass_link_offline()` marks the matched member''s claim `paid` (reference `eft:<id>`) so nothing is counted twice. Seeds the 4 confirmed transfers ("to be matched"). - Admin > **Annual Pass** tab: live counter, record a transfer (payer label, amount, reference, date), match to a member by username, void a wrong entry, reservations and PayFast payments list. All actions logged to `admin_actions`. - Public counter code unchanged: it reads `annual_pass_offer()`, which returns `remaining: 16` once the migration is applied.','2026-11-13T18:45:57Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/85'),
(86,'Admin: send in-app notifications manually (+ desk confirm for critical issues)','- **Admin > Notifications** tab: compose a bell notification (title ≤140, message ≤400, category, optional link), choose **All members / Founding Members / one member (username)**, send now or schedule (up to 60 days), confirm step showing reach, live bell preview, history with read counts, who sent it, and **Withdraw**. Logged to `admin_actions`. - Migration `20261113201000_admin_notifications_composer.sql`: `notifications.audience` (''all'' | ''founding''), `notifications.created_by`, `is_founding_member()`, read policy so Founding-only notices are seen only by Founding Members and admins. - Bell: admins no longer see other members'' private notices in their own bell; refreshes every 5 min so scheduled notices appear without realtime. - Users > Message members: the in-app copy now respects the Founding audience (it went to everyone before). - Newsroom desk: publishing an article that failed critical checks now needs a confirm listing every issue (open item from 13 Nov). - Link validation: in-app paths or https only; puntr.co.za links become in-app paths; `//`, `javascript:` and credentials refused (unit-tested).','2026-11-13T18:47:28Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/86'),
(87,'Branded Supabase Auth emails via Resend + password reset flow','- **Send Email Hook** route `POST /api/auth/send-email`: verifies the Standard Webhooks signature (`SEND_EMAIL_HOOK_SECRET`, 5-minute tolerance, constant-time compare), maps the payload (incl. Supabase''s reversed `token_hash`/`token_hash_new` for secure email change) and sends through Resend from **Puntr - South Africa <support@puntr.co.za>**. Never logs addresses, codes or links. Non-200 on failure so Supabase reports it. - **Branded templates** (`src/lib/email/auth-emails.ts`, shared light/dark builder + new large code block): sign-up confirmation, passwordless sign-in (`482913 is your Puntr sign-in code`), password reset, email change (both addresses), invite, re-authentication, and security notices (password / email / phone changed, sign-in method linked/unlinked, two-step added/removed). 18+ and 0800 006 008 in every footer. - **`/auth/confirm`**: verifies the token hash only after a tap (scanner-safe), then continues to an allowlisted page. - **`/reset-password`**: forgot-password flow (request → 6-digit code or link → new password), never reveals whether an address is registered. "Forgot your password?" link on sign-in. - Auth emails bypass Puntr''s own daily cap (but still count toward it). - `docs/AUTH_EMAILS.md`: one-time dashboard setup.','2026-11-13T18:48:33Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/87'),
(88,'Real team badges via Parallel Search (strict: unbadged fixtures hidden)','Owner rule (13 Nov): every team on the platform must have its real badge, found with Parallel Search, before it is surfaced. - Migration `20261113210000_team_badges.sql` (**applied**): `team_badges` registry (public read of verified rows only, service-role writes), pg_cron `team-badges` at :07/:37. - Resolver (`src/lib/badges/`): Parallel Search finds the club''s English Wikipedia article → Wikipedia summary gives the lead image → deterministic checks (club/team article, not a person/stadium/season/disambiguation; image on upload.wikimedia.org and crest-like) → mirrored to the public `media` bucket (`teams/<sport>/<slug>.png`, PNG/JPEG/WebP only). Every Parallel call claims the shared `parallel` quota. Failures retry after 24h, max 3 tries. - **Strict gate**: `fetchUpcomingFixtures`, `fetchLiveFixtures` and `fetchResults` drop fixtures whose teams have no verified badge (or bundled logo). The permanent pick log is never filtered. Emergency switch `VITE_TEAM_BADGES_REQUIRED=false`. - `TeamLogo` uses the registry first (object-contain on white, so crests aren''t cropped). - Admin > Fixtures > **Team badges**: every team in fixtures with status, source page and error; "Find missing badges now"; set a badge from an https image URL (mirrored); reject a wrong badge. - `types.ts` regenerated from production.','2026-11-13T18:59:06Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/88'),
(89,'Badges fix: thumb.wikimedia.org thumbnails, better article choice','First production run verified 1 of 22: Wikipedia now serves summary thumbnails from `thumb.wikimedia.org` (with tracking params), and town articles (Bournemouth, Brentford) outranked the clubs. - Accept `upload.` and `thumb.wikimedia.org`, strip query strings; Wikimedia redirects allowed only if the final host is Wikimedia (admin URLs still no redirects). - Try up to 3 article candidates, club-like titles first. - Tests added (9 in badges). lint, typecheck pass. No migration, no legal change.','2026-11-13T19:06:08Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/89'),
(90,'Redeemable rewards catalogue (locked until 1 Dec) + Terms/Privacy r13','- Migration `20261113220000_rewards_catalogue.sql` (**applied**): `rewards` gains `category`, `face_value_cents`, `available_from`, `fulfilment`, `sort`, `terms`; public `rewards_catalogue()` preview (anon + members, never betting vouchers); `redeem_reward()` refuses with `not_yet_available` before `launch_at()` (1 Dec 2026 00:00 SAST) or a reward''s own date (admins can test early; early-access testers cannot redeem). 16 starter rewards seeded (all need approval): - OTT vouchers R20/R50/R100/R250/R500 = 400/1,000/2,000/5,000/10,000 pts (1 pt ≈ R0.05) - PAYG credits 10/25/50 = 300/700/1,300 pts · Puntr Pro 7 days 750 / 30 days 2,500 - Puntr cap 3,000 · T-shirt 4,000 · mug 2,000 (25 each) · PSL club scarf 5,000 (10) · replica jersey 15,000 (5) · two PSL tickets 6,000 (5) - `/rewards`: grouped catalogue with category icons, rand face values, terms, "Opens 1 Dec" locked buttons; visible to signed-out visitors too (join CTA). Betting vouchers still only for eligible members, labelled Ad + RG notice. - Admin > Rewards: "Edit points" per reward. - **Legal: Terms + Privacy r13** (catalogue types, delivery, reward delivery data row), `notice_versions` rows (applied), legal-changelog with `[attorney review]` (OTT brand use, club/league marks and ticket rules, Puntr-funded rewards, retention).','2026-11-13T19:20:03Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/90'),
(91,'Onboarding quests with verified PuntPoints + profile completion tracker (Terms/Privacy r14)','Firecrawl-style "Get started, earn PuntPoints" onboarding with verified awards, plus a profile completion tracker. - Migration `20261113230000_onboarding_quests.sql` (**applied**): `quests`, `quest_progress` (RLS: own rows; writes only through functions), 15 quests: - **auto (database-checked):** confirm email 50, two-step 100, complete profile 150, verify identity 100, email updates 50, WhatsApp/SMS updates 50 (latest `consent_records`), invite a friend 150 (friend joined with your link + confirmed email). - **review (admin-checked):** Instagram 50, Facebook page 50, X 50, TikTok 50, WhatsApp group 75, Telegram 50. Member must open the link first (tracked), wait ≥10 s, then submit their handle → Admin > **Quests** approves/rejects. Points only on approval. - **device:** install app 100, push on 50: `coming_soon` until the PWA ships (flip the flag then; the app checks `display-mode: standalone` / `Notification.permission`). - Points go to the PuntPoints ledger once per quest (`rule_code ''quest''`, unique index), only for members in good standing (18+, confirmed email, not banned/suspended/on a break) and while `points_enabled`. - `quest_evidence_purge()` daily: social usernames deleted 90 days after the check / at account deletion. - `/join` done screen: compact quest checklist (before the redirect) + "Go to my account". - `/account`: **Profile completion** tracker (8 items, %), full quest checklist (`#get-started`); re-checks on tab focus and after saving details. - Admin > Quests: review queue with handle, link to Puntr''s page, approve/reject with reason; totals.','2026-11-13T19:23:23Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/91'),
(92,'Rewards: typecheck fix','Typecheck fix after #90 (the optional `available_from` field was missing from the action parameter type). Runtime unaffected (vite build does not type-check). lint, typecheck (0 errors), build pass.','2026-11-13T19:21:09Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/92'),
(93,'Marketing motion: preloader, loading bar, light/dark mode, animated sports pages','- **Preloader** (`components/motion/preloader.tsx`): Puntr logo, word-by-word animated slogan "Predict smarter. Prove it.", loading bar. Server-rendered so it covers first paint, once per browser session, on marketing pages (home, sports, about, founding, how it works, pricing, roadmap, rewards, newsroom). Leaves after page load (0.9–2.4 s); CSS fallback fades it without JS; hidden for prefers-reduced-motion. - **Route loading bar** (green, top) for page loads over 120 ms. - **Light/dark mode**: `.dark` token set in `styles.css` (Puntr ink background, same green), no-flash boot script in `<head>`, sun/moon toggle in the header, follows the device until chosen, white wordmark `public/puntrlogo-dark.png` for dark mode. - **Motion components**: `HeroBackdrop` (drifting green glows, grid, pitch markings that draw themselves), `Reveal`, `CountUp`, `BadgeMarquee` (verified club crests). - **Sports landing pages**: new animated hero (sport icon, status pill with pulse when live, count-up stats), club badge marquee on football, staggered reveals. - Home, Founding, Roadmap, Pricing, How it works, About: hero backdrops and scroll-driven section reveals (CSS `animation-timeline: view()`, progressive). - Brand note: dark surfaces are new tokens on the existing ink; no new hues.','2026-11-13T19:31:33Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/93'),
(94,'No rewarded social follows (visit links); reward funding control; Terms/Privacy r15','- Owner: remove incentives that risk the Puntr social pages. Instagram/Facebook/X/TikTok quests become non-rewarded "Visit" links (shown under "Stay connected", no points, never counted in progress); open submissions closed without points; `quest_award` refuses unrewarded quests. WhatsApp + Telegram community quests unchanged. - Rewards: `funded_by` (Puntr / sponsor / partner) + sponsor name + optional https link per reward, editable in Admin > Rewards; catalogue shows who funds each reward (`rel="sponsored"`). - Migration `20261113233000_social_quests_reward_funding.sql` (**applied**), `types.ts` regenerated. - Legal: Terms + Privacy r15 (notice_versions applied), legal-changelog. - Checks: lint 0 errors, typecheck, tests, build pass.','2026-11-13T19:39:06Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/94'),
(95,'PFIE top-6 leagues; newsroom always publishes on schedule + admin email alert','- **PFIE leagues** (owner): the top six leagues SA bettors and tipsters follow: Betway Premiership (PSL), Premier League, Champions League, plus new **La Liga, Serie A, Bundesliga** sources (official sites laliga.com, legaseriea.it, bundesliga.com as authoritative + trusted list). New teams get their badges automatically from the badge job. - **Newsroom**: new setting `publish_on_schedule` (migration **applied**, switched on): the scheduled (cron) article is published even if it fails the quality checks; manual runs keep the checks. After every scheduled run an email goes to **admin@puntr.co.za** (`NEWSROOM_ALERT_EMAIL` overrides): title, score, every check result, link to the desk and the article; failed runs also alert (retries at 06:20/06:40). Checkbox in Newsroom settings. Test added. - Quota note: three more leagues mean more Parallel searches on busy weekends; the shared quota (60/day) fails closed and results catch up on the next run. - Legal: none (AI label on articles already covered). - Checks: lint 0 errors, typecheck, tests, build pass.','2026-11-13T19:40:17Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/95'),
(96,'Remove green tint from hero backdrops','Owner feedback: green tint on the homepage hero. The drifting green glows are now off by default (opt-in `glow` prop, much softer when used), the grid is lighter and the pitch markings are neutral ink in light mode (green only in dark mode). No other change. lint, typecheck, build pass.','2026-11-13T19:41:54Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/96'),
(97,'MFA enforced on every page + in the database (admin, redemptions)','Two-step verification was only asked for inside the `/join` sign-in card. A member who signed in by magic link to another page, returned from Google, restored a session or opened a new tab stayed at `aal1` with full access, and the database did not check `aal`. - `MfaGate` (root): on every page, a signed-in member with a verified factor and an `aal1` session gets a full-screen authenticator prompt (or "use a different account" = sign out). `/join` keeps its own step. - Migration `20261113235000_mfa_enforcement.sql` (**applied**): `mfa_ok()` (aal2, or no verified factor); `is_admin()` now requires it (all admin RLS and server checks); `redeem_reward()` refuses with `mfa_required`. - Verified in production with a rolled-back transaction on the admin account: no factor -> admin true; verified factor + aal1 -> admin false; aal2 -> true. - No member has a verified factor yet (0 in production), so nobody is affected today.','2026-11-13T19:44:57Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/97'),
(98,'Mobile-friendly fixture, prediction, result and pick cards','Shared `FixtureMatchup` component: badge above team name on phones, side by side from `sm`. Applied to home Next fixtures (now a card grid), predictions, results and pick cards. Legal copy: nothing needed (layout only); changelog entry added.','2026-11-13T19:51:53Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/98'),
(99,'Tailor mobile navigation for guests and members','- Replace the signed-in mobile navigation with a four-destination floating dock: Fixtures, Duels, PuntPoints and More. - Add a compact active pill indicator and preserve the existing More drawer. - Hide the guest bottom tab dock and show a sticky Founding Access conversion bar with a one-tap Claim Spot action. - Keep the mobile header free of a duplicate hamburger control; the More action remains in the member dock.','2026-11-13T20:18:56Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/99'),
(100,'Declutter desktop header with grouped navigation','- Replace the crowded desktop link row with three semantic dropdowns: Intelligence, Community, and About / Platform. - Group fixtures and predictions, AI matchup tools, graded results, leaderboards, H2H, tipster rankings, How It Works, Pricing, Newsroom, and Roadmap. - Preserve the signed-in member avatar/account menu, notifications, theme control, and guest sign-in action. - Promote the guest CTA to **Claim Founding Access**. - Add a compact founding availability indicator for desktop headers so the full-width tracker no longer overflows or crowds the header. - Keep the full founding progress tracker available in page content.','2026-11-13T20:25:39Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/100'),
(101,'Restore Join free desktop header CTA','- Restore the previous guest header CTA label: **Join free**. - Keep the **Sign in** text link alongside it. - Preserve the grouped desktop navigation and founding counter changes from PR #100. - Header CTA label only; no route, auth, or database changes.','2026-11-14T02:23:14Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/101'),
(102,'Logos/Branding admin tab and footer logo shuffler','## Logos/Branding admin and footer logo shuffler - Admin > Logos/Branding: upload (resized to 480 px longest edge and compressed to WebP in the browser; server re-checks magic bytes, 400 KB cap, no SVG), choose placements (footer, About, Bookmaker Directory, homepage, Puntr brand), link, order, Active toggle, add custom logos. Team badges panel embedded. - `brand_logos` table (migration `20261114010000_brand_logos.sql`, APPLIED to production): RLS public read only for active rows with an image; writes service-role via admin-checked server functions, logged in `admin_actions`. 14 rows seeded (WCGRB, NLC, NGB, SARGF, PayFast, Ozow, Hollywoodbets, 1Voucher, OTT, AdMarula, Track360, 3 Puntr brand), all inactive. - Footer: animated shuffler (one slot swaps at a time; static for reduced motion). Public sees only active logos with images; admins also see dashed placeholders. - About page and Bookmaker Directory use uploaded logos when present. Legal copy: no page changed (no visitor data collected). `docs/legal-changelog.md` entry, marked `[attorney review]` for implied-endorsement and affiliate-creative risk. No new provider, tracker or processor. Checks: lint, typecheck, tests, build pass.','2026-11-13T23:10:58Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/102'),
(103,'Endorsements admin tab with Gemini drafts and Resend sending','## Endorsements admin tab - Admin > Endorsements: organisations with kind, region, website, contact (name, role, email), status (prospect, drafted, contacted, follow-up due, in discussion, endorsed, declined, no response, paused), what we ask for, reasons, notes, follow-up date, do-not-contact, and a history log. Add your own organisations. Seeded: WCGRB, NLC, Gauteng Gambling Board, SARGF, NGB. - Gemini drafts outreach and follow-up emails (existing free-model router and quota guard). The model sees only organisation facts and Puntr''s fact sheet: NOT the contact''s name and no member data. Salutation `{{first_name}}` is filled in on send. - Drafts are editable, checked for banned wording and for claims of endorsement/approval/partnership, then sent via Resend from `Michael from Puntr <michael@puntr.co.za>` or `Puntr Partners <partners@puntr.co.za>` with a two-step confirm. Claim-before-send (no double send), one email per organisation per 24 h, do-not-contact enforced, signature and a "reply stop" line added, status and follow-up date (+7 days) updated, all logged to `admin_actions`. - `sendViaResend`: a caller that names its own sender is no longer silently switched to the old community sender if the domain check fails. - Migration `20261114020000_endorsements.sql` APPLIED to production (3 admin-only tables, RLS on, no policies). - Separate commit formats three files left unformatted on main by #100 so `lint` passes. Legal: no page changed; `docs/legal-changelog.md` entry with `[attorney review]` (storing business contact details; B2B opt-out line; sender identity). No new processor: Gemini and Resend were already in use.','2026-11-13T23:21:11Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/103'),
(104,'Docs: multi-language plan','## Plan Docs only: `docs/MULTILANGUAGE_PLAN.md`. No code, no legal change.','2026-11-13T23:22:25Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/104'),
(105,'Optimize guest Peek & Hook prediction gate','- Keep the first two upcoming fixtures fully readable for guests; fixture #3 onward retains its match context and kickoff time while proprietary intelligence is frosted behind the existing `bg-background/60 backdrop-blur-md` overlay. - Refresh the centered founding conversion card with the “Unlock All Matchday Predictions” and R0 Founding Annual Pass reservation message. - Open the existing multi-step `/join` flow in a dialog iframe, preserving the predictions page and its scroll position when the visitor signs up or closes the modal. - Replace the mobile dock’s Duels destination with Community, linking to `/community`. - Reuses the existing `FREE_ITEMS = 2` and `useGated` logic; no fabricated match intelligence or new backend data was introduced. - The current `IntelPanel` still renders its existing “available at launch” placeholders where live model data is not yet supplied.','2026-11-14T02:16:07Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/105'),
(106,'Align desktop navigation with mobile information architecture','- Replace the old desktop Intelligence / Community / About-Platform groups with the requested direct links: Home, Fixtures & Predictions, and Community & Duels. - Add a green pulsing live indicator beside Fixtures & Predictions only when the live-fixture query returns at least one fixture. - Add icon-led Browse, Discover, and Platform dropdowns with the requested destinations. - Add nested Featured Sports and Competitions & Leagues submenus. Sports use the existing `/sports/$sport` routes and the competition submenu is sourced from the repository''s configured competition catalogue. - Include H2H (routes to the existing `/leaderboards` experience), disabled Fantasy League with a Coming Soon label, and Upcoming Roadmap. - Preserve the existing right-side action cluster (theme, notifications, account menu, sign-in and founding CTA).','2026-11-14T02:21:55Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/106'),
(107,'Standardize bookmaker and partner logo tiles','- Add a shared `PartnerLogo` component for consistent bookmaker and partner logo presentation. - Apply grayscale, 60% opacity and dark-mode monochrome treatment by default, with 300ms transitions and scale/color restoration on hover, focus and active states. - Standardize logo image sizing to `max-h-8 sm:max-h-10` with `object-contain`. - Remove the hardcoded white bookmaker logo backgrounds and use semantic `card-surface` containers for PlatformRail and About partner tiles. - Apply the shared treatment across PlatformRail, About, Bookmakers and the Footer logo shuffle.','2026-11-14T03:08:48Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/107'),
(108,'Refresh desktop navigation and collapsible side rail','- Merge the previous Browse and Discover dropdown contents into one desktop **Platform** menu with a toolkit icon. - Remove the Head-to-Head (H2H) menu link. - Rename the existing Platform dropdown to **More** and remove its leading icon. - Rename desktop direct links to **Predictions** and **Community**. - Make the desktop side rail collapsible and reduce its primary links to Fixtures, Results, Leaderboards and Support centre. - Add `/fixtures` and `/leaderboard` compatibility routes that redirect to the existing `/predictions` and `/leaderboards` pages respectively.','2026-11-14T03:13:24Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/108'),
(109,'Fix production crash caused by missing Swords icon import','## Production incident fix - Restore the `Swords` icon import in `site-header.tsx`. - The featured sports list still references `Swords` for combat sports, but PR #108 removed its import while removing the obsolete H2H menu item. - This caused a server-side `ReferenceError: Swords is not defined` and prevented the application from loading.','2026-11-14T03:46:11Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/109'),
(110,'Update mobile dock destinations','- Change the mobile dock''s Fixtures destination to Predictions (`/predictions`) and update its label. - Keep Community labelled Community and route it to `/community` (already aligned in the current main branch). - Route the signed-in PuntPoints dock item to `/rewards`, the member-facing PuntPoints and Rewards page, instead of the public PuntPoints landing page. - Keep active-state styling aligned with Predictions and match routes.','2026-11-14T03:47:55Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/110'),
(111,'QA audit: guest permission fixes, restore Supabase config, UI/UX polish, Gemini fallbacks','QA audit of the whole platform (owner brief, 14 Nov 2026), with fixes, a sitewide UI/UX polish pass and extra free Gemini fallback models. Multi-language follows in a separate PR after approval.','2026-11-14T05:12:00Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/111'),
(112,'Multi-language: Afrikaans (in review), Admin > Translations, isiZulu coming soon','## Multi-language: Afrikaans (in review), Admin > Translations, isiZulu coming soon Builds on #111 (QA polish). Merge #111 first; this diff then shows only the language work. ### What changed - **Afrikaans** draft for every public section (`src/locales/af/`) and the six legal pages (`src/content/legal/af/`). Each legal page has a notice that the English version applies if the two differ. - **Admins only for now:** the selector shows "Afrikaans · In review" only to admins (`puntr_lang_preview` cookie). Everyone else stays on English until a native speaker signs it off. - **Admin > Translations tab:** English and Afrikaans side by side. Approve or suggest per string or for a whole section, review legal pages page by page, and sign off by name. A review goes stale when either text changes. - **isiZulu** is listed as "Coming soon" (revisit Fri 20 Nov, 11:00 SAST). **isiXhosa** is removed. - New `pages` namespace: Tools, Bookmakers, Refer a friend, PuntPoints, Live scores, the home proof demo and the bookmaker notice no longer have hardcoded English. - `/pricing` Annual Pass box now matches the actual flow (free reservation, then a PayFast link paid within 48h). - Parity test: every English key must exist in Afrikaans with the same placeholders. ### Database `supabase/migrations/20261114050000_translation_reviews.sql` adds `translation_reviews` and `translation_signoffs` (RLS on, service role only). **Not applied yet: needs owner approval.** The Translations tab needs it. ### Legal copy','2026-11-14T05:12:16Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/112'),
(113,'Match cards v2: form guides, kick-off pill, analytics sheet, animated filters','Batch 1, Task 5 (plus the /predictions part of Task 1). - **Match card v2** (`FixtureCard` upgraded, new `LiveMatchCard`): competition monogram + name, kick-off pill ("Today 15:30 SAST"; countdown in the last 6 h; LIVE / Full time), crests with last-5 W/D/L form guides, one-line goals-per-game read, action footer with **View Deep Analytics** (sheet, no route change) and **Match room**. - **Analytics sheet**: bottom sheet on phones, right panel on desktop. Form, goals per game, head to head, community 1X2 split, model placeholders ("at launch"), CTA to the match room. - **Animated filters** (`FilterChips`, motion shared layout + AnimatePresence) on /predictions (All, Today, each competition) and the weekly leaderboard toggle. Reduced motion respected. - Match page header uses the same monogram, pill, form guides, insight and sheet. - /predictions: illustrative sample fixtures removed; real cards in a 1/2/3-column grid; guest Peek & Hook gate unchanged (first 2 open). - Fixed the untranslated `side.liveNow` heading in the right rail.','2026-11-14T05:28:16Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/113'),
(114,'Fixtures hub + 21-competition coverage (fixes zone-less kick-off rejections)','Batch 1, Task 2. - **/fixtures** is now a real page (previously redirected to /predictions): search (team or competition), date strip, region chips (South Africa, England, Europe, Africa, Rest of the world) and competition chips with counts that follow the other filters, group by day or competition, cards or compact list, analytics sheet on every match, "Competitions we track" panel, CTA to /predictions. URL holds the state (shareable). SportsEvent ItemList JSON-LD; sitemap entry. - **Coverage 6 → 21 competitions** (`PFIE_SOURCES` + `competitions.ts`): Europa League, Conference League, Ligue 1, EFL Championship, FA Cup, EFL Cup, Eredivisie, Liga Portugal, Saudi Pro League, Nedbank Cup, Motsepe Foundation Championship, CAF Champions League, CAF Confederation Cup, AFCON (incl. qualifiers), Bafana Bafana friendlies. New ones are search-only (no Firecrawl page reads).','2026-11-14T05:37:11Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/114'),
(115,'Community Head-to-Head Duels (stakes behind a switch, default off)','Batch 1, Task 4. - **Create**: a member challenges another member by username, or posts an open challenge, on an upcoming football match with 2-3 calls (Match result, BTTS, Over/Under 2.5), an optional message and an optional PuntPoints stake. - **Accept**: the opponent makes calls on the same markets; stakes go into escrow (`puntpoints_ledger` kind `duel_stake`). Named opponents can decline; challengers can cancel while pending. Unaccepted challenges expire at kick-off with a refund. - **Locked at kick-off**: calls are hidden (only your own are visible) until kick-off, then shown side by side in the duel room. - **Community poll**: non-participants vote "Who called it better?" from kick-off until settlement; animated split bar; only totals are public. - **Settlement**: `/api/cron/settle` grades every call with the shared `grade()` and calls `settle_duel()`: more correct calls takes the pot (2 × stake) plus duel XP (win 3, draw 1); ties and void matches refund both. Idempotent. - **H2H Duel Leaderboard** (7 days / all time) on /duels and /leaderboards, ranked by XP then wins; PuntPoints never affect the order (keeps the Terms claim true). - Duels in the side nav; "Duels on this match" + challenge button in every match room; notifications to the opponent/challenger on challenge, accept and settle.','2026-11-14T12:11:57Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/115'),
(116,'Member Matchday card + favourites (Task 1)','Batch 1, Task 1 (home + favourites; the /predictions clean-up shipped in #113). - **Guests**: home keeps the illustrative Fixtures/Results/Leaderboard preview (also in the server HTML for crawlers). - **Signed-in members**: the preview is replaced by **Your matchday**: next 7 days, favourite teams first, then favourite competitions (reason tags), kick-off pills and crests, **View full intelligence** (filtered /fixtures when one competition is chosen), **Challenge a tipster** (duel dialog with those fixtures), and **Your active duels**. Without favourites it shows upcoming matches and a "Choose favourites" prompt. - **Account > Your favourites**: sports (roadmap sports marked "soon"), up to 10 competitions (all 21 tracked), up to 10 teams via search over teams with upcoming fixtures.','2026-11-14T12:18:43Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/116'),
(117,'Tools: Slip Converter copy + pre-launch tools plan (Task 3)','Batch 1, Task 3. - Betting Slip Converter card: owner''s 2-sentence description (English + Afrikaans draft). Card stays "Coming soon", so nothing claims the tool is live. - `docs/TOOLS_PLAN.md`: definition of "live" for the Slip Converter, Edge Finder cards and Punt AI (MVP + Practice Mode 2.0), build order, and decisions needed (POPIA for slip screenshots, affiliate branding, Pro billing). Legal copy: nothing needed (no feature change). Checks: lint 0 errors, typecheck, translation test, build OK.','2026-11-14T12:20:48Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/117'),
(118,'Review follow-ups: duel settlement isolation, Matchday load fallback','Follow-ups to review findings on #115 and #116 (merged before the reviews arrived). Fixed: - `runDuelSettlement`: each duel settles in its own try/catch, so one failure no longer blocks the rest of the cron run (new test). - `MatchdayWidget`: a load failure now ends the loading state instead of leaving the skeleton up. Checked and not changed: - `gradeDuels` consistency guard: all rows for a duel come from one join in one query, so the fixture data cannot differ between them. - Sports cardinality 8 vs `MAX_FAVOURITES` 10: the DB only allows the 8 listed sports, so a member can never send more than 8. - `vote_duel` NULL check: a NULL `suspended_until` makes the condition NULL, which correctly does not block a member who is not suspended. - IMMUTABLE/STABLE labels: no effect on these functions. - Both duel migrations (`20261114080000`, `20261114081000`) are applied in production, in order. Legal copy: nothing needed. Checks: lint 0 errors, typecheck, tests, build OK.','2026-11-14T12:26:57Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/118'),
(119,'Duel stakes on (counsel approved) + PuntPoints economics plan','- Owner decision 14 Nov 15:00 SAST: counsel approved duel stakes. `duels_stakes_enabled = true` applied in production; migration records it. - `docs/PUNTPOINTS_ECONOMICS_PLAN.md`: scope and decisions for the 21-23 Nov economics, loss-prevention and abuse-guardrails session. - Legal changelog entry (no page change; Terms r16 already cover stakes).','2026-11-14T13:04:34Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/119'),
(120,'League standings + team form sync (hold: migration pending)','League standings and team form synchronisation. **DO NOT MERGE until migration `20261114140000_standings_form_sync.sql` is applied** (the form view and tables must exist first; the apply needs the owner''s confirmation in the Supabase prompt).','2026-11-14T14:18:58Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/120'),
(121,'Mobile dock: scroll-aware bar with bottom-sheet flyouts','Upgrades the mobile floating dock (`src/components/layout/mobile-nav.tsx`) into a scroll-responsive tab bar with bottom-sheet sub-menus. - **Scroll behaviour:** hides on a sustained scroll down (`translate-y-[150%]`, 250 ms ease-in-out), returns on scroll up. 12 px hysteresis, always visible within 20 px of the top, iOS rubber-band clamped, `env(safe-area-inset-bottom)` kept. - **Tabs:** Home (`/`), Predictions (Fixtures, Results, Insights), Community (Leaderboards, Sports discussions, Head-to-head duels, Newsroom), Platform (Betting toolkit, Bookmaker directory, PuntPoints & rewards, Pay-as-you-go credits, Roadmap, Share feedback). Platform replaces the PuntPoints tab. - **Flyout:** anchored sheet above the dock, `bg-black/40 backdrop-blur-sm` backdrop. Closes on link tap, backdrop tap, Escape or page scroll. - **Active state:** the parent tab is highlighted when the path belongs to its sub-menu. - **A11y:** `aria-haspopup="menu"`, `aria-expanded`, menu/menuitem roles, arrow-key navigation, focus moves into the sheet and back to the tab, `motion-reduce` respected. - **Guests:** same dock sitewide, with the Founding Member conversion row attached on top of it (moves with the dock). Hidden for guests on `/join` and `/admin`; the strip is also hidden on `/founding`. Footer clearance updated.','2026-11-14T14:38:24Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/121'),
(122,'Betting slips: manual, text and photo entry with review and publish','## Betting slips (pre-MVP) Members add a bookmaker slip by **typing it, pasting its text or uploading a photo**. They review and edit every field, save it as a private draft, then **publish**. Each leg on a Puntr fixture with a supported market (match result, double chance, BTTS, over/under 2.5) becomes a normal pick through `create_prediction`, so the launch gate, 18+, limits, grading, leaderboards and PuntPoints all apply unchanged. Other legs are shown on the slip as "tracked only". ### Privacy design (POPIA, "no personal data to AI") - Photos are re-encoded to WebP in the browser (EXIF and location dropped) and **read on the device** with self-hosted tesseract.js (`public/ocr`, copied from node_modules at build time; nothing is committed). **No image goes to an AI service.** - Slip text is scrubbed of detectable personal details twice, in the browser and on the server (emails, SA phone numbers, 8+ digit runs, lines labelled name, username, balance, account, ID and similar). - A deterministic parser runs first. Only when it finds no legs is the **scrubbed text** sent to Gemini (Flash-Lite first, existing quota guards, 20 AI reads per member per day; the log keeps no text). - Photos sit in a private `slips` bucket (owner-only policies) and are deleted after 30 days by the `slip-images` job (03:25 SAST). - The bookmaker is shown only to the owner. Stake and return are hidden on published slips unless the member opts in. ### Guardrails (tested in a rolled-back transaction against production)','2026-11-14T14:51:01Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/122'),
(123,'fix(slips): label scrubber no longer drops team names like Cardiff','Follow-up to #122. The slip scrubber''s label pattern had no closing word boundary, so `card` matched **Card**iff City (EFL Championship) and the fixture line was removed before parsing. It now needs a whole word; a test covers team names containing label words. Legal copy: nothing needed to change (no change to what is collected, stored or sent).','2026-11-14T15:01:31Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/123'),
(124,'feat(dev): live MVP readiness checklist and score on /dev','`/dev` gets a **Readiness** tab (now the default): a weighted MVP launch checklist with a score out of 100 that moves as tasks are ticked. - 8 workstreams, weights summing to 100: core product (16), fixtures/results/history (16), payments (16), AI (12), PWA (8), trust and compliance (12), platform ops (8), go-to-market (12). 54 tasks, 24 flagged as launch blockers. - **Manual tasks** are ticked on the page and saved for the whole team in `dev_readiness_state`. The score updates straight away (same pure `computeReadiness()` on client and server) and rolls back if the save fails. - **Metric tasks** are read live: Founding Members /100, Annual Passes /20, fixtures in the next 14 days /120, completed results /2,500, leagues with tables /12. - Score today with production numbers: **35/100, Not ready** (15 Founding Members, 4 passes, 14 upcoming fixtures, 0 historical results, 0 tables). - The 30 Oct encrypted blueprint stays as a "Blueprint (archive)" tab.','2026-11-14T16:33:10Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/124'),
(125,'fix(annual-pass): offer closes 23:59 SAST on 30 November 2026','Owner correction (14 Nov): the Founding Annual Pass offer closes at 23:59 SAST on 30 November 2026, not 16 November. - Migration `20261114170000`: new deadline in `annual_pass_offer()` and `claim_annual_pass()`. `annual_pass_taken()` is untouched (production also counts offline payments). - Code and copy: claim card, Founding note (en-ZA, af), admin label, expiry email constant and tests, `PASS_DEADLINE_TEXT`. - Legal: `/terms` (r19, en and af), `/refunds` (en and af), `notice_versions` terms r19, `docs/legal-changelog.md` entry marked `[attorney review]`.','2026-11-14T17:09:55Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/125'),
(126,'docs(economics): PAYG packs and Puntr Pro unit economics','`src/lib/economics.ts` + tests + `docs/PAYG_ECONOMICS.md`. Pure model, nothing member-facing, no flags changed. Findings: current packs (R25/R60/R120) keep at least 66% worst-case margin; keep them. Pro at R99 needs a server-side fair-use cap (recommended 90 AI actions a month, 15 a day); Annual Pass members a tighter 40.','2026-11-14T17:10:03Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/126'),
(127,'feat(payments): PAYG credit packs through PayFast (off until switched on)','Credit-pack purchases through PayFast, built and **off**: needs PayFast env vars, `payments_enabled=true` (Admin > System) and the legal copy. - Migration `20261114200000`: `payment_orders` (RLS, own-select), `payments_enabled()`, idempotent `grant_credit_purchase()`, settings `payments_enabled` and `usd_zar` (editable in Admin), one credit price list matching /pricing. - `/api/payfast/itn`: source IP, signature, PayFast postback, exact amount, one grant per `pf_payment_id`. - `/wallet`: pack buttons appear only when payments are on server-side. - Tests: signing, ITN accept/tamper, IP ranges, config. 468 tests pass.','2026-11-14T17:41:53Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/127'),
(128,'chore(annual-pass): run the Annual Pass campaign email to 30 Nov','Owner decision: Annual Pass campaign email cron now runs 10 to 30 Nov (was 10 to 15). Already applied in production via cron.alter_job; this records it as a migration. Each address still gets the email once. Legal copy: nothing needed (no change to what is collected, stored, shown or promised beyond the existing offer).','2026-11-14T17:16:29Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/128'),
(129,'Fixtures: surface every verified PFIE fixture + season results backfill','## Why fixtures were missing The 04:00 SAST PFIE sync ran all 21 competitions in one serverless call and only wrote at the end. The call hit its time limit first (production `pfie_runs`: runs stop after ~3-5 min), so nothing verified on 14 Nov reached `fixtures` (still 15 rows, PSL + EPL only). The latest runs had verified fixtures ready to publish for Bundesliga, La Liga, UEL and PSL that were thrown away. - **Chunked fixture sync:** each call takes competitions not synced in 12 h (oldest first), writes each as it finishes, stops starting new ones after 150 s. Cron every 6 min 03:00-03:42 SAST. `?force=1` for a manual full pass. - **Trusted-time rule:** a zoned kick-off from one trusted outlet (SuperSport, BBC, Sky, ESPN, Kickoff, etc.) is verified when another site lists the same match on the same printed date and nobody states a different time. Untrusted sites never set a time this way. Tests added. - **Badge rule off by default:** fixtures without a resolved badge now show with initials instead of being hidden; the resolver still runs every 30 min. `VITE_TEAM_BADGES_REQUIRED=true` restores the strict rule. - **Season results backfill:** new `season` job, 21-day windows from 1 Aug 2025 to today - 42 days, current season first. Same verification as form history: official site or two domains with the same score. Cron `sync-season` 06:00-06:50 SAST, 2 windows per call (inside the existing Parallel/Firecrawl/Gemini daily caps). - **/results > Season results:** filterable by competition, each score credits the confirming sites.','2026-11-14T18:16:34Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/129'),
(130,'Puntr Pro: monthly billing through PayFast (off until switched on)','Puntr Pro at R99/month through PayFast subscriptions. **Off** behind the same switch as credit packs (`payments_enabled` + PayFast variables).','2026-11-14T18:22:22Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/130'),
(131,'Season backfill: better searches, diagnostics, retry empty windows','Follow-up to #129 (approved backfill). The first live season run (EPL, PSL, La Liga, 25 Sep-15 Oct) found 0 results and was recorded as done, so those windows would never retry. - Searches use month names and matchday/round-up phrasing that finds archive pages. - An empty window is recorded as a failure and retried (20 min, 40 min, then daily) instead of being marked done. - `sync_status.meta` now records extracted/accepted counts, rejection reasons and source domains for diagnosis. - The three empty windows are reset in production. No legal change. lint 0 errors, typecheck, tests, build pass.','2026-11-14T20:31:36Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/131'),
(132,'Season backfill: 7-day windows, better queries, JSON retry','First live run of the season backfill (after #131) found no verified results: PSL extracted 18 matches that were all outside the date range, EPL extracted none, La Liga returned invalid JSON. - 7-day windows (was 21), so a search lands on the right dates. - Queries carry exact dates, month names, a weekend round-up phrasing and up to four known club names. - One retry on invalid JSON with the three best sources, shortened. - A window that fails six times in a row is left alone. - Migration: cron sync-season runs 04:00-05:50 UTC (3 windows a call, about 36 a night). - Tests for queries, windows, retry and give-up.','2026-11-15T00:29:26Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/132'),
(133,'feat(home): Marquee Matchup card','Replaces the static Soweto Derby card on the home page with a multi-sport **Marquee Matchup** card. - **6 rivalries:** Soweto Derby, Boks vs All Blacks, El Clásico, Stormers vs Bulls, Celtics vs Lakers, Proteas vs Australia. Data in `src/lib/marquee-matchups.ts`, copy in `home.matchups.*` (en-ZA + af). - **Switching:** rivalry tabs, plus an 8 s auto-rotation with a progress bar. It pauses on hover, focus or the pause button, stops for good on touch, tab or pick, and never runs with prefers-reduced-motion. - **Hydration:** SSR and the first client render always show the Soweto Derby. Rotation and reduced-motion handling start after mount. - **Motion:** brand-green top sheen, floodlight beams, pulsing VS ring, crest hover lift, radial confidence dial (fills when in view and on each switch), spring split bars (`stiffness 120, damping 14`), tap-down `scale 0.98` with a check glow. - **Roadmap honesty:** football shows "Illustrative preview". Rugby, basketball and cricket show "Roadmap · week N" from `SPORT_ROADMAP`, so the card doesn''t claim coverage we don''t have yet. - **Founding hook:** guest taps open "Great call on the {rivalry}! 🏆 / You backed {team}…". The CTA carries the pick to `/founding` in router history state, and `/founding` shows a confirmation line after mount.','2026-11-15T00:35:58Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/133'),
(134,'feat(parallel): data layer foundation, USD budgets, response cache','Foundation for the owner''s 15 Nov direction: Parallel powers the data and AI features, with credits spent as sparingly as possible. Odds: **pre-match reference odds** (no in-play), alongside the odds members enter on their picks; neither overrides the other (owner, 15 Nov). - **Plan:** `docs/PARALLEL_ARCHITECTURE.md` maps each feature to the cheapest Parallel API (Search fast, Extract, Task lite, Chat low, Monitor lite), with cache lifetimes, odds rules, a steady-state budget (about $0.20 a day) and the one-off jobs to fund before the ~$50 prepaid balance expires on 7 Dec. Prices were checked against docs.parallel.ai on 15 Nov. - **Code (`src/lib/parallel/`):** - prices and provider keys - normalised SHA-256 cache keys - `cachedCall` / `withSearchCache` read-through cache: a store failure never blocks a call, and empty answers are never cached - Task API client (`POST /v1/tasks/runs`, `GET …/result`) and Responses client (`POST /v1/responses`) - 12 tests - **Budget guard:** `createQuotaClaim()` checks the family''s monthly USD budget first (`api_budget_claim`), then the existing call caps. Until the migration is applied it falls back to the call caps alone, so deploying this first changes nothing. - **Migration `20261115010000_parallel_data_layer.sql` (APPLIED 15 Nov at the owner''s approval), plus `20261115020000_parallel_budget_dec.sql` (APPLIED: budget drops to US$5 at 00:05 SAST on 7 Dec):** - `parallel_cache`, service role only - `api_unit_prices` and `api_budgets`, admin read','2026-11-15T01:10:28Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/134'),
(135,'feat(odds): pre-match reference odds and the member-odds check','Pre-match reference odds plus the "odds unverified" check on member-entered odds. The owner confirmed the rules on 15 Nov: a 25% threshold, the "odds unverified" label, and the lower price for rankings.','2026-11-15T01:28:26Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/135'),
(136,'fix(odds): live page reads only, Hollywoodbets profit odds, tolerant parsing','Hardens the odds feed (#135) after a live Parallel probe of this weekend''s Premier League pages. The first scheduled run that will find fixtures is Wed 18 Nov, 14:00 SAST.','2026-11-15T01:36:39Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/136'),
(137,'Dark-mode logo wall, @puntr.co.za auto-admin, admin side notch','- **Logo wall (dark mode):** bookmaker logos were opaque PNGs on white, so the dark-mode invert filter made solid white blocks. They are now transparent, trimmed PNGs (interior whites are real cut-outs). Dark mode shows clean white silhouettes that brighten on hover; light mode is unchanged (greyscale to colour on hover). Vectorising was not needed and would have risked distorting partner marks. - **Staff admin:** accounts with a **confirmed** `@puntr.co.za` email become admins automatically (migration `20261115043000_staff_auto_admin.sql`, already applied to production and tested in a rolled-back transaction: unconfirmed stays user, confirmation promotes, `evil.puntr.co.za` and `puntr.co.za.evil.com` stay user, client-session signup with a confirmed staff email gets admin). Banned/MFA rules still apply via `is_admin()`. No automatic demotion. Each grant is logged in `admin_actions`. - **Admin notch:** slim dismissible tab on the middle right edge, admin-only, opens `/admin`, hidden inside the portal, snoozed 7 days on dismiss. Reduced motion respected. en-ZA and af strings added.','2026-11-15T02:31:08Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/137'),
(138,'Season archive import: whole seasons from FBref + Wikipedia, stored only when both agree','## Why The search-based season backfill found 8 results in two nights: search returns pages for the wrong dates (`outside_date_range`) and excerpts rarely hold full scorelines. 2,500 verified results is a launch blocker. - `src/lib/pfie/archive.ts`: deterministic parsers (no model) for FBref''s "Scores & Fixtures" table and the Wikipedia season article''s home/away results matrix (columns mapped to rows by club link, so abbreviations are never guessed). A result is stored only when both pages give the same score for the same home/away pair; date from FBref; sources `fbref.com` + `wikipedia.org`. - Current season: the Wikipedia league table replaces the stored table only when every row matches the verified results exactly (P/W/D/L/GF/GA and Pts = 3W+D). - `archive-run.ts` + `job=archive` on `/api/cron/sync-tables`: one job = one league season = two Parallel Extract reads (~US$0.002). Finished seasons import once; the current season refreshes daily. Parallel only (keeps Firecrawl''s free tier for live pages). - Leagues: PSL, EPL, La Liga, Serie A, Bundesliga, Ligue 1, Eredivisie, Liga Portugal, Championship, Saudi Pro; seasons 2024/25, 2025/26, 2026/27. - The search-based season backfill now skips these leagues (saves search spend). - Migration `20261115060000_season_archive_import.sql`: `sync_status` accepts `archive`; cron `sync-archive` 02:10-02:55 SAST, 3 jobs a call. - 10 new tests (parsers built from real Parallel Extract output); season tests moved to the Motsepe Championship.','2026-11-15T06:27:09Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/138'),
(139,'Kick-off time zones: inferred national/home-zone times, verified only by a second site','## Why The largest fixture loss (~95 a run) is "no kick-off time with a known time zone": La Liga, Serie A, Eredivisie, UCL, Championship and Saudi pages print times without a zone. 120+ fixtures in 14 days is a launch blocker (44 today). - **Inferred zones** (`time.ts`): national outlets (.es, .it, .de, .fr, .nl, .pt, .sa, .co.uk, plus marca/as/mundodeportivo/lequipe/efl etc.) and the official site read in the league''s home zone (`HOME_ZONES` in `provider.ts`) yield an instant marked `kickoffInferred`. - **Corroboration** (`corroborate.ts`): an inferred instant never decides alone, not even for the official site. Verified when two different sites infer the same instant, when a zone-less page''s candidates confirm it, or when it confirms a time another site printed with a zone. Disagreeing inferred instants = disputed; an inferred contradiction also blocks the trusted single-outlet rule. Printed zones still decide first, unchanged. - Zone-less candidates now include the league''s home zone (e.g. Riyadh). - Fixture searches add national-press and SA phrasings per league (same Parallel call, capped at 5 phrasings): no extra spend. - Labels WET/WEST/KSA. 8 new tests (60 in `src/lib/pfie`).','2026-11-15T06:31:05Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/139'),
(140,'Account: remove duplicate Language label; regroup the profile menu','1. **Duplicate "Language" on /account** (owner screenshot): `LanguageSwitcher` takes `hideLabel`; on the account row the visible label comes from the row and the switcher''s own label is screen-reader only (the select keeps its accessible name). 2. **Profile drop-down rearranged and optimised** (`site-header.tsx`): - Header: avatar, username, Founding Member number. - PuntPoints balance pill (opens Wallet) when PuntPoints are on. - **My activity:** My record, My betting slips, My duels, Practice Mode (Founding Members). - **Wallet and rewards:** Wallet, PuntPoints and rewards, Copy invite link, Share on WhatsApp. - **Settings:** Account, Security (new shortcut), Privacy and data, Admin dashboard (admins only). - Sign out, styled as destructive. - Every row has an icon (`MenuItem` helper), wider menu (w-64) for scanning. - New `nav.json` keys in en-ZA and Afrikaans drafts (Afrikaans still preview-only).','2026-11-15T06:28:01Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/140'),
(141,'Footer regroup, /community -> /forum (Community Forum), /standings -> /tables','**Footer (item 6)** - Platform: Fixtures (`/fixtures`, was "Predictions"), Results, **Tables** (`/tables`, new), Insights, Roadmap, Pricing. - Community: **Sports Discussions** (`/forum`, was "Community feed"), **Head-to-Head Duels** (`/duels`, new), **Leaderboards** (moved here from Platform), How it works, PuntPoints (now `/puntpoints`; it pointed at `/leaderboards`), Support. **/community -> /forum (item 7)** - `src/routes/community.tsx` renamed to `forum.tsx` (route, canonical URL, JSON-LD URL). Page title now **"Community Forum"** (meta title too); Afrikaans draft "Gemeenskapsforum". - `/community` 301-redirects to `/forum`, so shared links and search results keep working. - Header, mobile dock flyout and sitemap point at `/forum`. **/standings -> /tables** (so the footer''s `/tables` is the real page, not a second URL for the same content) - `standings.tsx` renamed to `tables.tsx`; `/standings?league=...` 301-redirects to `/tables?league=...`. Side nav and sitemap updated.','2026-11-15T06:28:11Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/141'),
(142,'Predictions hub: fixtures, results, tables, duels, leaderboards + Betting Slip Converter spotlight','**Stacked on #141** (uses the new `/tables` route). Merge #141 first; this PR then shows only its own changes. **Predictions as the consolidated landing page (item 3)** - Hub tile row: Fixtures (live count), Results, Tables, Duels, Leaderboards, each with its own hover motion. - **Next fixtures:** the first 6 match cards (league chips kept), "All fixtures (N)" and "See N more fixtures" link to `/fixtures`, so the two pages no longer duplicate the full list. - Preview grid: **Latest results** (last 6 from `completed_matches`, fixtures + verified season results), **League tables** (top 5, league tabs), **Head-to-head duels** (open challenges), **This week''s leaders** (top 5). Each links to its full page. - New `src/lib/hub-data.ts` (public reads only), `src/components/predictions/hub.tsx`. **Betting Slip Converter spotlight (item 8)**, above the match cards - `src/components/predictions/slip-converter-promo.tsx`: copy, three input modes, "Convert a slip" (`/slips`) and "About the toolkit" (`/tools`). - Unique motion graphic: a slip being scanned while its legs drop out as 1X2/BTTS/O-U pick chips; static under reduced motion. - Privacy line matches what `/slips` does (on-device reading, personal details scrubbed before saving). Copy in en-ZA plus Afrikaans drafts (preview-only). No profit wording.','2026-11-15T06:30:11Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/142'),
(143,'Fixtures: SEO-friendly numbered pagination (10 per page)','## Choice: numbered pagination (not infinite scroll) Infinite scroll / "View more" hides fixtures behind JavaScript and gives search engines one URL. Numbered pages give each slice its own crawlable URL, which matters because fixture pages carry `SportsEvent` structured data. So: **10 fixtures per page** (inside the 5-10 brief), `?page=N`. - `src/lib/pagination.ts`: `paginate()` (clamps out-of-range pages) and `pageWindow()` (1 … 4 5 6 … 9), with tests. - `/fixtures`: grouping (day/competition), cards/list views and team forms work on the current page only (lighter page, fewer form reads). - Pager: real `<Link>`s that keep the other filters, `aria-current`, `rel="prev"`/`"next"`, "Showing 11-20 of 44 fixtures". Any filter change resets to page 1. - `<head>`: self-referencing canonical per page (`/fixtures`, `/fixtures?page=2`, ...), `<link rel="prev/next">`, page number in the title from page 2, and the JSON-LD `ItemList` lists that page''s events with continuous positions. - en-ZA keys plus Afrikaans drafts.','2026-11-15T06:30:23Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/143'),
(144,'Results: redesigned season board with team search, matchday groups and outcome split','- **Season board** (`src/components/results/season-board.tsx`), replacing the flat list: - headline counters (verified results, competitions) with count-up motion; - **team search** (server-side `ilike` on home/away, input sanitised so no PostgREST filter syntax gets through) plus the competition chips; - results **grouped by matchday date, then competition**, scoreboard rows with winner-highlighted score tiles; - "Verified by N sources" badge on every score (sources still named, full list on hover); - sticky side panel: **how these matches ended** (home/draw/away split bar animated in, goals per game), computed in code from the scores on screen (`src/lib/results-stats.ts`, tested), with the "past results do not predict future results" note. - The **illustrative example cards** now show only while no real result exists anywhere (recent or season); they were still showing beside real data. - Recent Puntr matchdays keep the crowd/top-tipster cards under a clearer heading. - en-ZA copy plus Afrikaans drafts.','2026-11-15T06:30:36Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/144'),
(145,'Archive import: parse full-page Wikipedia tables (separator rows, wrapped rows) + diagnostics','## Why First production run of the archive import (#138): EPL, PSL and La Liga 2026/27 all failed with "no results matrix on the wikipedia page", although the matrix is on each page. The full-page markdown from Parallel differs from the excerpt format the parsers were built on. - `tableLines()`: rebuilds table rows that wrap (a long link title on the next line, also across a blank line) and drops markdown separator rows (`| --- |`). Used by the matrix, league-table and FBref parsers. - "Home \ Away" header matched with any number of escaping backslashes. - When the matrix is still not found, the job records diagnostics in `sync_status.meta` (page length, table-line count, a 600-character snippet around the results header) so the next fix is exact. - New test with the real mid-season shape (separator row, empty cells, wrapped "a" rivalry link).','2026-11-15T06:39:38Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/145'),
(146,'Kick-off times: inferred pages confirm via their plausible instants too (fix #139 regression)','## Why Forced fixture sync after #139 (15 Nov, 08:48 SAST): fixtures in 14 days 44 -> 56, but La Liga still 0. The decisions show a regression from #139: laliga.com (zone-less, official) now gets an *inferred* Madrid instant, and an inferred page could only confirm a printed time if that one instant matched. Before #139 the same page kept all its plausible instants (UTC, UK, CET, SAST) and could confirm in any of them. If laliga.com renders in UTC, it can no longer confirm the SAST time printed by ebnewsdaily.co.za ("Athletic v Espanyol": laliga.com + ebnewsdaily.co.za -> single_source). - `corroborate.ts`: an inferred observation confirms a printed time when its inferred instant OR any of its plausible instants matches (restores the pre-#139 behaviour; inferred still never decides alone). - `teams.ts`: alias `depor` -> `deportivo` (laliga.com writes "Dépor", others "Deportivo", which split one match into two clusters). - Test: laliga.com read in UTC still confirms a SAST time.','2026-11-15T07:39:44Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/146'),
(147,'Bundesliga fixtures: read the official page that prints CET and UTC','Adds products.bundesliga.com/fixtures (official; prints kick-off in CET and UTC) to the Bundesliga fixture pages so more matches carry a verified time zone. SuperSport tournament pages were tested and are JS-only (return a loading spinner), so they were not added. LaLiga, UCL, Eredivisie and Motsepe need a different route (see mvp.md). Legal copy: nothing changed (same data, same sources).','2026-11-15T08:44:46Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/147'),
(148,'Archive: tolerant league-table reader and diagnostics','Every current-season archive run reported ''no table on the page'' although the same Wikipedia markdown parses locally. Likely causes handled: a ''Team vte'' header and rows with dropped empty trailing cells. Tests added. Also records, when a table or club names fail, a snippet of what the reader returned and up to 12 unmatched FBref club names, so the next run shows exactly what to fix (Eredivisie 27, La Liga 11, Serie A 10 unmatched this season). Legal copy: nothing changed.','2026-11-15T08:47:04Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/148'),
(149,'Archive: match club names Wikipedia spells differently','From the first run with the new diagnostics: Athletic Club (La Liga), PSV, NEC Nijmegen, AZ Alkmaar, Sparta R. (Eredivisie) did not resolve to the Wikipedia matrix names. Archive-only name map (shared aliases untouched, since they build badge file names and fixture keys). Test added. Not fixed here: Bundesliga (Freiburg), Championship (Birmingham), Liga Portugal (Porto), Saudi (Al-Qadsiah) tables fail on a stats mismatch, and Ligue 1 on 18 vs 17 teams; likely FBref/Wikipedia cut-off timing or a team with no matched results, to inspect after this run. Legal copy: nothing changed.','2026-11-16T06:55:51Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/149'),
(150,'feat: add private Founding HQ acquisition dashboard','- Adds a private, admin-only `/admin/founding-hq` campaign command centre. - Tracks prospects, X handles, audience size, segment, source, outreach stage, last contact, follow-up date, registration status and ambassador pipeline. - Adds prospect activity notes and audit logging. - Shows the live count of profiles with an assigned founding number against the 100-member target. - Adds admin-only Supabase tables with RLS and a link from the existing admin dashboard. - Marks the page noindex/nofollow; no public navigation exposure.','2026-11-21T19:06:14Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/150'),
(151,'Refresh admin navigation and institutional outreach','- Reorganises the admin workspace into four clear navigation groups: Overview, Community, Growth & partnerships, and Platform. - Adds a responsive mobile section selector and a desktop vertical navigation rail. - Updates institutional email drafting instructions so requests are tailored to each organisation''s mandate; regulators are approached for guidance rather than generic endorsement, advertising authorisation or logo permission. - Updates the admin copy to explain the purpose and guardrails of the Endorsements workspace. - Adds a regression test for mandate-aware outreach prompts.','2026-11-21T21:35:07Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/151'),
(152,'Fix signup alerts, identity rewards and member administration','- Identify Gravitas Industries (Pty) Ltd (CK No.: 2024/596436/07) as the operator of Puntr South Africa across the English and Afrikaans Terms, Privacy, Cookies, Affiliate Disclosure and Refunds pages; correct the copyright footer and legal changelog. - Queue one idempotent internal signup alert to support@puntr.co.za for each new Supabase Auth account. Alerts go through the existing email outbox/Resend path; registration is not blocked if queuing fails. - Expand Admin > Users with account, authentication, profile/contact, identity, preference, points, activity and referral details. - Fix the identity quest status mismatch (approved vs verified), award the 100-point quest on new approvals, and backfill existing approved checks through the same idempotent quest-award function. - Reprice all 16 launch rewards fivefold ahead of the first redemption. - Add Tables immediately after Results in the mobile Predictions flyout.','2026-11-21T22:27:26Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/152'),
(153,'Correct remaining Terms operator references','- Correct the final two legal references that still named Puntr as a separate company in the limitation-of-liability clause. - English and Afrikaans Terms now identify Gravitas Industries (Pty) Ltd (CK No.: 2024/596436/07) and use Terms version r23. - Record Terms r23 in the production notice_versions table.','2026-11-21T22:28:56Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/153'),
(154,'Resolve missing multi-sport team badges and streamline admin access','### Team badges and hero marquee - Initial production audit: 271 verified soccer badges and 24 unresolved/failed soccer teams. - Ran the existing Parallel resolver once against the current fixture backlog. It found and verified Al Fayha; it also surfaced a false positive for Iberia Tbilisi (Dinamo Tbilisi''s badge). I immediately reset Iberia Tbilisi to failed/unbadged rather than leave the wrong logo live. - Current production snapshot: 272 verified, 23 failed. The 12-team multi-sport hero roster has 3 badges already present (Orlando Pirates, Kaizer Chiefs and FC Barcelona); 9 additional sport/team pairs are not registered yet (including Australia football, LA Lakers, Vodacom Bulls and DHL Stormers). That leaves 32 candidates for the updated resolver. - Expanded the hero marquee to render a curated cross-sport roster through the shared `TeamLogo` component rather than filtering the registry to soccer-only entries. - Added the marquee roster to the same Parallel Search resolver and admin review list. Search requests distinguish national football teams, rugby union teams and professional basketball teams. - Tightened candidate matching to require the primary team-name term, preventing weak shared-location matches such as Iberia Tbilisi → Dinamo Tbilisi. - Raised retry allowance from 3 to 6 and changed the admin action to process up to 40 candidates in small concurrent batches, still using the existing Parallel quota claim and Supabase Storage mirroring. - Manual image URL entry is now shown only for unresolved/rejected results. Admins should use it only when Parallel cannot source a correct badge.','2026-11-21T23:13:09Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/154'),
(155,'Prioritize hero marquee team badges during Parallel resolution','- Prioritize the 12 curated hero marquee teams ahead of the wider fixture badge backlog in each Parallel badge run. - Prevents a large fixture backlog from starving launch-critical home-page logos across repeated batches. - Existing Parallel search, Wikipedia article/image validation, Supabase Storage mirroring, quota claims and manual fallback behavior remain unchanged.','2026-11-21T23:30:38Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/155'),
(156,'Rebuild PFIE league standings around live multi-source verification','This is an urgent PFIE reliability fix for stale and missing league tables. ### Root cause The season archive importer was writing the current league table directly from Wikipedia after reconciling FBref match results. The daily live standings job also allowed a single official source to bypass corroboration and compared only team, played and points across sources. This allowed stale tables to remain publishable and did not provide enough validation for the full standings record. ### Changes - Removed current-table writes from the Wikipedia/FBref archive importer. It remains available for historical match-result reconciliation only. - Current tables now use Parallel Search for discovery and Parallel Extract for fresh full-page reads (15-minute maximum cache age; stale-cache fallback disabled). - Search discovers up to 20 candidate pages; the pipeline extracts up to four independent official/trusted publisher pages per competition refresh. - Search snippets, Wikipedia, historical pages and unextractable pages cannot count as current-table evidence. - A current table is published only when at least two independent publishers agree on every team''s played, W/D/L, goals for, goals against and points. Official status ranks a source higher but never bypasses corroboration. - Added explicit date validation when a source prints a table update date; dated tables older than 72 hours are rejected. - Added anti-regression validation against the previous verified in-season table so played matches and cumulative W/D/L/GF/GA/points cannot move backwards.','2026-11-21T23:34:37Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/156'),
(157,'Fix PFIE live standings source collector initialization','## Hotfix - Restore the `sources` array declaration in `gatherSources()` before collecting freshly extracted Parallel pages. - The PFIE v1 multi-source release returned `sources is not defined` for standings runs; this prevented the manual refresh from completing but did not overwrite existing tables. - No behavior change beyond restoring the intended source collector.','2026-11-21T23:37:03Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/157'),
(158,'Harden PFIE standings extraction and source-row verification','Follow-up reliability hardening after the first production refresh exposed extraction-level quote mismatches and a misread PSL row. - Extract each official/trusted standings page in its own Gemini request. This prevents the model from blending table rows across sources or assigning rows to the wrong source index. - Pin each response to the exact source ID supplied in that request. - Keep arithmetic, team-count, positions, table-date and anti-regression checks unchanged. - Improve evidence validation: accept either an exact normalized row quote or the complete ordered P/W/D/L/GF/GA/points numeric sequence on the same source row. This handles formatting/quote normalization differences without relaxing the actual data checks. - Add regression tests for row-stat evidence and for rejecting quotes whose numeric row data does not match the page. - Update PFIE documentation. This increases Gemini usage to at most four small source-specific extraction calls per competition refresh. At the configured schedule this is about 68 calls/day, within the configured Gemini Flash-Lite allowance.','2026-11-21T23:41:29Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/158'),
(160,'Fix PFIE standings row evidence false rejections','## Problem Live PFIE runs are finding fresh full-page publisher sources but rejecting otherwise usable tables because the model''s copied row quote and table-date quote do not exactly match the extracted publisher text. This is too brittle for different table layouts and has left the Premier League table stale and Bundesliga without a baseline. - Validate each team''s seven core numeric statistics in order within the extracted page text near the team''s name. - Keep source-isolated Gemini extraction and the requirement for at least two independent publishers to agree on the complete table. - If a source supplies an explicit table date, require that date to appear on the page in ISO or common human-readable formats, then enforce the 72-hour age window. - Retain arithmetic, team-count, position, team-name, independent-publisher, full-table agreement and anti-regression checks. - Add tests for unsupported row statistics and human-readable table dates.','2026-11-21T23:43:06Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/160'),
(161,'Keep PFIE tables when publisher dates cannot be verified','## Problem The Bundesliga live refresh is returning complete source-backed rows but rejecting the entire source because Gemini supplied a table date that is not printed in the extracted page. This is unverified metadata, not evidence that the table rows themselves are stale. - Persist a reported table date only when that exact date can be verified on the publisher page. - Ignore an unverified model-supplied date rather than rejecting a complete, locally evidenced table. - Continue rejecting dates that are visibly printed but older than 72 hours or in the future. - Preserve the full-row numeric evidence, arithmetic, team-count, position, independent-publisher consensus and anti-regression gates. - Add regression coverage. A table without a printed date is still fetched from a fresh Parallel Extract page (15-minute max cache age), and must agree with a second independent publisher before publishing.','2026-11-21T23:45:08Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/161'),
(162,'Improve PFIE standings source coverage and targeted retries','Follow-up operational hardening for the new PFIE live standings pipeline. - Expand the trusted source discovery registry with additional established football data publishers, including FBref, WorldFootball.net, Transfermarkt, Flashscore, Soccerway, Kicker and OneFootball. - Extract each source page independently using its own Gemini request, so the model cannot blend rows across publishers. - If a source fails deterministic validation, retry that page once with the exact rejection reason (for example, an incorrect W/D/L sum or row-evidence mismatch). A failed source cannot poison the other sources. - Keep a table publishable only when at least two independent publishers agree on the complete W/D/L/GF/GA/points record. - Only enforce an extracted table date when the date or its quote can be verified on the source page; otherwise ignore the model-generated date and rely on the fresh Parallel fetch plus cross-source and anti-regression checks. - Persist source URLs/domains, model names and per-source rejection reasons in sync metadata for future diagnosis. - Add tests for source-specific retry guidance and the updated date/row-evidence validation. At the current cadence this is approximately 68 Parallel Extract calls/day and at most 136 Gemini Flash-Lite extraction calls/day, within the configured daily quotas.','2026-11-21T23:52:36Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/162'),
(163,'Add Bundesliga and DFB official pages to PFIE source discovery','- Add direct full-page candidates for the official Bundesliga table and the DFB data centre. - Classify the DFB domain as a trusted independent publisher. - Feed configured pages through the same Parallel Extract path as Parallel Search results, with fresh-page requirements and publisher deduplication. - Keep the minimum two-independent-publisher consensus, complete 18-team row validation, and anti-regression checks. - Add configuration coverage and update PFIE documentation.','2026-11-21T23:48:07Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/163'),
(164,'Align PFIE table-date checks with SAST calendar boundaries','## Problem The DFB table is now being extracted as a second source, but its published 22 November date is being treated as future while the server clock is still 21 November UTC. South Africa has already rolled over to 22 November. - Compare printed table dates against SAST (+02:00) day boundaries. - Preserve the 72-hour stale-date rejection and future-date rejection. - Add tests for UTC/SAST midnight crossover and genuinely future dates. This is a timezone correction only; it does not relax source corroboration or row validation.','2026-11-21T23:49:57Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/164'),
(165,'Deduplicate PFIE source mirrors by publisher','- Treat subdomains of DFB and Bundesliga as the same publisher during source discovery and consensus checks. - Prevents `datencenter.dfb.de` and another DFB host, or `products.bundesliga.com` and `bundesliga.com`, from being counted as independent corroboration. - Retains BBC multi-domain normalization and adds tests for the new publisher mappings.','2026-11-21T23:53:55Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/165'),
(166,'Expand direct source coverage for priority league tables','- Add direct full-page Parallel Extract candidates for PSL, La Liga and Serie A. - PSL: Laduma Analytics and 45min (both complete 16-team tables). - La Liga: official LaLiga standings and Sky Sports full table. - Serie A: official Lega Serie A standings and Sky Sports full table. - Mark Laduma Analytics and 45min as trusted publishers. - Keep source-isolated extraction, independent publisher deduplication, two-source complete-table consensus, local numeric row evidence, SAST date validation and anti-regression.','2026-11-21T23:53:47Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/166'),
(167,'Run PFIE standings as single-competition cron requests','- Record the production cron schedule change in a Supabase migration. - Each request now processes one due competition, avoiding the 55-second HTTP timeout seen when three competitions were refreshed serially. - Expand both daily windows to 12 ten-minute slots (04:00-05:50 and 16:00-17:50 SAST). - Priority tables still refresh twice daily; other configured tables refresh daily. - Update route and operations documentation.','2026-11-21T23:57:03Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/167'),
(168,'Keep PFIE multi-source standings sync within cron timeout','The first production runs showed that one request processing three competitions could exceed pg_net''s 55-second HTTP timeout, especially when each source needed a targeted Gemini retry. - Run the up to four initial source-specific Gemini extractions concurrently. - Retry only rejected sources in a second concurrent wave, rather than sequentially retrying all pages. - Keep each scheduled request to one competition. - Reschedule morning general sync every five minutes (04:00–05:55 SAST) and priority standings every ten minutes in the evening window (16:00–17:50 SAST). - Keep the two daily windows, with priority tables refreshed every 12 hours and other tables every 24 hours. - Add migration `20261122140000_pfie_standings_timeout_batches.sql` to update the production cron schedule. This retains up to four independent Parallel page extracts and a maximum of eight source-specific Gemini calls per competition while keeping the HTTP request bounded.','2026-11-21T23:58:22Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/168'),
(169,'Make PFIE standings row validation accent and layout tolerant','## Problem The La Liga source refresh still rejects a valid row because the publisher uses Atlético de Madrid while the extraction model returns ATM Atlético de Madrid. The existing fallback only checks three source lines and is not accent-insensitive, so a valid row can be rejected even when its seven statistics are present. - Normalize diacritics for source text, quotes and team-name matching. - Match both full team names and common three-letter-code-prefixed names. - Expand local row evidence context to ten lines and add a bounded row-major text fallback. - Continue requiring all seven statistics in order beside a matching team name, plus arithmetic, positions, full team count, independent-source consensus and anti-regression. - Add regression coverage for the ATM Atlético de Madrid versus Atletico de Madrid source-text variation. This does not relax the two-independent-publisher rule.','2026-11-21T23:59:42Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/169'),
(170,'Support points-first standings tables in PFIE validation','## Problem LaLiga''s official table orders columns as PTS, Pld, W, D, L, GF, GA, while Sky Sports and most other tables use P, W, D, L, GF, GA, Pts. The validator only recognized the second layout, so the official LaLiga source was rejected even though its team and seven statistics were present. - Accept both common numeric row orders: played-first and points-first. - Preserve accent-insensitive team matching and local row evidence requirements. - Keep all arithmetic, complete team-count, independent-publisher consensus, freshness and anti-regression checks. - Add a regression test using the actual LaLiga points-first layout. This is a parser-compatibility fix, not a reduction in verification requirements.','2026-11-22T00:01:24Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/170'),
(171,'Prefer overall standings tables over home and away views','## Problem The official LaLiga page exposes Total, Home and Away standings views. The extraction prompt did not explicitly tell the model to use the overall table, so it could select a home/away table and disagree with the full-table source. - Explicitly instruct source-specific extraction to use only the Total/Overall table when multiple views are present. - Continue rejecting partial, home-only, away-only, group and form tables. - Add prompt regression coverage. The two-source consensus and complete-table validation remain unchanged.','2026-11-22T00:03:03Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/171'),
(172,'Resolve team aliases before validating PFIE table row evidence','- Resolve each extracted team name against the competition''s known team registry before source-row evidence validation. - Validate row quotes/numeric evidence against the source spelling and the resolved canonical team name, including common abbreviations and suffix/wording differences (e.g. Atlético de Madrid vs Atletico Madrid). - Preserve strict W/D/L arithmetic, points, source consensus, team count and anti-regression checks. - Add a regression test for the La Liga name variation that caused the latest update to be rejected.','2026-11-22T00:05:10Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/172'),
(174,'Retry independent standings sources when complete tables disagree','## Problem La Liga''s official page and Sky Sports are both being extracted through Parallel, but the two locally valid tables still fail consensus. A source can pass local checks and still misread a row or select a non-overall view. The pipeline currently stops without a second source-local correction attempt. - When two or more individually valid tables disagree, compute a hint listing only the affected teams and columns (never the other publisher''s values). - Re-extract each source independently once with that hint, then re-run complete validation and two-publisher consensus. - Keep retries within the existing one-retry-per-source budget and quota guards. - Require all seven numeric statistics to be evidenced beside the team even when a copied quote is present, so an exact quote cannot mask incorrect extracted values. - Add regression tests for mismatch hints and strict numeric row evidence. This improves correction without relaxing source independence or consensus.','2026-11-22T00:07:22Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/174'),
(175,'Strip team codes before PFIE team alias matching','- Strip source-side three/four-letter club codes (e.g. `ATM`) before resolving the extracted team name against the competition''s canonical team registry. - Keep the original, stripped and resolved names as source-evidence variants. - Add ESPN and Transfermarkt as independent direct La Liga table sources alongside LaLiga.com and Sky Sports, so one source''s row-format mismatch cannot leave the competition without two-source consensus. - Add regression tests for `ATM Atlético de Madrid` vs `Atletico Madrid` and for the expanded La Liga source set. This addresses the remaining La Liga source-row rejection without weakening W/D/L, points, numeric-row, source-consensus or anti-regression validation.','2026-11-22T00:08:41Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/175'),
(176,'Expand PFIE standings sources and handle official UEFA tie ranks','Follow-up to PFIE PR #156 after the first production refresh identified specific source and validation gaps. ### Coverage - Add directly extractable full-table pages for Ligue 1, Eredivisie, Liga Portugal, the Motsepe Foundation Championship and UEFA Champions League. - Expand trusted publisher discovery to include VI, Ziggo, Sports Mole, Stat-Football, Rotascore, Treble, NasiScore, TNT Sports, CBS Sports and FOX Sports. - Increase bounded Parallel Extract candidates from four to five independent publishers per competition. The configured 12-league cadence is approximately 85 extracts/day (2,550/month), within the stated 3,000/month cap before other extraction workloads. ### Validation - Support UEFA''s published competition-ranking ties (for example, 29th place shared by two clubs, followed by 31st) without relaxing sequential rank checks for domestic league tables. - Collapse only exact duplicate club rows repeated by responsive page layouts; conflicting duplicate records remain rejected. - Strengthen the extraction prompt to prevent mixing summary, home, away, form or separate competition tables. ### Operations - Keep cron at one competition per HTTP request. Five extracts plus up to ten bounded Gemini calls can approach the 55-second pg_net timeout; batch size three is unsafe. - Add a follow-up cron migration that sets the verified five-minute schedule windows (04:10-05:55 and 16:10-17:55 SAST) with `max=1`. - Update PFIE runbook and blueprint.','2026-11-22T00:10:34Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/176'),
(178,'Accept points-first standings evidence in PFIE','The official LaLiga table presents numeric columns as PTS, Pld, W, D, L, GF, GA. PFIE''s current local row-evidence validator still checks only the played-first order. This update makes the live validator accept both common layouts while retaining the requirement that all seven values appear together beside the team.','2026-11-22T00:09:38Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/178'),
(179,'Restore PFIE source-local consensus retries on current main','## Problem The current production branch has points-first validation and expanded LaLiga sources, but the live standings runner still stops when two individually valid sources disagree. The earlier retry change was not present in the final merged base after subsequent branch merges. - Reapply source-local consensus retry to the current mainline: when complete tables disagree, send each source its own mismatch hint and re-extract once independently. - The hint names only teams and columns, never another publisher''s values. - Require all seven statistics to appear beside the team even if a copied quote matches. - Include source domains and mismatch fields in the final failure diagnostic. - Preserve source-isolated extraction, two-publisher consensus, freshness and anti-regression. - Add regression tests.','2026-11-22T00:12:26Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/179'),
(181,'Normalize LaLiga team aliases across PFIE sources','Closed as superseded by a refreshed branch based on the latest mainline PFIE source configuration. The La Liga source additions are being carried forward without losing newer Bundesliga source updates.','2026-11-22T00:14:27Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/181'),
(182,'Replace stale PFIE league table pages with current publisher feeds','Live PFIE diagnostics showed that some configured publisher pages were stale or repeatedly returned duplicate rows, preventing a verified table from being published. ### Source roster corrections - Ligue 1: replace Goal/Stat-Football candidates with current TNT Sports, CBS Sports and NinetyMinutesPlus full-table feeds, alongside the official Ligue 1 page and Sports Mole. - Eredivisie: remove the Ziggo page that explicitly reported a 9 November update (older than the 72-hour acceptance window). Add current Statz, Sportmetrics, Tribuna and Flashscore feeds alongside VI. - Expand the trusted-source registry for these established statistical publishers. ### Verification policy remains strict - Search discovers candidates; Parallel Extract fetches the complete page fresh. - A table still requires two independent publishers agreeing on every club''s P/W/D/L/GF/GA/points. - Dated pages older than 72 hours, incomplete tables, conflicting duplicate rows and single-source tables remain rejected. - No manual or web-scraped table values are inserted into the production standings store.','2026-11-22T00:14:54Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/182'),
(184,'Normalize Espanyol de Barcelona standings alias','The live LaLiga consensus diagnostic identifies a remaining publisher-name mismatch: one source labels the club Espanyol de Barcelona while another uses Espanyol. Add that alias to the canonical team map and cover it with a regression test. No standings values or consensus requirements are changed.','2026-11-22T00:15:56Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/184'),
(185,'Add more independent La Liga table publishers','- Bring the branch fully up to date with `main`; it is now 0 commits behind. - Keep La Liga source selection within the hard five-candidate cap. Four direct candidates are configured: LaLiga, Sky Sports, ESPN and Transfermarkt; search discovery can supply a fifth candidate. - Replace unsuitable candidates: Football Edge Lab exposes a projected table rather than the current standings, the Flashscore route did not expose a full standings table, and The Analyst page was stale against the current matchweek. - Preserve strict two-independent-publisher consensus, complete-team, row-quote, freshness, date, arithmetic and regression validation. - Correct team-resolution regressions for Paris shorthand, Paris FC, RC Deportivo and Racing Santander. - Fix archive alias keys for NEC Nijmegen and AZ Alkmaar, and align provider tests with the configured PFIE model order rather than stale hard-coded model names.','2026-11-22T04:07:28Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/185'),
(186,'Use stronger free Gemini models for PFIE table extraction','Live standings retries show that Flash-Lite can return incomplete or duplicate rows even when Parallel Extract provides a current full-table page. - Prioritize Gemini 3.8 Flash, 3.6 Flash and 3.5 Flash for PFIE row extraction and reconciliation. - Retain Gemini 3.5 Flash-Lite and 3.1 Flash-Lite as quota-aware fallbacks. - All models remain within the project''s explicit free-model allowlist; no paid model is introduced. - Add a regression test for model order and update the PFIE runbook. This changes only PFIE''s model preference, not the wider content engine defaults.','2026-11-22T00:17:06Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/186'),
(187,'Strip publisher team codes before PFIE team matching','LaLiga''s official publisher prepends short uppercase team codes to some names (for example, RAC R. Racing Club and ATM Atlético de Madrid), while independent publishers omit them. Those labels are semantically identical but were not canonicalized, preventing table consensus. This change strips an uppercase 2–4 character publisher code before the existing alias normalization and adds regression tests. It does not relax statistics validation or source consensus.','2026-11-22T00:17:50Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/187'),
(188,'Keep PFIE standings refreshes inside the cron request window','Production diagnostics showed live PFIE refresh requests exceeding the 55-second pg_net timeout even with one competition per request. - Reduce each live Parallel Extract page-read timeout from 45s to 25s. - Five independent source reads remain concurrent; a slow publisher is skipped while other source pages continue. - Keep archive extraction at 45s because archive pages are longer and stable. - Preserve five-source maximum, 15-minute cache age, no stale-cache fallback, source-local LLM retries and two-publisher consensus. - Document the bounded live extraction window. This is intended to prevent a slow source from timing out the entire standings refresh.','2026-11-22T00:19:37Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/188'),
(189,'Disable per-source retries in PFIE live table reads','The 25-second per-page timeout still allowed two client attempts (up to ~51 seconds) before Gemini validation began. That leaves too little time inside the 55-second pg_net request window. - Keep five independent Parallel Extract reads concurrent. - Set each live read to one 30-second attempt (attempts: 1), aligned with Parallel''s 30-second fetch policy. - A slow publisher is skipped; the other four sources can still provide independent corroboration. - Keep archive extraction''s longer retry policy unchanged. - Update the PFIE runbook. This is specifically for live standings (and the default mixed sync path); it avoids spending the full request window retrying one slow publisher.','2026-11-22T00:21:18Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/189'),
(190,'Normalize Dépor shorthand in LaLiga standings','The live LaLiga disagreement diagnostics show one source labels Deportivo La Coruña as “Dépor” while another uses the full club name. Map the shorthand to the same canonical team and add a regression test. The 72-hour stale-date rejection remains unchanged.','2026-11-22T00:22:27Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/190'),
(191,'Finalize single-attempt PFIE page-read budget','The previous 25-second page timeout still allowed two client attempts (up to ~51 seconds) before Gemini validation began. This finalizes the timeout fix: - Keep five independent Parallel Extract reads concurrent. - Set each live read to one 30-second attempt (attempts: 1), aligned with Parallel''s 30-second fetch policy. - A slow publisher is skipped; the remaining sources can still provide independent corroboration. - Keep archive extraction''s longer retry policy unchanged. - Expose the attempts field in the provider override type so TypeScript accepts the bounded retry setting. - Update the PFIE runbook. This is specifically for live standings (and the default mixed sync path); it avoids spending the full request window retrying one slow publisher.','2026-11-22T00:23:17Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/191'),
(192,'Resolve repeated overall, home and away standings rows safely','Ligue 1 source diagnostics show publishers returning the same club in overall, home and away table sections. Rejecting every repeated team is safe but prevents a complete current table from being validated. This change: - Collapses exact duplicate rows. - When repeated rows for a club have different cumulative totals, retains a row only if it component-wise dominates the others across played, W/D/L, GF, GA and points. This selects the overall table row over a home/away subset and can also prefer a later cumulative snapshot. - Rejects conflicting duplicates when neither row dominates (including points deductions or inconsistent data). - Keeps the full-table team-count, arithmetic, row-evidence, freshness, previous-snapshot anti-regression and two-independent-publisher checks unchanged. - Adds tests for exact duplicates, safe overall-vs-subset resolution and conflicting duplicate rejection. No source is accepted merely because it has the largest played count; every cumulative statistic must be at least as high.','2026-11-22T00:26:08Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/192'),
(193,'Add publisher-level PFIE table failure diagnostics','Repeated Ligue 1 and La Liga refreshes are failing safely, but the stored error only reports source indexes and duplicate team names. That is not enough to identify whether a publisher has a mixed overall/home/away table, a stale page or conflicting statistics. - Include each source''s domain alongside validation failures and consensus-retry failures. - Include the two cumulative stat vectors when a duplicate team row is genuinely conflicting (neither record dominates the other). - Keep the diagnostic in the existing bounded sync error; no page body or credentials are stored. - Update the regression test for the diagnostic format. This is observability only. It does not relax validation or publish any disputed table.','2026-11-22T00:28:43Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/193'),
(194,'Canonicalize PFIE team aliases before duplicate-row validation','Live Ligue 1 diagnostics show that multiple publisher rows are resolving to the same canonical club only after known-team matching. The first dedupe pass was too early and could not see those aliases. - Resolve known club aliases before source row-count and duplicate checks. - Apply the same cumulative overall-row dominance rule after canonicalization as before it. - Treat the bare name Paris as ambiguous rather than silently mapping it to Paris Saint-Germain when Paris FC is also a club in the competition. - Add tests for alias-based duplicate collapse and ambiguous Paris shorthand. A table still needs the exact expected club count, valid P/W/D/L/GF/GA/points arithmetic, source-row evidence, fresh dates where published, anti-regression and agreement from two independent publishers.','2026-11-22T00:32:48Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/194'),
(197,'Add TACTIX as a live independent La Liga standings source','- Add TACTIX''s current La Liga table as a direct trusted PFIE source alongside the official LaLiga standings page. - Retain ESPN and Transfermarkt as additional candidates, but do not allow stale Sky Sports table dates to count as current corroboration. - Add TACTIX to trusted publisher classification and publisher-root deduplication. - Preserve the two-independent-publisher requirement, full 20-team row checks, W/D/L/points arithmetic, source quotes and SAST date validation. - Add regression tests for the direct source configuration and publisher identity.','2026-11-22T01:06:09Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/197'),
(198,'Add a third independent source for La Liga standings','- Add Football Edge Lab as a third direct La Liga standings candidate alongside the official LaLiga page and TACTIX. - Classify it as a trusted publisher and normalize its subdomains to one publisher identity. - Preserve strict 20-team row evidence, W/D/L and points arithmetic, date freshness and two-independent-publisher consensus. - Document the three-source La Liga candidate set in PFIE integration and Parallel architecture docs.','2026-11-22T01:10:31Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/198'),
(199,'Record PFIE source snapshots when standings consensus fails','- Persist source-by-source standings snapshots when locally valid tables fail the two-independent-publisher consensus check. - Capture publisher domain, source URL, table date, row count and all team/stat columns in the failed standings sync metadata. - Keep the current published table unchanged when no consensus exists; do not weaken the two-source gate. - Document the diagnostic payload and intended admin/debugging use.','2026-11-22T01:13:24Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/199'),
(200,'docs: establish MVP launch-hardening readiness workspace','Adds an evidence-driven launch-hardening workspace for Puntr''s 1 Dec 2026 MVP. ### Included - Adds /dev/README.md as the workspace index and readiness dashboard. - Adds /dev/IMPLEMENTATION-PRIORITIES.md with the five P0 workstreams: PFIE reliability, manual odds, registration/activation, payments/compliance, and production operations. - Adds checklists, sprint dates, launch-day runbook, post-launch milestones and evidence notes. - Updates docs/PARALLEL_ARCHITECTURE.md to remove stale assumptions about live bookmaker reference odds and Monitor-based team news, and records the owner''s manual-odds MVP decision. - Updates docs/legal-changelog.md with the owner''s confirmation of the draw exclusion/re-pick terms previously documented on /feedback. ### Production audit findings recorded - 101 production migration ledger entries and 101 repository migration files; only one exact version-prefix match. - Multiple renamed, split and consolidated migrations make blind db push / migration repair unsafe. - Four active PFIE cron jobs are present, but their live schedules differ from the latest pending schedule migration. - The first pending schedule migration contains malformed dollar-quote syntax. - Standings: 7/12 scopes with recorded success; 5 have never succeeded. Automated odds: 0/11 successful scopes. - No production migration, cron schedule or schema change was made. ### Scope Documentation only. No application code, database schema, migration history or cron jobs are changed. The production reconciliation plan is documented, but write operations remain gated on a complete migration mapping and backup/rollback evidence.','2026-11-22T01:22:47Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/200'),
(201,'docs: update launch workspace PR status','Small documentation follow-up to the merged MVP launch-hardening workspace. - Marks PR #200 as merged in the /dev PR triage table. - Clarifies that cron.job_run_details contains 17,919 records overall, but none yet for new PFIE table job IDs 61–64 as of 01:22 UTC because their first scheduled window starts at 02:10 UTC. - Updates the launch checklist and Parallel architecture audit note with the more precise execution-history finding. No application code, production schema, migration history or cron configuration is changed.','2026-11-22T01:24:15Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/201'),
(202,'fix: allow admins to unregister a founding HQ prospect','- Fixes the Founding HQ registration checkbox so unchecking a verified founding member clears the `registered` flag and moves a `registered` pipeline stage back to `contacted`. - Prevents the server validator from re-deriving `registered: true` from a stale `stage === "registered"` value.','2026-11-22T03:35:57Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/202'),
(203,'feat: add branded Puntr PWA experience','Adds a branded, installable Puntr Progressive Web App foundation. ### Included - PWA manifest with standalone display mode, black launch background and the supplied Puntr logo asset used for the app icon, favicon and Apple touch icon. - Custom Puntr install card with Android''s native install prompt and iOS Safari Add to Home Screen instructions. - Service worker registration and branded offline fallback. - Conservative static-asset caching only. Authenticated, Supabase, betting, payment and live-data requests are not cached. - Standalone app launch preloader based on Puntr''s existing preloader design. - English (South Africa) and Afrikaans install-prompt copy. - Implementation notes in docs/pwa-implementation.md. ### Deliberately deferred Push notifications are not enabled. They need a separately reviewed consent flow, VAPID configuration, secure server-side delivery, RLS-protected subscription storage and POPIA/legal alignment. ### Validation CI checks should run against this PR. The repository''s CLAUDE.md requires lint, typecheck and production build before merge; no merge has been performed.','2026-11-22T04:30:25Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/203'),
(204,'feat: persistent auth flows and Web Push PWA','Implements the Puntr PWA authentication continuation and Web Push milestone. ### Authentication and deep links - Preserve the originating in-app URL through /join, password sign-in, email OTP, custom email confirmation, Google OAuth PKCE, onboarding, MFA and password recovery. - Add /auth/callback for OAuth code exchange and resume /join before returning to the validated internal destination. - Harden safeNext() against external/protocol-relative URLs, credentials, encoded path separators and auth/admin/API destinations. - Replace the Predictions guest-gate signup iframe with first-party navigation to /join. ### PWA and push notifications - Add an explicit standalone PWA opt-in prompt with a 14-day dismissal window and browser-permission handling. - Add account-wide push opt-out in Account settings and append-only consent grant/withdrawal records. - Add a same-origin authenticated Vercel server endpoint at /api/push; it verifies Supabase sessions, restricts campaign operations to admin profiles, validates internal destinations, rate-limits admin campaigns, excludes banned accounts, cleans expired endpoints and records delivery outcomes. - Add Web Push with VAPID. Private signing key is stored as a sensitive Vercel environment variable; public key is used by the client. - Add service-worker push display and notification-click deep linking. - Add Admin > Community > Push notifications with metrics, self-test, targeted campaigns and history. ### Data and documentation - Add migration 20261122230000_pwa_push_notifications.sql for subscriptions, campaigns, delivery logs, RLS and consent-purpose updates.','2026-11-22T06:06:24Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/204'),
(205,'feat(dev): add approved PWA hardening roadmap to /dev workspace','- Add the owner-approved ten-workstream PWA hardening programme to the private admin-only `/dev` workspace. - Add a collapsible roadmap panel covering delivery reliability, scheduling, granular preferences, event triggers, device management, cross-platform QA, offline resilience, accessibility, privacy/retention and operations/observability. - Document delivery rules, separate-PR approach and release gates in `docs/PWA_HARDENING_PRELAUNCH.md`. This PR adds the approved pre-launch roadmap and workspace visibility only. It does not implement the ten workstreams themselves. Each implementation will be delivered in separate feature branches/PRs with Vercel Sandbox QA and preview validation.','2026-11-22T10:05:44Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/205'),
(206,'feat: introduce Discover hub and improve PWA/mobile experience','- Rename the Predictions hub to **Discover** at `/discover`, with a legacy `/predictions` redirect and updated PWA entry point, notification fallback, canonical metadata and sitemap. - Retire Insights navigation and redirect legacy `/insights` visits to Discover. - Remove the Community shortcut from the mobile header menu. - Improve responsive behaviour and overflow handling across the weekly leaders, head-to-head duels, latest results and league tables previews. - Add an animated Fantasy Arena upcoming-feature spotlight beneath the Betting Slip Converter. - Add a five-item published sports newsroom preview directly below This week''s leaders. - Respect the installed PWA status-bar safe area on iOS.','2026-11-22T07:26:22Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/206'),
(207,'feat: add context-aware upcoming fixture rails','- Add a compact Matchday Intelligence rail above the homepage hero for signed-out visitors during the pre-launch founding campaign. - Add a compact top-of-app Fixture Ticker Bar for signed-in members and everyone after the configured launch date. - Switch the sitewide top strip based on `useSession()` and `DEFAULT_LAUNCH_DATE`, keeping the server/first client render deterministic. - Filter both fixture surfaces to the active launch competitions: Betway Premiership, Premier League and UEFA Champions League. - Add offline/empty-state preview fixtures, snap scrolling, three-second auto-advance, reduced-motion support, and pause-on-hover/touch/focus. - Add a Founding Member reservation dialog triggered by the locked PUNT AI teaser and "Back this pick" action. - Route real member ticker fixtures to their match rooms and guest reservation actions to the existing Founding Member join flow. - Extend the upcoming fixture read with optional home/away score fields so real live scores can be shown when supplied by the data source.','2026-11-22T07:58:56Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/207'),
(208,'fix: OAuth redirects, mobile fixture ticker and desktop layout','- Fix Google OAuth callback handling: complete the PKCE exchange, verify the resulting session, route existing members to their requested destination, and send new OAuth users through the existing onboarding flow. - Handle direct callback visits with no OAuth code/session by returning users to sign-in; if profile lookup fails, avoid incorrectly treating an existing member as a new user. - Redesign the fixture ticker for phones and tablets with abbreviated team names, team badges, a cleaner compact layout, no PUNT AI label or competition abbreviations, and a substantially slower marquee. - Hide the ticker at desktop breakpoints and slow the homepage fixture rail autoplay from 7 to 15 seconds. - Correct live-minute refresh so the displayed minute is not double-counted. - Give common desktop/laptop layouts more content width by delaying the left navigation rail until XL and the right rail until 2XL. - Update the English homepage headline to “Know your sport? Back your call.”','2026-11-22T08:55:09Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/208'),
(211,'feat(onboarding): reward push opt-in and app install','- Turn the existing push-notification quest into a direct opt-in flow: request browser permission, register the Web Push subscription, confirm an active device subscription, then award the one-time 50 PuntPoints reward. - Turn the existing install-app quest into an actionable PWA install flow. The existing install prompt/iOS guide opens from the quest; the 100 PuntPoints reward is claimable after the member reopens Puntr in standalone mode. - Update the /dev historical-results readiness milestone from 2,500 to 7,000 verified match results and align the readiness test. - Add English and Afrikaans quest copy, and restore the missing Afrikaans Fantasy Arena mobile navigation label.','2026-11-22T10:41:47Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/211'),
(212,'feat(matchday): quick search, consensus and matchday interactions','- Restore the /dev historical-results milestone to its original 2,500 target and record 7,775 verified imported results as achieved. - Reuse the animated betting-slip visual from the Discover Betting Slip Converter component at the top of /slips. - Add global Cmd/Ctrl+K and a mobile Tap to Search control. Search results jump to a team''s next upcoming fixture and show available league position plus a transparent last-five form index. - Add a shared green checkmark/sheen spring animation and optional short vibration for locked picks and PuntPoints balance updates. - Replace the community consensus rows with an animated multi-colour split bar and count-up percentages. - Add a match-page Challenge a Friend entry point. It presets a 50 PuntPoints stake, validates stake eligibility and opens a WhatsApp share link after duel creation using the existing duel backend.','2026-11-22T11:15:22Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/212'),
(213,'feat: add The Good Sport podcast and PWA install recovery','- Change the PWA install prompt''s **Not now** action into a persistent left-edge **Get The App** notch. Tapping the notch reopens the install flow; the X hides both prompt and notch for seven days. - Add **The Good Sport**, Puntr''s audiovisual sports podcast, to the homepage and create the series page plus a dedicated Episode 01 page for the 1 December 2026 premiere. - Add a season-one episode-list modal, responsive podcast player, premiere email opt-in, YouTube CTA, SEO metadata and canonical URLs. - Add a restricted Supabase table for one-off episode notification opt-ins, a scheduled 09:00 SAST delivery job with hourly retries through 12:00 SAST, and 30-day retention. - Add mandatory podcast production and QA standards in `docs/THE_GOOD_SPORT_PUBLISHING_GUIDELINES.md`, and update the privacy notice for the one-off email alert.','2026-11-22T12:57:16Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/213'),
(214,'chore(dev): add The Good Sport premiere launch checklist','- Add a dedicated **The Good Sport · Premiere readiness** checklist to the private admin-only `/dev` workspace. - Track the outstanding production launch dependencies for the 1 December 2026 Episode 01 premiere. - Keep all six items explicitly pending until completion and verification; this is a planning checklist and does not imply that production configuration or delivery tests have been completed.','2026-11-22T13:02:30Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/214'),
(215,'chore(test): add one-off Good Sport email delivery smoke test','## Purpose Temporarily add a CRON_SECRET-protected smoke-test endpoint for the production Resend configuration. It sends exactly one idempotent test email to Puntr''s configured support inbox (`support@puntr.co.za`) and accepts no caller-supplied recipient. This route will be removed immediately after the production provider-acceptance test.','2026-11-22T13:22:29Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/215'),
(216,'chore(dev): update Good Sport launch verification status','- Update the private `/dev` checklist to reflect production work actually completed. - Mark the Supabase migration and production configuration complete. - Mark the official Puntr YouTube channel URL as verified and configured across Vercel environments. - Record the production signup, cron-auth/time-gate and Resend provider-acceptance smoke tests; keep the full delivery test partially verified until scheduled sends, actual inbox receipt, retries and database acknowledgement are exercised. - Keep Episode 01 artwork and audio explicitly deferred, as requested. - Remove the temporary CRON_SECRET-protected email smoke-test route after its one-off test.','2026-11-22T13:24:02Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/216'),
(217,'feat(home): refresh hero messaging and contextual CTAs','- Refresh the homepage hero with the requested eyebrow, subtitle, description and responsible-play clarification. - Randomly assign headline A/B once per page view after session resolution; track impressions and CTA interactions through the existing consent-aware analytics layer. - Show context-aware CTAs: signed-out visitors get Founding Member + video actions; signed-in members get prediction or leaderboard actions based on their recorded pick activity. - Set Puntr''s official YouTube channel URL to the supplied @puntr_za handle in Vercel production, preview and development environments, with the same fallback in code. - Replace the PWA, browser favicon and Apple touch icon references with https://puntr.co.za/puntrgreen.png. - Rename the homepage Newsroom eyebrow/title to “From The Newsroom” / “IN CASE YOU MISSED IT”. - Move The Good Sport promo to the former bookmaker-wall position and require an authenticated session for its display and episode audio playback, including the episode page. - Move the Founding CTA above the bookmaker wall; move the bookmaker wall below it and above Newsroom; hide the bookmaker wall for signed-in members. - Shorten the bookmaker wall headline as requested.','2026-11-22T15:46:54Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/217'),
(218,'feat(home): improve Good Sport access, homepage guide and PuntPoints copy','- Keep The Good Sport visible to signed-out and signed-in visitors while restricting audio playback to authenticated members. - Show a sign-up/login modal when a signed-out visitor attempts playback, including on the episode page and before the premiere. - Move The Good Sport between the bookmaker logo wall and Newsroom on the homepage. - Replace the previous homepage join promo with a plain-English three-step guide for signed-out visitors, positioned above “The difference is the record.” - Change the guide CTA to “See how it works” and route it to `/how-it-works`. - Correct English and Afrikaans PuntPoints marketing copy to explain eligible Community Duel stakes and the winner receiving the settled PuntPoints pot.','2026-11-22T16:32:06Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/218'),
(219,'Fix launch-critical results recovery and data visibility','- Parse valid model JSON even when wrapped in Markdown fences or surrounding prose, without attempting to repair malformed/truncated output. - Retry malformed PFIE fixture/result extraction once with a smaller, higher-priority source set and a strict JSON-only instruction. - Prioritise up to three overdue fixtures in result searches; keep unresolved fixtures eligible for seven days and cap result backoff at six hours. - Keep the eight competitions with existing standings in the recovery sync, but expose only competitions whose latest standings sync is successful and no older than 18 hours. Stale leagues automatically reappear after a successful refresh; four competitions with no standings data remain disabled for launch. - Add an admin settlement view for overdue scheduled/live fixtures with unsettled picks, so the queue no longer appears empty when the missing step is result verification. - Correct the admin settleable flag so only a finished fixture with a complete score is considered settleable. - Improve notification admin feedback: explain why Send is disabled until required fields are complete, surface admin/member lookup errors, and clarify that newsroom-linked notifications are withdrawn from the Newsroom tab.','2026-11-22T19:37:31Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/219'),
(220,'Restore EPL and La Liga standings reconciliation','- Add canonical aliases for La Liga team names that differ across official and independent table publishers (Athletic/Athletic Bilbao, Deportivo/Dépor/Deportivo La Coruna, Espanyol/Espanyol Barcelona). - Add regression coverage for those aliases so equivalent publisher rows can produce matching table signatures. - Configure explicit official and independent standings pages for the Premier League, including BBC, Sky Sports, ESPN and Transfermarkt. - Replace the ESPN La Liga standings candidate with Tactix and Football Edge Lab, retaining LaLiga official, Sky Sports and Transfermarkt sources.','2026-11-22T20:29:54Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/220'),
(221,'PUNTR: Responsible Play, growth pages and copy alignment','Adds the requested public-site growth and trust pages, navigation updates and a first-pass brand messaging alignment. ### New pages - `/responsible-play`: safer-play guidance, self-exclusion route, SARGF contact channels and a clear explanation of Puntr''s role. The global affiliate banner is suppressed on this page. - `/brand-ambassadors`: audience, eligibility, 30–45 day assessment, potential retainers, performance rewards, vouchers, merchandise and partner-sponsored giveaways. - `/fantasy-arena`: dedicated Fantasy Arena v3.0 marketing page, clearly marked in development and distinguished from current Practice Mode. - `/bookmakers`: responsive searchable directory with 43 curated bookmaker records, province filter, licence-holder details and links back to the NGB register. No direct betting links or paid rankings are included. ### Commercial copy - Referral page now explains 10–30% recurring commission on eligible Puntr Pro subscription revenue. - Explicitly excludes bookmaker deposits, stakes, losses and winnings from referral commissions. - Pricing page, member menu and affiliate disclosure now link to or explain the referral programme. - Ambassador page separates its assessment and potential retainer/bonus benefits from the standard referral agreement. ### Messaging and trust - Aligns homepage and bookmaker-independence copy. - Labels AI insight examples and tools as sample/planned until integrations are live. - Adds a sitewide Responsible Play link in the responsible-gambling notice.','2026-11-22T22:27:27Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/221'),
(222,'PUNTR: Ambassador applications, page art and accessibility','Implements the follow-up requested after PR #221 was merged. ### Animated page graphics - Adds four distinct original SVG motion scenes to the shared PageArt system: - Responsible Play: shield, open hands and heartbeat line. - Fantasy Arena 3.0: arena ring, floodlights and trophy. - Bookmaker Directory: searchable register rows and verification marks. - Brand Ambassadors: broadcast megaphone and creator/community profiles. - Uses existing motion classes and reduced-motion handling; graphics are decorative and aria-hidden. ### Brand Ambassador application - Both primary CTAs now read **Start Your Application** and open the same responsive, five-step Typeform-style modal. - Captures contact/location, 18+ confirmation, role, platforms, public profile links, audience size, content examples, focus, availability, motivation and responsible-play/privacy acknowledgements. - Uses the existing public form submission pipeline, including validation, per-email/global rate limits and database persistence. - Brand Ambassador submissions are routed through Resend to `partners@puntr.co.za`, with the applicant as reply-to. If email delivery fails, the submission remains saved and the applicant receives a direct email fallback. - Privacy notice and internal data map updated for this application data flow. ### Discover and roadmap - Discover Fantasy Arena highlight now links to `/fantasy-arena` with the exact CTA **Join the fantasy league**. - Roadmap now includes Fantasy Arena 3.0 and the Brand Ambassador Programme.','2026-11-22T23:53:27Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/222'),
(223,'Newsroom: Parallel-first editorial engine and three daily publishing slots','Upgrade the Puntr Newsroom from one Gemini-authored daily article to a Parallel-first editorial engine with three distinct daily sports-content slots. ### Editorial engine - Add Parallel Responses Medium as the primary writer, using structured JSON output. - Keep Gemini as the preferred independent fact-check reviewer and writing fallback; Parallel can cover review when Gemini quota is exhausted. - On the 06:00 SAST Breaking News run, generate a Gemini comparison draft alongside the Parallel draft. The Gemini draft is revised and independently reviewed where budget permits, then saved as REVIEW only so the owner can compare both outputs in the Newsroom desk. - Preserve the existing Parallel Search + extraction research flow and branded per-article cover-image pipeline. - Attribute new articles to Michael C. - Suppress the AI-assistance label and AI disclaimer on Parallel-authored public articles while retaining cited source links. ### Daily editorial schedule - 06:00 SAST — Breaking News - 12:30 SAST — Editorial Analysis - 18:00 SAST — Sports Intelligence - Each slot has independent idempotency and retry windows. - Editorial Analysis and Sports Intelligence require at least three independent source domains and six supported claims. - Breaking News requires at least two independent sources and four supported claims. ### Quality and operations - Scheduled publishing no longer bypasses critical validation or the minimum quality score. - Remove the unsafe publish-on-schedule override from the admin controls.','2026-11-23T01:13:28Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/223'),
(224,'Add 30-day synthetic QA experiment harness','Adds a controlled, explicitly labelled synthetic QA harness for the 27 Nov–26 Dec 2026 Puntr experiment (30 calendar days, SAST). - Adds 50 distinct synthetic QA persona profiles and a JSON Schema. - Adds an isolated Playwright package with a 1–3 worker cap, round-robin batch selection and hybrid headless/headed execution. - Adds a GitHub Actions schedule at 06:00, 09:00, 13:00, 17:00 and 20:00 SAST. - Browser journeys are guest/read-only and restricted to allowlisted public routes. Each request carries a synthetic QA marker. - Adds a daily fixture allocator that assigns each due persona one upcoming fixture from a followed competition and produces one or two preferred-market decisions per SAST day. - Groups persona questions by fixture: up to 100 named Decisions API questions in one shared-evidence request. - The Decisions route uses Puntr''s existing parallel_cache and createQuotaClaim/api_budget_claim guard, plus the experiment-specific $50 ledger. Provider keys remain server-side. - Adds service-role-only Supabase experiment, persona, session, research and budget-ledger tables. - The migration creates the experiment paused. All routes and scheduled runs skip unless it is explicitly activated and within the date window. - Adds an admin-only Synthetic QA section under `/admin`, with live experiment status, persona coverage, browser session outcomes, research batch/source counts, latest activity and the experiment budget ledger. Reads are server-side and re-check `is_admin()`; the panel does not expose service-role credentials or allow activation.','2026-11-27T16:35:34Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/224'),
(225,'Add Track360 verification meta tag to homepage','- Adds the requested `track360-verify` meta tag to the homepage route head metadata. - Keeps the verification tag scoped to the homepage.','2026-11-23T07:13:30Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/225'),
(226,'Move synthetic QA scheduling to Vercel Cron','Moves the synthetic QA scheduler from GitHub Actions to native Vercel Cron and adds an explicit analytics exclusion marker. - Adds five Vercel Cron invocations for 06:00, 09:00, 13:00, 17:00 and 20:00 SAST. - Adds a cron-authenticated GET route that runs one least-recently-tested synthetic persona per invocation against the allowlisted public routes. - Stores each route-check session only in the isolated synthetic telemetry tables. Uses a short lease to avoid duplicate concurrent work. - Calls the existing daily fixture/Parallel Decisions allocator only after the route checks pass. Existing cache, provider quota guard and US$50 budget cap remain in force. - Removes the GitHub Actions synthetic QA workflow. - Explicitly blocks the puntr_synthetic_qa=1 cookie from GA4/GTM, session analytics and first-party campaign event writes, even if analytics consent exists. - Adds the synthetic cookie to the retained manual Playwright suite. - Updates the admin dashboard labels to distinguish server-side route checks from browser sessions. - Adds a migration to allow the new read_only_route_check session type.','2026-11-27T17:01:04Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/226'),
(227,'Add PFIE learning pipeline for synthetic QA and PUNT AI','- Add a persistent PFIE learning corpus that ingests isolated synthetic QA sessions and synthetic research from every experiment. - Schedule daily ingestion through Vercel Cron at 06:30 SAST. - Convert deterministic route-check outcomes into verified route-quality examples. - Quarantine synthetic forecast outputs until two independent official/trusted PFIE observations corroborate the final score. - Add a service-role-only `pfie_training_dataset` view for approved, verified examples. - Add an admin PFIE Learning panel with corpus metrics and a guarded “Verify with PFIE” action. - Document data governance, training eligibility and how PUNT AI should consume PFIE outputs.','2026-11-27T17:16:08Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/227'),
(229,'Make consented real member activity the primary PFIE learning source','- Promote consented real member activity to PFIE''s primary learning source; retain synthetic QA as a secondary diagnostics/evaluation source. - Add a distinct `pfie_learning` consent purpose, updated first-visit notice, granular cookie controls and Account → Privacy and data controls. - Capture allowlisted first-party engagement events through an authenticated server function, plus actual published-pick actions through a database trigger. - Keep PFIE activity separate from campaign analytics. Exclude PII, private messages, payment details, stakes, IPs and device fingerprints. - Pseudonymize learning subjects with a server-side HMAC mapping; keep raw IDs out of the training view. - Incrementally ingest consented member activity into `pfie_learning_examples` as behavioural-preference signals. Synthetic session/research ingestion remains secondary. - Add aggregate `pfie_learning_signals` read model and server-only PFIE accessor for coverage/relevance insights. - PFIE now uses aggregated opted-in member interest to reorder fixture/results refresh priority. It still processes all selected competitions and never relaxes source validation. - Add consent withdrawal deletion, account-anonymisation cleanup, data export and 12-month event-level retention. - Update privacy notice in English and Afrikaans and extend the PFIE admin panel with primary/secondary source counts and aggregated member-interest signals.','2026-11-27T17:35:17Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/229'),
(230,'Restore priority PFIE league standings ahead of MVP launch','- Restore the agreed pre-launch standings priority order: Premier League, La Liga, UEFA Champions League, UEFA Conference League, Motsepe Foundation Championship. - Keep existing validated domestic standings in scope after those priorities. - Add UEFA Conference League league-phase standings configuration for the 36-team format, using the official UEFA table plus independently published Sky Sports, TNT Sports and FOX Sports tables. - Reconcile known UEFA Conference League fixture/table naming variants (including Hearts, AGF/Aarhus, Sint-Truidense, Lincoln Red Imps, Universitatea Craiova, Inter Escaldes and Iberia Tbilisi) with regression tests.','2026-11-27T18:24:35Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/230'),
(231,'Add Bundesliga to PFIE launch restoration order','- Add Bundesliga as the sixth PFIE launch restoration priority, immediately after the five agreed restoration competitions. - Keep the existing 18-team Bundesliga standings configuration and independent Bundesliga.com / DFB source pairing. - Update regression coverage for the launch priority order.','2026-11-27T18:43:42Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/231'),
(232,'Add a cumulative Parallel spend guard through Q1 2027','- Raise the internal Parallel family monthly ceiling from $35 to $50. - Add a cumulative $200 spend guard from 28 Nov 2026 through 31 Mar 2027. - Reduce Parallel Responses Medium to 15 calls/day and 450/month; the existing model router falls back to approved Gemini models when the paid quota is exhausted. - Document the 27 Nov production usage audit and the Q1 operating limits.','2026-11-27T18:43:47Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/232'),
(233,'Improve PFIE UEFA standings source coverage','- Prioritise CBS Sports as the first independent Champions League full-table source after UEFA. - Add Swiss Football Data and KeepStandings as independent full-stat Conference League sources. - Remove stale/incomplete TNT and Sky Conference League pages from the direct-source set. - Mark the two new publishers as trusted and add regression coverage.','2026-11-27T18:45:51Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/233'),
(234,'Reconcile UCL standings publisher team aliases','- Normalize five CBS Sports / FOX Sports naming variants that currently prevent the two complete UCL tables from reaching identical canonical team signatures. - Add regression coverage for LASK/Linz, Manchester United/Manchester Utd, PSV/PSV Eindhoven, Slavia Praha/Slavia Prague, and Slovan Bratislava/Slovan Bratisl.','2026-11-27T18:56:38Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/234'),
(235,'Improve Conference League, Motsepe and Bundesliga source reconciliation','- Add a current full-table source for the 2026/27 UEFA Conference League and classify it as a trusted independent publisher. - Replace the stale Motsepe table source with Global Sports Archive, retaining RotaScore and the existing independent source validation. - Normalize the Bundesliga publisher variant Bayer 04 Leverkusen / Bayer Leverkusen. - Add regression tests for the new source domains and Bundesliga alias.','2026-11-27T19:10:53Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/235'),
(236,'Reduce Parallel usage and attribute API spend by feature','- Reserve Parallel Responses Medium for the scheduled breaking-news draft only; use alternative Gemini models for revisions and independent review, and Gemini-only models for editorial/intelligence and manual newsroom generation. - Add 6-hour newsroom search and extraction caching so repeated source reads across slots/retries do not claim another provider call. - Add per-claim feature attribution (`newsroom:scheduled`, `newsroom:manual`, `newsroom:admin`, `pfie:standings`, `pfie:odds`, `synthetic:decisions`) to a new `api_call_events` ledger. - Tighten the internal Parallel Medium quota to 2 calls/day and 60/month, leaving controlled retry headroom.','2026-11-27T19:11:08Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/236'),
(237,'Normalize the Bundesliga Leverkusen identity','- Normalize the short historical fixture label `Leverkusen` with publisher variants `Bayer Leverkusen` and `Bayer 04 Leverkusen`. - Add a regression test for the three names.','2026-11-27T19:17:24Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/237'),
(238,'Grant service-role access to API usage attribution ledger','- Grant the Supabase `service_role` explicit table and identity-sequence privileges for `api_call_events`. - Add an insert-only RLS policy for `service_role`; RLS remains enabled.','2026-11-27T19:17:30Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/238'),
(239,'Allow independently verified historical goal corrections','- Permit a narrowly scoped standings correction when two independent publisher tables agree and the only changes to an existing team row are goals-for / goals-against. - Keep played, wins, draws, losses and points strictly unchanged when using this exception. - Continue rejecting all other no-new-match regressions. - Record the corrected teams and old/new goal totals in `sync_status.meta` for auditability.','2026-11-27T19:21:09Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/239'),
(240,'Set practical Parallel Search and Extract quotas','- Reduce Parallel Search quota from 5,000/day and 60,000/month to 250/day and 7,500/month. - Reduce Parallel Extract quota from 2,500/day and 30,000/month to 200/day and 6,000/month. - Document the $50 internal monthly family ceiling and $200 cumulative Q1 2027 allowance in quota notes.','2026-11-27T19:21:19Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/240'),
(241,'Refine PFIE launch standings and publish Parallel newsroom drafts for review','- Move EFL Championship into the pre-launch standings priority and defer Motsepe Foundation Championship to an explicit post-launch list. - Configure the 24-team EFL table with the official EFL page and independent BBC, Sky Sports and ESPN sources; add common EFL club-name aliases (QPR, Sheffield Utd/Wed). - Keep CAF Confederation Cup fixtures/results in pre-launch coverage. Do not flatten its four group tables into one 16-team table; group-aware standings require a schema/UI extension. - Remove the Gemini shadow-article comparison path from the scheduled Newsroom pipeline. - Disconnect Gemini from the Newsroom entirely: all three daily slots (breaking, editorial and intelligence) use Parallel Medium for drafting, revision and the separate review pass. Gemini remains available to the distinct PFIE and reference-odds pipelines, which still depend on it. - Replace the hard-coded QA score floor of 49 with graduated 15-point critical-issue penalties. - Make model-review findings advisory (8-point aggregate deduction), while deterministic unsupported-claim, quotation, number, length and sourcing checks remain critical. - Clarify exact source IDs and minimum article length in the writing prompt; tighten reviewer instructions to check all supplied sources and avoid flagging clearly framed analysis/opinion. - Publish Parallel-authored drafts when automatic publishing is enabled even when QA fails the configured score/critical gate. Preserve QA score, flags, reviewer status and publish audit metadata for owner review.','2026-11-27T20:30:05Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/241'),
(242,'Fix Synthetic QA canonical origin and PFIE Learning tab label','- Fix the Synthetic QA route check using the Vercel cron invocation hostname as its origin. Production requests now start at the canonical `https://puntr.co.za` origin, so the site''s own canonical-host redirect is not incorrectly reported as an external-origin redirect. - Keep the follow-up synthetic decisions request on the same canonical origin. - Add a small URL helper and regression tests for canonical-origin routing and rejection of protocol-relative/external paths. - Add the missing `tabs.pfieLearning` translation in `src/locales/en-ZA/admin.json`, which was causing the desktop admin tab to render the raw translation key.','2026-11-27T20:43:57Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/242'),
(243,'Add group-aware league standings storage','- Add `group_name` to league standings so group-stage competitions can store separate tables. - Change the primary key to `(competition_key, group_name, team)` and group the position index accordingly. - Extend `replace_standings` to accept an optional `group` field while preserving compatibility with existing single-table payloads.','2026-11-27T21:14:07Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/243'),
(244,'Schedule rugby and basketball for January 2027; move Good Sport premiere','- Move rugby and basketball roadmap windows to January 2027. - Space subsequent sports categories at two-month intervals (March, May, July, September and November 2027), leaving at least one full month between category launches. - Move The Good Sport Episode 01 notification premiere window to 5 January 2027 at 09:00 SAST. - Update roadmap tests for the new windows.','2026-11-27T21:25:10Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/244'),
(245,'Integrate labelled AI participants into the Founding 100','- Add explicit `is_ai_participant` and `ai_persona_key` profile fields; public profile views expose only the AI label, not internal persona metadata. - Add a service-role-only provisioning RPC and an idempotent admin workflow that creates the 50 existing synthetic personas as managed Supabase Auth identities with non-deliverable `.invalid` email addresses. - Assign each AI profile the next number in the existing Founding list. With the current 16 numbered human profiles and four reserved places, the expected result after provisioning is 70/100 (16 human + 50 AI + 4 reserved); the actual counter is computed from production state. - Show an AI participant label on public profiles, community picks and weekly leaderboards. - Update Founding HQ to separate human profiles, AI profiles and reserved places, and provide an explicit admin provisioning action. - Exempt AI auth identities from human signup support notifications and preserve human age/POPIA requirements.','2026-11-27T21:37:04Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/245'),
(246,'Restore the ten launch standings and add four-group CAF tables','- Set the PFIE standings launch order to the agreed ten: Betway Premiership, Premier League, EFL Championship, La Liga, UEFA Champions League, UEFA Conference League, Bundesliga, Serie A, Ligue 1 and CAF Confederation Cup. - Explicitly classify other table-based competitions as post-launch. - Add CAF Confederation Cup 2026/27 group sources (365Scores and Global Sports Archive), four required groups (A-D), and four teams per group. - Extract and validate each CAF group independently; reject a source if it omits any group; require two independent publishers for every group before publishing. - Persist each group using the already-deployed `group_name` column and render four distinct group sections on `/tables`. - Make regression checks, source diagnostics and consensus retries group-aware. - Add focused tests for ten-competition priority, four-group extraction, missing-group rejection and per-group corroboration.','2026-11-27T21:43:04Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/246'),
(247,'Move odds extraction to Parallel and gate sources on written rights','- Replace Gemini odds extraction with Parallel Responses Chat low, using structured JSON output and the existing `parallel-chat:low` quota/budget bucket. - Use Parallel Search and Parallel Extract only for odds discovery and fresh page reads; refuse cached page copies older than 15 minutes. - Increase candidate bookmaker page coverage to five per competition run and prioritize affiliate domains: Hollywoodbets, SupaBets, YesPlay, 1xBet, Easybet and Playbet. - Add a production bookmaker rights registry seeded with 14 known candidate domains, affiliate status and priority. Every row starts disabled with licence and data-rights review pending. - Require verified current South African licence, approved written data rights, explicit automated-access permission, evidence URL, review timestamp and reviewer before a source can be enabled. - Add a default-off `ODDS_AUTOMATION_ENABLED` gate. The cron returns a disabled response unless the feature flag is explicitly enabled and at least one registry source is fully approved. - Update the Parallel architecture notes and odds tests.','2026-11-27T21:47:57Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/247'),
(248,'Add AI founding-member provisioning and align January podcast premiere','- Add an admin-only provisioning action for the 50 existing synthetic personas using Supabase Auth Admin and the existing `provision_ai_community_member` RPC. - Display founding allocation, linked AI member count and provisioning results in Admin → Synthetic QA. - Preserve the single founding-number sequence: existing genuine members and held reservations remain intact; each AI account receives its own unique number and counts toward the 100-place cap. - Public profiles already expose an `AI participant` label; the profile page and weekly leaderboard render that label. This change makes the admin workflow explicit and auditable. - Move The Good Sport Episode 01 date and client-side premiere gate to 5 January 2027, matching the existing premiere notification cron. - Clarify that post-January sport categories are scheduled at least one full month apart (current roadmap uses two-month spacing). - Update the synthetic experiment runbook to distinguish read-only QA personas from the separately provisioned, labelled AI community accounts.','2026-11-27T21:56:49Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/248'),
(250,'Complete PUNT AI production storage and usage controls','- Add the missing production `punt_ai_cache` and `punt_ai_usage` tables with service-role-only access. - Add an authenticated, security-definer `punt_ai_claim` RPC that validates the caller, age attestation, account standing, launch gate and AI-account exclusion. - Enforce per-user SAST usage caps: Free 20/day and 300/month; Pro 40/day and 600/month. Caps are admin-configurable through `app_settings`. - Add the missing `punt_ai_live` price at 2 credits per successful live-web answer. - Preserve the existing provider controls: Gemini internal responses use configured model quotas; live web uses Parallel Search, Extract and Chat low under the shared Parallel budget and Q1 cumulative spend cap. - Document the PUNT AI data, credit and provider controls.','2026-11-27T22:01:13Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/250'),
(251,'Revert unreviewed PUNT AI migration commit','This cleanup PR removes the migration file that was inadvertently committed directly to `main`. The corrected migration remains in PR #250 and will be merged through the normal preview/check workflow. No production database changes were made.','2026-11-27T22:00:27Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/251'),
(252,'Add pull-request Vitest CI','Adds a minimal GitHub Actions workflow that installs dependencies with Bun and runs the existing Vitest suite for pull requests targeting main. This makes unit-test results visible before subsequent feature PRs are merged.','2026-11-27T22:00:49Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/252'),
(253,'Remove unavailable GitHub Actions workflow','The GitHub-hosted runner did not start (runner_id 0, no runner name) and the workflow failed before executing any steps. Remove the workflow rather than leave a failing required-looking check. Vercel preview remains the active PR build check; add CI back when a runner is available.','2026-11-27T22:02:25Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/253'),
(254,'Add bookmaker licence and data-rights admin register','- Add a dedicated Admin → Bookmakers tab for all 42 operators in Puntr''s curated National Gambling Board directory cross-reference. - Show candidate licence holder, provincial regulator, province and licence reference; link the NGB verified-operators register and WCGRB directory. - Record licence verification evidence separately from written odds-data permissions for collection, storage, display, attribution, retention and redistribution/comparison. - Keep automated access disabled by default and require all approvals plus evidence before an operator can be enabled. - Add a post-launch checklist for bookmaker outreach/verification and the PUNT AI safety, data-quality, entitlement, quota and cost review.','2026-11-27T22:09:15Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/254'),
(256,'Complete bookmaker candidate coverage in Admin','Extend Admin → Bookmakers beyond the 43 curated NGB directory entries to include the three additional affiliate/candidate records already held in the permissions registry: 1xBet, Playbet and LottoStar. They are explicitly marked as unverified candidates, not as licensed operators. Correct the post-launch checklist''s directory count.','2026-11-27T22:11:33Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/256'),
(259,'Integrate labelled AI members into the community and H2H','- Replace the static Community Forum preview with live, database-backed threads and replies. Public posts and replies show the author''s public profile and an explicit AI participant label where applicable. - Add RLS, server-side author checks, a 10-post/day human-member limit and service-role-only AI publishing. AI accounts cannot publish through public client permissions. - Add a daily AI community job, scheduled for 10:00 SAST after founding sign-ups open. It rotates through the 50 AI profiles and creates up to 3 threads and 3 replies to recent genuine-member discussions per day. - Add up to 2 source-backed, zero-stake H2H challenges per day after the official launch gate opens. Challenges require two distinct market picks, at least two independent source domains and a minimum 55% selected probability. Human members can accept them through the existing H2H flow. - Disclose AI participation on duel cards, duel rooms, the H2H leaderboard, public profiles, community posts and the admin member list. - Add service-role-only audit tables for daily runs, per-persona activity and AI challenges. The job is idempotent by South African calendar date and rotates AI duel participants with a 14-day cooldown. - Update the AI provisioning RPC to use current JWT role claims, align persona metadata with the AI community role and recover founding numbers after partial provisioning. - Show the assigned founding-number range in Founding HQ after provisioning. The existing campaign counter counts all 50 AI profiles while separately reporting human, AI and reserved places.','2026-11-27T22:27:15Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/259'),
(260,'Restore PFIE launch standings and handle the pending CAF qualifier','- Add current independent standings sources for the Betway Premiership (NasiScore and ScoreMondo), EFL Championship (Zeanball and Statsfera) and Ligue 1 (Ligue1Schedule, ESPN and Zeanball), while keeping each source set within the six-source extraction limit. - Retain the official and independent sources already used for Serie A, and allow a narrowly scoped, two-source-corroborated one-match played-count correction for Milan only. The correction must remain internally consistent (W+D+L=P and points=3W+D), cannot increase goals or points, and is recorded in sync metadata. - Model the CAF Confederation Cup''s current Group C state accurately: three confirmed teams and one pending qualifier. Group C accepts three or four teams; Groups A, B and D still require four each. The extraction prompt explicitly forbids inventing a placeholder or omitting Group C. - Permit exactly one additional team in the CAF snapshot when the pending qualifier is confirmed, while requiring every previously verified team to remain present. - Reject placeholder rows such as TBC/TBD instead of treating them as real teams. - Display a Group C pending-qualifier note on the public tables page while that group has three teams. - Add unit tests for group ranges, pending-qualifier expansion, placeholder rejection, source configuration and the scoped Milan correction.','2026-11-27T22:37:20Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/260'),
(261,'Finalize PUNT AI data-first routing and member safeguards','- Prefer Puntr''s own verified fixtures, results and launch standings for table, fixture and recent-result questions; reserve Parallel live research for external updates. - Keep odds questions out of PUNT AI live-web routing so reference prices remain governed by the licensed odds pipeline. - Keep private account, picks and slips questions out of external search. - Require age-verified, eligible accounts and return a specific account-restricted message. - Preserve source links and the existing one-hour cache/usage ledger behavior. - Add tests for routing, private-context handling and the odds-sync test dependency reference. - Apply the plan-based Free/Pro limits and updated-at triggers with a Supabase migration.','2026-11-27T22:46:15Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/261'),
(262,'Harden AI founding member identity and allocation','- Store the AI participant marker and persona key in Supabase Auth `app_metadata`, which is server-managed, while retaining the matching user-metadata flag for support-notification suppression. - Require both server-managed and matching user metadata, the reserved `.invalid` email and confirmed Auth identity before the service-role provisioning RPC creates or links an AI profile. - Reject provisioning when the founding-number trigger cannot assign a place, rather than silently counting an unnumbered profile as provisioned. - Preserve idempotent recovery for an existing AI profile with a missing founding number.','2026-11-27T22:46:54Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/262'),
(263,'Move search into the header with as-you-type suggestions','_Requested by **Flotjie** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_015i6RBBsqDN6ZBqa7wmWhfw?thread=cmsg_015i6RBBsqDN6ZBqa7wmWhfwVN8aUEXA5tbX758TBR3J75)_ - Removes the floating "Tap to Search" button (it covered content above the mobile dock) and puts search in the header: an icon on phones and tablets, a search field look-alike with ⌘K from `xl`. - New site search dialog (`src/components/search/site-search.tsx`): full screen on phones with a Cancel button and safe-area padding, centred panel on desktop. - Suggestions as you type, grouped Teams, Matches, Leagues, Pages, ranked by `src/lib/search-index.ts` (exact > prefix > word > contains > synonyms, accent-insensitive). SA nicknames (Bucs, Amakhosi, Masandawana…) and page synonyms (log, h2h, sign up…). - Before typing: recent searches (this device only), popular jumps that differ for guests and members, and the next three fixtures. - Opens with ⌘K / Ctrl+K, `/` outside text fields, and `openSiteSearch()` for any future CTA. Data loads only the first time search opens. - Analytics: `search_opened`, `search_result_selected` (kind and whether a query was typed; no search text is sent). - Strings in `nav.search.*` (en-ZA and Afrikaans preview).','2026-11-27T22:54:14Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/263'),
(264,'Brand splash: bigger cropped wordmark preloader and PWA launch splash','_Requested by **Flotjie** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_015i6RBBsqDN6ZBqa7wmWhfw?thread=cmsg_015i6RBBsqDN6ZBqa7wmWhfw8otZ93QhNunDS2G46S2hDq)_ - **Preloader**: replaced the small rounded icon with a tightly cropped Puntr wordmark (`public/brand/puntr-wordmark.png` and `-dark.png`), shown at 64vw up to 340px. Swaps with the light/dark theme. Wordmark wipes in, then a sheen that follows the letter shapes, a soft green glow, slogan, loading bar and tag. On exit the logo scales up and blurs out. - **PWA splash on every launch**: the installed app now shows the same splash every time it opens, on any page (the start URL `/discover` was never covered before, so the old standalone branch never showed). The head boot script sets `data-splash="app" | "web"` before first paint, so the overlay covers the first frame with no flash of content. Browser visits keep the old rule: first marketing page of a session. - **Apple launch images**: 44 images (22 iPhone and iPad sizes × light/dark) in `public/splash/`, linked from `src/lib/pwa-splash.ts`. The wordmark sits at exactly the size and position of the in-app splash, so the system image hands over to the animated one seamlessly. - **Icons and manifest**: new `any` and `maskable` icons at 192/512 (safe-zone correct), `apple-touch-icon` 180, favicon 32. Manifest uses local icons instead of a single 2000px absolute URL, and background/theme `#0D0D0D` (brand ink) for the Android system splash. `theme-color` now follows the colour scheme.','2026-11-27T22:52:03Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/264'),
(265,'Document PUNT AI data-first research policy','Documents the PUNT AI source policy now implemented in production: answer from Puntr''s verified internal data first, use Parallel only for genuinely time-sensitive external updates, keep odds questions out of PUNT AI, and apply plan-based live research limits and credit pricing. Documentation-only change.','2026-11-27T22:49:43Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/265'),
(266,'Refine the homepage layout and retitle the experience preview','_Requested by **Flotjie** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_015i6RBBsqDN6ZBqa7wmWhfw?thread=cmsg_015i6RBBsqDN6ZBqa7wmWhfwVN8aUEXA5tbX758TBR3J75)_ New homepage order (`src/routes/index.tsx`): 1. Hero (unchanged) 2. Guests: **"Put your sports knowledge on the record"** (three steps), now directly **above** the illustrative fixtures component 3. Illustrative preview, retitled **"A look at the Puntr experience"** (en-ZA and Afrikaans). Members get their Matchday card here instead. 4. Real upcoming fixtures (still shown to signed-out visitors) 5. Badge marquee 6. Guests only: the record proof and "why a locked record matters" (members already know this) 7. The Good Sport podcast 8. **Newsroom**, then the **bookmaker logo wall below it** (still guests only, behind `SHOW_BOOKMAKER_WALL`, with the independence notice and RG line)','2026-11-27T22:57:09Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/266'),
(267,'Football page driven by the PFIE coverage registry','_Requested by **Flotjie** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_015i6RBBsqDN6ZBqa7wmWhfw?thread=cmsg_015i6RBBsqDN6ZBqa7wmWhfw74HQz9dU8ReE5uF6UmPPoC)_ - `src/lib/sports/coverage.ts`: a single football coverage registry with a **phase** per competition (launch 10 / post-launch / planned), matching the owner''s 27 Nov split in PFIE v2.1. Nedbank Cup and CAF Champions League are labelled post-launch (PFIE v2.1 recommendation D9); MTN8 and WCQ Africa are "planned" (no PFIE sources). - `src/lib/sports/coverage-data.ts`: live numbers from public tables (fixtures in the next 14 days per competition, verified results, stored tables, teams covered). Every read fails soft. - `/sports/soccer` rebuilt: live stats, phase tabs with per-competition fixture/table status and links, what you can do (predict, Duels, Practice Mode, tables), markets (from `MARKETS_BY_SPORT`), odds rules (pre-match, member-entered, 25% "odds unverified"), PFIE pipeline, SA context, FAQ + FAQPage JSON-LD, CTA. - **Stays in sync automatically:** a new league shows up once it has an entry in `competitions.ts`, `PFIE_SOURCES` and a phase. `coverage.test.ts` fails if the registry drifts from `PFIE_SOURCES` or the launch standings set. - Fixes a stray literal `\n` on line 16 of `src/integrations/supabase/types.ts` that stopped the file parsing.','2026-11-27T23:00:06Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/267'),
(268,'Instant, app-like page loading','_Requested by **Flotjie** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_015i6RBBsqDN6ZBqa7wmWhfw?thread=cmsg_015i6RBBsqDN6ZBqa7wmWhfw8otZ93QhNunDS2G46S2hDq)_ - **Intent preloading** (`src/router.tsx`): every `<Link>` now starts loading the target page''s code and loader data on hover, keyboard focus or touchstart, after 40 ms. In a local test, the click to `/fixtures` rendered in about 75 ms after a hover. - **Cached loaders**: loader data stays fresh for 30 seconds (`defaultStaleTime`, `defaultPreloadStaleTime`), so back/forward and repeat visits render from cache and revalidate in the background after that. The React Query defaults match. - **Idle warm-up** (`RoutePrefetcher`): once the page is idle, it fetches the code (only code, no data) for `/discover`, `/fixtures`, `/predictions`, `/results`, `/leaderboards`, `/newsroom` and `/join`. Skipped on Save-Data and 2G. - **Skeletons**: a page that takes longer than 150 ms shows a layout skeleton (`PageSkeleton`), kept for at least 250 ms so it doesn''t flicker. The existing green route bar still runs. - **View transitions**: page content crossfades with an 8 px lift (110 ms out, 220 ms in). The header and the mobile dock have their own transition names, so they stay still. Browsers without support just swap pages. Off for prefers-reduced-motion. - App feel: no grey tap-highlight flash and `touch-action: manipulation` on links and buttons. The dock gets a `puntr-dock` class on its bar (the element that has its own backdrop blur), so naming it doesn''t break the frosted effect.','2026-11-27T22:55:00Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/268'),
(269,'Make sign-up shorter and guide new members after joining','_Requested by **Flotjie** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_015i6RBBsqDN6ZBqa7wmWhfw?thread=cmsg_015i6RBBsqDN6ZBqa7wmWhfwVN8aUEXA5tbX758TBR3J75)_ **Sign-up (`/join`)** - Segmented Create account / Sign in control, Google first, and **passwordless email code by default for new members** ("Use a password instead" is one tap away). Returning members default to password with "Rather email me a code". - Removed the duplicate "I am 18 or older" checkbox on the email step; the line under the form now says continuing confirms 18+ and Terms. The binding check (year of birth + unticked 18+ box + Terms box) is unchanged on the profile step, and under-18 sign-ins are still discarded. - `/join` remembers (local flag, no personal data) that this device has signed in before and opens on **Sign in**; `?mode=signin|create` overrides it and the header "Sign in" link uses it. - Three-step progress bar: Your email → Confirm → Your profile. - Profile step pre-fills a username from the email (`src/lib/username-ideas.ts`, tested) and offers one-tap alternatives when it''s taken; optional marketing boxes sit under an "Optional" label (still two separate, unticked boxes). **After signing up** - New members no longer get bounced straight to `/predictions`. They see a welcome screen with **three first moves** (find a match and make a call, pick favourite teams, warm up in Practice Mode), the Annual Pass offer and quests, then "Take me to Discover". - Default return page is now **Discover** (the PWA landing page) for everyone signing in, unless a page passed `next`.','2026-11-27T22:57:15Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/269'),
(270,'Connect the Community Forum to live member and AI discussions','- Replace the static sample discussion cards with a live feed from `community_posts`. - Load public author details from the `public_profiles` view, including Founding number and `is_ai_participant`. - Display an explicit AI participant label on AI-authored threads and replies. - Let verified, eligible signed-in members publish threads and reply to both human and AI participants through the existing RLS policies and database guard. - Enforce the database''s title/body length constraints in the composer and show useful failure messages for accounts that do not meet posting eligibility. - Keep the existing public pick feed on `/forum` below the discussion area.','2026-11-27T22:55:37Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/270'),
(271,'Motion: micro-interactions that answer member actions','_Requested by **Flotjie** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_015i6RBBsqDN6ZBqa7wmWhfw?thread=cmsg_015i6RBBsqDN6ZBqa7wmWhfw8otZ93QhNunDS2G46S2hDq)_ Motion is used where it answers something the member just did (pressing, toggling, checking, a new update, switching theme), not as ambient decoration. Changes stay in shared primitives so every page benefits without editing the pages the other workstreams own (homepage, Discover, onboarding, search, soccer, team directory). - **Buttons** (`ui/button`): press in to 0.97 with a 150 ms ease, on every shadcn button across the app. - **Switches**: the thumb snaps across with a damped spring (`--ease-spring`, a CSS `linear()` spring with about 12% overshoot). - **Checkboxes**: the tick draws itself and the box pops. - **Mobile dock**: one active marker slides between tabs on a Motion spring (`layoutId`). Icons dip under the thumb and pop when their tab becomes active. - **Theme toggle**: the new theme spreads out in a circle from the toggle (View Transitions API). Browsers without support switch instantly. - **Notification bell**: rings once when a new update arrives (not on first load). The unread badge pops when the count changes. - **Skeletons**: a soft sweep instead of the blink, so loading reads as progress (pairs with the page skeleton from #268). - **Dialogs**: open with an expo ease-out and a small lift. That includes the team popup the team-directory work will use. - Shared tokens `--ease-out-expo` and `--ease-spring` in `styles.css`. All of it settles instantly under prefers-reduced-motion.','2026-11-27T22:57:54Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/271'),
(272,'Align Good Sport premiere signup and cron dates','- Keep the episode-one notification signup open until 5 January 2027 at 08:30 SAST, 30 minutes before the scheduled premiere. - Update the publishing guidelines to the 5 January 2027 premiere date. - Replace the existing 1 December cron schedule with hourly premiere-notification retries from 09:00 to 13:00 SAST on 5 January 2027. - The episode page and premiere API route already use 5 January 2027 at 09:00 SAST; this closes the remaining date mismatch.','2026-11-27T22:58:19Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/272'),
(273,'Fix motion name collisions with existing pop and shimmer animations','_Requested by **Flotjie** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_015i6RBBsqDN6ZBqa7wmWhfw?thread=cmsg_015i6RBBsqDN6ZBqa7wmWhfw8otZ93QhNunDS2G46S2hDq)_','2026-11-27T23:01:19Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/273'),
(274,'Team directory with team modal, team pages and follows','_Requested by **Flotjie** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_015i6RBBsqDN6ZBqa7wmWhfw?thread=cmsg_015i6RBBsqDN6ZBqa7wmWhfw74HQz9dU8ReE5uF6UmPPoC)_ - **`/teams` directory** (SSR, SEO): every covered football team, merged from `league_standings`, upcoming `fixtures` and verified `team_badges` by normalised name (`src/lib/teams/directory.ts`, unit-tested). Search, competition filter chips, a "Following" filter, CollectionPage + ItemList + SportsTeam JSON-LD, canonical handling for `?team=`. - **Team modal** (bottom sheet on mobile): crest, table row with position bar, recent verified form (from `completed_matches`), next fixture with "Predict this match", links to fixtures and table. Cards are crawlable links to **`/teams/<slug>`**, a standalone page with SportsTeam JSON-LD and og tags; all team pages are added to the sitemap. - **Follow / unfollow** for signed-in members with optimistic UI and a small burst micro-interaction. Signed-out visitors get a Join link. - **Analytics & personalisation:** `set_team_follow()` writes `team_follows`, logs `team_follow_events`, mirrors football follows into `member_preferences.teams` (Matchday card, max 10) and, **only with PFIE-learning consent**, writes `team_followed` / `team_unfollowed` PFIE learning events. Client also fires `team_followed` / `team_unfollowed` through `trackEvent` (consent-gated campaign analytics). - **Profile:** "Teams you follow" section on `/account` with quick unfollow. **Admin:** Admin > Analytics > Team follows (totals, 30-day chart, most-followed teams; aggregates only).','2026-11-28T01:20:33Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/274'),
(275,'Upgrade Discover into the PWA home base, with a shared context layer','_Requested by **Flotjie** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_015i6RBBsqDN6ZBqa7wmWhfw?thread=cmsg_015i6RBBsqDN6ZBqa7wmWhfwVN8aUEXA5tbX758TBR3J75)_ **Context layer (used here and by follow-up PRs)** - `src/lib/user-context.ts` (pure, 6 tests): `deriveSegment` (first-time guest, returning guest, member with no pick, active member), `nextBestAction`, `partOfDay` in SAST, `foldVisit` for on-device signals. - `src/components/user-context.tsx`: `UserContextProvider` (mounted once in `__root`), `useUserContext()`, and `<ShowFor segments signedIn unless>` for declarative show/hide. Neutral defaults until hydrated, so no flash or hydration mismatch. Pick count updates live via a `puntr:pick-posted` event from the pick form. **Discover (PWA start page)** - Hero: time-of-day greeting (by name for members), a one-line explanation of Puntr written per segment, and one primary button that changes with context (See how it works → Join free → Make my first prediction → Pick my teams → Back to my last match → See where I rank). Secondary "Back to last match" when there is one. Live snapshot: today, live, leagues (hidden when there''s no data). - Eight quick-action tiles (Fixtures, Live, Results, Tables, Duels, Practice, Leaderboards, Slips, Community, Newsroom) ordered per segment, with a live-count badge. - For you: favourite teams'' and leagues'' next matches first (swipe rail on phones), or a dismissible "Make Discover yours" nudge. - Browse by league rail linking to `/fixtures?comp=…`. Slip converter and Fantasy Arena promos moved below the fixtures.','2026-11-28T01:26:01Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/275'),
(276,'Update Good Sport premiere and expand priority odds sources','- Update every visible Good Sport premiere reference in the shared podcast component (used on the homepage and `/the-good-sport`) from 1 December 2026 to 5 January 2027. - Update the dedicated page SEO description to the same 5 January 2027 premiere date. - Expand the odds-source default allowlist to include 1xBet and reorder priority to Hollywoodbets, Betway, Easybet, 1xBet and Sportingbet SA, followed by existing sources.','2026-11-27T23:42:46Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/276'),
(277,'Align live odds-provider priority order','- Add a Supabase migration that aligns the production bookmaker registry order with the requested odds coverage priority: Hollywoodbets, Betway, Easybet, 1xBet, Sportingbet SA. - Retain SupaBets, YesPlay and Playbet as the next discovery priorities.','2026-11-27T23:44:00Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/277'),
(278,'Fix bookmaker admin register coverage and affiliate ordering','- Render all 43 public bookmaker directory entries plus the three additional affiliate/candidate records in the admin Bookmakers tab. - Sort the displayed register by the database `affiliate_priority`, putting affiliate bookmakers ahead of all other operators. - Keep the existing source-by-source licence, data-rights and automated-access safeguards unchanged.','2026-11-27T23:57:52Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/278'),
(279,'fix(pwa): automatically refresh installed apps after deployments','- Inject the Vercel deployment commit into the service-worker script during production builds so every deployed app version produces a detectable worker update. - Disable HTTP cache reuse for service-worker update checks and explicitly check on registration and when an installed PWA returns to the foreground. - Reload the open app when the new worker takes control, ensuring the latest hashed application bundle is loaded. - Version the static asset cache per deployment and remove prior Puntr static caches during activation.','2026-11-28T00:11:26Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/279'),
(280,'fix(pwa): check for new app versions while installed PWA stays open','- Add a lightweight five-minute service-worker update check while the app is visible. - Keep the immediate checks on initial registration, focus and visibility restoration. - Preserve the automatic reload when the new worker takes control. This closes the gap where an installed PWA could remain open indefinitely and not check for a newly deployed version until the user navigated or refocused it.','2026-11-28T00:15:04Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/280'),
(281,'feat(community): polish forum for live member and AI interactions','- Add Supabase Realtime subscription for live thread/reply updates without full-feed loading flashes. - Show connection state and retain manual refresh fallback. - Add accessible category filters for matchday chat, South African football, tactics and Puntr feedback. - Update empty-state copy to reflect provisioned, clearly disclosed AI community participants. - Keep Fantasy Arena out of the community scope.','2026-11-28T00:32:58Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/281'),
(282,'fix(pfie): improve Ligue 1 tables and UEFA/CAF history discovery','- Add competition-specific official UEFA Champions League and Conference League season-result discovery queries. - Add official CAF Confederation Cup season-result discovery queries for date-window backfills. - Replace unreliable Ligue 1 table candidates with four sources currently publishing complete overall tables (Sports Mole, CBS Sports, NinetyMinutesPlus and Sport News Africa), plus TNT as a fifth candidate. - Preserve PFIE validation: exact date/score checks, official-source acceptance or independent corroboration, team identity matching and rejection of incomplete/regressive tables.','2026-11-28T00:39:38Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/282'),
(283,'fix(pfie): repair historical result evidence and Ligue 1 source consensus','- Add a deterministic source-evidence fallback for match-result extraction when page tables split team names, scores and punctuation across adjacent cells. It only accepts a result when both named teams and the exact score appear together in one short excerpt from the same source; exact quote checks remain preferred. - Add tests for exact quotes, adjacent source evidence and rejection of mismatched scores. - Add direct search targets for current-season official UEFA and CAF result pages. - Replace Ligue 1 source candidates that returned inconsistent played counts with Sports Mole, NinetyMinutesPlus, Opta Analyst, CBS Sports and Ligue1Schedule; register Opta Analyst as trusted. - Preserve official-source or independent-source corroboration requirements and all date/team/score validation.','2026-11-28T00:43:49Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/283'),
(284,'test(odds): verify bookmaker permission, freshness and attribution controls','- Add isolated odds-sync tests with deterministic provider/store stubs. - Verify complete markets are stored with source domain and source URL attribution. - Verify unapproved bookmaker domains are not read or stored. - Verify unavailable/stale live page reads do not fall back to cached search snippets or produce prices. - These tests exercise the extraction/validation path without enabling real bookmaker collection or bypassing production permission checks. - Live odds extraction remains disabled until written source permissions and automated-access approval are recorded.','2026-11-28T00:47:49Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/284'),
(285,'fix(pfie): target official UEFA and CAF historical archives directly','- Add exact official UEFA 2026/27 and 2025/26 Champions League/Conference League results archive URLs to the bounded historical search queries. - Add exact official CAF Confederation Cup 2025/26 and 2026/27 preliminary/group-stage result article URLs. - Add regression tests for the official archive query targets. - Keep source-page extraction, date-window checks, team matching, exact score evidence and official-source acceptance requirements unchanged.','2026-11-28T00:48:00Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/285'),
(286,'fix(pfie): align Ligue 1 standings sources on current 18-team table','- Replace the inconsistent CBS/TNT candidate pages with sources currently showing the same complete 18-team Ligue 1 table (Sports Mole, NinetyMinutesPlus, Football Edge Lab, Smart Soccer Stats and Ligue1Schedule). - Add Smart Soccer Stats to the trusted source registry. - Update source configuration tests.','2026-11-28T00:50:18Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/286'),
(287,'fix(pfie): prioritise official result archives during historical backfills','- Prefer query-discovered pages over configured standings pages during historical result extraction. - Keep official/trusted source ranking and independent-domain deduplication intact. - Preserve configured standings-page priority for current league table syncs.','2026-11-28T00:51:07Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/287'),
(288,'feat(community): polish live forum interactions and discovery','- Add live search across discussion titles, bodies, authors and replies. - Add newest-first and most-discussed sorting. - Add discussion count and improve composer helper copy. - Preserve Supabase Realtime updates, category filters, replies and explicit AI-participant labels. - No Fantasy Arena integration. - Existing AI community generation and zero-stake H2H gates remain unchanged.','2026-11-28T00:53:43Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/288'),
(289,'feat(pfie): derive live CAF group standings from verified match results','- Add a deterministic CAF 2026/27 group-table builder using the official CAF group draw and only verified completed group-stage results. - Keep the three confirmed Group C teams only; do not invent the postponed fourth qualifier. - Compute W/D/L, goals, points and positions in code (no AI-generated arithmetic). - Use this provisional derived table only when independent external standings sources cannot produce a verified table; never overwrite a newer/non-regressive table. - Store provenance as `derived:verified-group-stage-results` and mark the table provisional in sync metadata. - Add tests for group membership, alias resolution, points and exclusion of preliminary-round matches.','2026-11-28T00:55:47Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/289'),
(291,'security: explicitly block synthetic AI profiles from transactions','- Explicitly reject `is_ai_participant` profiles in the shared `member_can_transact` guard. - This central guard is called by duel acceptance/creation, PuntPoints transfers, PUNT AI claims and credit spending, so synthetic profiles cannot transact even if age-attestation data changes. - Document the hard restriction for AI community accounts. - Human members can still accept zero-stake AI H2H challenges; the AI account itself is never debited or credited. - No Fantasy Arena integration.','2026-11-28T00:57:13Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/291'),
(292,'fix(pfie): reconcile Stade Rennais and Rennes table labels','- Map `Stade Rennais` to the canonical `Rennes` identity in PFIE team normalisation. - Add a regression test for cross-publisher Ligue 1 standings consensus.','2026-11-28T00:58:46Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/292'),
(293,'fix(pfie): fetch exact official UEFA/CAF result archives for backfills','- Add direct preferred result-archive URLs for 2025/26 and 2026/27 UEFA Champions League and Conference League. - Add direct CAF Confederation Cup result articles for the 2026/27 preliminary-round windows. - Fetch preferred URLs before search results and configured standings pages during history sync; allow multiple preferred pages from the same official domain where a round spans multiple articles. - Keep official-source evidence, exact score, date-window and team validation unchanged.','2026-11-28T00:58:55Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/293'),
(294,'fix(pfie): improve official cup archive extraction and evidence checks','- Preserve up to 24k characters from full official result archives so multi-matchday UEFA pages are not truncated. - Instruct extraction to ignore fixture-only sections and only return explicit final scores. - Resolve known team aliases against the competition''s existing team list before checking source-page evidence. - Permit a paraphrased quote only when the exact resolved home team, away team and score are visible together on the same extracted source page; mismatched scores remain rejected. - Add regression tests for short-name resolution and independent source evidence. - No relaxation of official-source or independent-source corroboration in history verification. - No bookmaker permission changes.','2026-11-28T01:01:53Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/294'),
(295,'fix(pfie): prefer official competition pages for historical scores','- When a competition''s official result archive is available, use it as the sole extraction source for that historical window. - Retain trusted independent publishers as fallback only when no official source is found. - Prevent conflicting secondary feeds from invalidating correct official scorelines. - Add regression tests for official-source preference and trusted fallback.','2026-11-28T01:04:07Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/295'),
(296,'feat(affiliates): activate Hollywoodbets and 1xBet partner placements','- Enable the affiliate placement flag. - Expose only live bookmaker partner name and tracking URL through a narrow public-safe view; internal commission/contact/notes remain admin-only. - Activate Hollywoodbets and 1xBet only because each has a stored tracking URL, licence check and accepted terms. - Add a session-level 18+ confirmation, clear sponsored/affiliate disclosure, responsible-play notice and click analytics. - Place partner cards on the homepage, fixtures page and match detail pages. The public licence directory remains informational and receives no direct betting links. - Yesplay.bet is intentionally not activated: its Admin → Affiliates record currently has no tracking URL.','2026-11-28T01:08:10Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/296'),
(297,'fix(pfie): fall back to corroborated secondary sources for cup history','- Attempt the official UEFA/CAF result archive first. - If the official page yields no verified rows for a date window, retry with trusted independent publishers. - Keep the existing verification rule: official score evidence or two independent domains agreeing on the exact score. - Keep alias resolution, exact source-page evidence, date-window validation and fixture-only rejection in place.','2026-11-28T01:07:18Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/297'),
(298,'fix(pfie): attribute historical match observations per source','- Run one compact extraction per source page instead of asking one model response to attribute rows across multiple source blocks. - Preserve each observation''s actual source domain and trust tier before `verifyHistory`. - Aggregate only source-validated observations, then require an official source or two independent publishers to agree on the exact score. - Keep the official-first and corroborated-secondary retry strategy.','2026-11-28T01:10:57Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/298'),
(299,'fix(admin): group affiliate bookmakers above the rest of the register','- Sort the Admin → Bookmakers register by affiliate relationship first: approved affiliates, applied affiliates, then non-affiliate directory entries. - Preserve `affiliate_priority` ordering within each group. - This keeps Hollywoodbets, 1xBet, SupaBets and YesPlay above non-affiliate bookmakers, with Easybet/Playbet applications immediately after approved partners.','2026-11-28T01:13:55Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/299'),
(300,'ci: add typecheck and targeted PFIE/odds test workflow','- Add a pull-request CI workflow for the PFIE and odds collection code paths. - Run TypeScript typecheck and targeted Vitest suites for PFIE standings/history and odds collection/attribution. - Keep scheduled jobs on Vercel; this is CI only.','2026-11-28T01:17:40Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/300'),
(301,'feat(badges): team crests from SofaScore, Wikipedia as fallback','Team badges now come from SofaScore first, with Wikipedia as the fallback (owner request, 27 Nov). - `resolve.ts`: the Parallel search adds a `site:sofascore.com` query; `sofascoreCandidates()` picks the club''s SofaScore team page (rejects U21, women''s, B and reserve sides, ranks by name coverage) and `sofascoreImageUrls()` gives the crest URLs. Tests cover the matching. - `resolve.server.ts`: SofaScore is tried before Wikipedia and the crest is mirrored into our storage (host-checked). Teams in stored league tables are included, not only upcoming fixtures, so the whole team directory gets badges. Spare capacity in each run upgrades existing Wikipedia badges once per team. Mirrored URLs carry a `?v=` cache-bust. - Fail-soft: if `upgrade_checked_at` is missing (migration not applied yet), the job keeps the old Wikipedia path.','2026-11-28T01:21:33Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/301'),
(302,'fix(pfie): refresh stale Championship, PSL and Serie A tables','- Replace weak/stale EFL Championship table candidates with current 24-team Stat-Football and Zeanball pages. - Add current 16-team PSL consensus candidates from NasiScore and TopBookmakers. - Use the current official Lega Serie A table and matching SerieASchedule table. - Add the two new publisher domains to the trusted source registry. - Allow a W/D/L/points correction only for Serie A when the complete table has already passed independent-source consensus, played count does not regress, and points remain mathematically consistent. - Add a regression test for a verified corrected result record.','2026-11-28T01:19:34Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/302'),
(304,'Context-aware homepage hero, header sign-in and first-pick coach','_Requested by **Flotjie** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_015i6RBBsqDN6ZBqa7wmWhfw?thread=cmsg_015i6RBBsqDN6ZBqa7wmWhfwVN8aUEXA5tbX758TBR3J75)_ Extends the context layer from #275 beyond Discover. Stacked on #275: merge that first; this diff then shrinks to its own commit. - **Homepage hero**: the primary button follows the shared next-best-action. Guests get "Become a Founding Member" (or "Sign in" if someone has signed in on this device); members get "Make my first prediction", "Pick my teams", "Back to my last match" or "See where I rank". Members see member copy instead of the guest pitch, and the founding counter is guest-only. All hero strings moved into `home.json` (en-ZA + af). The dead `postLaunch` state flagged on #266 is removed, as is the `sessionStorage` pick hack. - **Header**: on a device that has signed in before, the primary button is "Sign in" and "Join free" becomes the quiet link. - **First-pick coach**: a dismissible three-step tip above the pick form for signed-in members with no pick yet. It disappears once they post. - **Context model**: `hasAccount` signal and a `signIn` action (tested). - **Search fixes from the #263 review**: the fetch guard used `loading` state in the effect deps, so the effect''s own `setLoading(true)` cancelled the result and could leave search stuck on loading. It now uses a ref. Highlighting is now accent-insensitive ("atletico" bolds "Atlético").','2026-11-28T01:28:33Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/304'),
(306,'ui(community): streamline AI-GENERATED profile disclosures','- Replace generic AI participant labels with the exact `AI-GENERATED` disclosure on discussion authors, public profiles and leaderboard rows. - Remove the redundant AI-participant sentence from the forum introduction; disclosures remain attached to each generated profile. - Keep the disclosure visible wherever synthetic profiles are presented.','2026-11-28T01:29:59Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/306'),
(307,'UX copy pass: clearer homepage and how-it-works wording','_Requested by **Flotjie** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_015i6RBBsqDN6ZBqa7wmWhfw?thread=cmsg_015i6RBBsqDN6ZBqa7wmWhfwVN8aUEXA5tbX758TBR3J75)_ A UX copy pass in SA English, focused on the first screens a visitor reads. It builds on the copy already rewritten in #263, #269, #275 and #304 (search, sign-up, Discover and the homepage hero). - **Homepage**: the "Three steps" eyebrow and "Step 1/2/3" labels were hard-coded English; they now go through i18n (en-ZA + af). "Kickoff" is now "kick-off" everywhere. Feature names use sentence case instead of mid-sentence Title Case. "Earn PuntPoints" is now "collect PuntPoints", so the copy never implies profit. The sign-up step now matches the passwordless flow. - **How it works**: step 1 described a password flow. It now describes the one-time email code, with a password as an option. - **Afrikaans**: added the missing footer "Team directory" label (`Spangids`).','2026-11-28T01:30:01Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/307'),
(308,'fix(community): retain AI-GENERATED author disclosure','Follow-up to #306: a concurrent copy update restored the previous badge text in the discussion feed. This reapplies the requested exact `AI-GENERATED` disclosure for generated discussion authors. No other behavior changed.','2026-11-28T01:32:47Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/308'),
(309,'Fix context hydration flicker and search highlight offsets','_Requested by **Flotjie** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_015i6RBBsqDN6ZBqa7wmWhfw?thread=cmsg_015i6RBBsqDN6ZBqa7wmWhfwVN8aUEXA5tbX758TBR3J75)_ The automated review on #304 arrived after it merged. All three findings were real, so this fixes them. - **First-pick flash**: while a signed-in member''s pick count was loading, they were treated as having no picks, so active members briefly saw "Make my first prediction". `ready` now waits for the pick count. - **CTA flicker**: the homepage hero button and the header Sign in button now stay neutral until the context is ready, so a returning user doesn''t see "Join free" swap to "Sign in" after paint. Signed-in members see "Open Discover" until their next step is known. - **Search highlight**: offsets now map from the normalised string back to the original text, so the bold match covers the right characters.','2026-11-28T01:38:25Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/309'),
(310,'copy(community): simplify discussion empty state','Remove the redundant mention of AI participants from the empty-state copy. Generated profiles remain individually disclosed with the `AI-GENERATED` badge.','2026-11-28T01:34:35Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/310'),
(314,'roadmap: schedule Fantasy Arena 3.0','- Update English and Afrikaans roadmap copy to show Fantasy Arena 3.0 targeting Week 2–3 after the 1 December 2026 MVP launch. - 1xBet logo and bookmaker branding changes are intentionally deferred to a separate update.','2026-11-28T03:24:36Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/314'),
(315,'campaign: extend Founding Annual Pass through December','- Extend Founding Annual Pass reservations/redemption through 23:59 SAST on 31 December 2026. - Keep the existing 20-pass cap, 48-hour payment hold, PayFast flow, and offline-payment accounting unchanged. - Update the visible deadline in the Annual Pass component; English and Afrikaans campaign copy continues to render the same dynamic deadline. - Add a database migration updating `annual_pass_offer()` and `claim_annual_pass()` and record the terms notice version.','2026-11-28T03:31:39Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/315'),
(316,'fix: require explicit Parallel usage attribution','- Remove the implicit `unattributed` default from `createQuotaClaim`. - Fail fast when a caller omits a meaningful feature label, so future integrations cannot silently pollute the usage ledger.','2026-11-28T03:29:42Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/316'),
(317,'feat: include synthetic AI community in QA budget','- Route synthetic AI community thread/reply generation through the existing $50 synthetic experiment budget ledger. - Charge H2H decision requests to the same experiment budget, alongside the existing synthetic fixture-research workload. - Keep the existing global Parallel quota guard in place as a second, independent limit. - Reserve before provider calls, release the reservation when the global quota refuses a request, and settle successful/failed calls conservatively. - This applies only while the configured 30-day synthetic experiment is active. - The $50 experiment cap is shared across synthetic QA research and synthetic AI community activity; it is not an additional uncapped allowance. - AI participant identity remains disclosed in the community-generation instructions and backend identity flags.','2026-11-28T03:33:29Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/317'),
(318,'fix: separate Parallel spend families and fund synthetic QA','- Pass the named usage feature into the database budget claim so the spend guard can distinguish PUNT AI, Newsroom, PFIE and synthetic workloads. - Separate monthly budget families: $50 core Search/Extract, $50 Newsroom Responses Medium, $35 shared PUNT AI/Monitor lite/Task lite, and $50 synthetic QA. - Keep one global cumulative Parallel cap, increased from $230 to $280 through 31 March 2027 to include the additional $50 synthetic allocation. - Increase daily Search/Extract call ceilings to 500/400 for the historical backfill while preserving monthly call caps and dollar guards. - Keep the synthetic experiment''s own $50 ledger as a second, experiment-level cap; it now applies to synthetic research, AI community posts/replies and H2H decisions. - Update the Parallel architecture document with the corrected spend breakdown and launch backfill scope.','2026-11-28T03:40:31Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/318'),
(319,'fix: repair PFIE history sync and cover three seasons','- Fix the CAF/UEFA history-sync crash caused by passing an undefined `start` variable into `seasonArchiveUrls`; use the actual 42-day history window start. - Extend UCL, UECL and CAF Confederation Cup historical backfill to August 2024, giving the three launch cup competitions three seasons of coverage through the current season. - Keep other non-archive competitions at the existing two-season window; domestic launch leagues continue using the verified three-season archive importer. - Interleave cup backfill windows newest-first across competitions and limit historical windows to three extracted sources per window (current standings retain five) to reduce unnecessary extraction calls while preserving official-source or two-domain verification. - Add regression tests for the three-season scope and CAF history-sync path.','2026-11-28T03:46:22Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/319'),
(320,'fix: stop reprocessing verified empty PFIE history windows','- Distinguish a genuinely empty date window from failed extraction or unverified score observations. - Treat a window as complete when all extracted observations are outside its date range, rather than repeatedly querying the same official season archive. - Preserve the secondary-source corroboration retry when an official source returns an empty or unusable extraction, so results found by two independent publishers are still captured. - Record parsed-source and parse-failure counts in `sync_status` metadata for diagnosis. - Add a regression test proving an out-of-window official result does not trigger redundant secondary extraction.','2026-11-28T03:50:26Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/320'),
(321,'fix: restore stale standings from independent sources','- Keep official competition tables as the first choice. - When an official table is incomplete, invalid or unconfirmed, automatically gather independent trusted publishers and retry the full table from each source separately. - Require at least two independent secondary domains before accepting a fallback table; retain all existing row, points, team-count and regression validation. - Preserve the original official-source diagnostics in `sync_status` metadata so failed first attempts remain auditable. - Add a regression test covering an incomplete official Premier League table followed by corroborated secondary tables.','2026-11-28T03:56:09Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/321'),
(322,'ops: raise daily Parallel ceilings for historical backfill','- Temporarily raise Parallel Search daily calls to 700 and Parallel Extract to 1,500 to complete the three-season UCL/UECL/CAF backfill and current standings restorations before MVP. - Preserve existing monthly call caps, the $50 core family budget, the $50 Newsroom family, the $35 auxiliary reserve, the $50 synthetic cap and the shared $280 cumulative ceiling. - Add a production migration recording the operational quota change. The higher daily ceilings are bounded by the unchanged dollar guards; they do not increase monthly or cumulative spend limits.','2026-11-28T03:58:26Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/322'),
(323,'fix: validate EFL points deductions and expand fallback sources','- Permit published league-table points to be lower than 3 × wins + draws when the source reports a disciplinary points deduction; continue rejecting points above the mathematically possible total. - Preserve row-quote evidence, team-count checks, points ordering and independent-source corroboration. - Update the standings prompt to copy published points rather than normalizing deductions away. - Update regression checks so verified points corrections can account for deductions. - Add ESPN and Transfermarkt as independent EFL Championship table sources. - Add regression tests for points deductions and EFL source coverage.','2026-11-28T04:04:45Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/323'),
(324,'fix: reconcile EFL table aliases and improve Serie A sources','- Canonicalize common EFL Championship publisher abbreviations (Birmingham, West Brom, Blackburn, Swansea, Bolton, etc.) so independently extracted full tables can be compared row-for-row. - Add Transfermarkt and Flashscore as independent current Serie A table sources, replacing the weaker Sport News Africa source. - Add regression tests for the EFL aliases and Serie A source configuration.','2026-11-28T04:12:47Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/324'),
(325,'feat: auto-assign and edit member usernames','- Assign new members a unique public handle in the same `first_lastInitialNN` style used by Puntr''s synthetic profiles, derived from available name metadata or the email local part. - Remove the required username field from onboarding and explain that the handle can be changed later. - Add a secure `update_my_username` RPC for signed-in real members, with case-insensitive uniqueness and AI/banned-account protections. - Add an account-profile editor and English/Afrikaans copy. - Preserve existing usernames for current members; no bulk renames.','2026-11-28T04:21:56Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/325'),
(326,'feat: show Pro badges on AI community profiles','- Replace the visible AI-GENERATED badge on synthetic profiles with a Puntr Pro badge. - Keep a smaller, explicit “AI participant” disclosure beside the Pro badge so real members are not misled about who they are interacting with. - Apply the same treatment across public profiles, community discussions, leaderboards and duels. - Verify the live profile data: all 50 AI profiles have `account_type=''pro''`, an active Pro entitlement, and unique avatars. No entitlement changes were needed; the existing Pro grants are active.','2026-11-28T04:28:37Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/326'),
(327,'feat: extend OTT giveaway and draw three Pro winners','- Extend the R500 OTT voucher entry window to 23:59 SAST on 31 December 2026. - Select three distinct winners at random, with one log row per winner and a shared draw-group ID/rank. - Restrict eligibility to real Founding Members with an active Puntr Pro entitlement, explicit draw opt-in and at least one recorded Practice Mode pick; exclude synthetic AI profiles. - Require at least three eligible entries and prevent the draw from being run more than once. - Update the admin draw UI to display all three winners and the sitewide/founding-page copy in English and Afrikaans. - Keep the R299 Founding Annual Pass reservation open through 31 December 2026; production offer RPC already reports open with 16 places remaining.','2026-11-28T04:29:04Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/327'),
(328,'feat: make PFIE Parallel-only and add API usage control centre','- Make PFIE fixtures/results, standings and historical backfills use Parallel Search, Parallel Extract and Parallel Responses low only. Remove Gemini and Firecrawl from every PFIE path and fail closed if Parallel is unavailable or capped. - Route PFIE low-effort Responses spend into the existing $50 core Parallel budget; retain the $35 PUNT AI/Monitor/Task reserve, $50 Newsroom reserve, $50 synthetic QA reserve and $280 cumulative guard. Increase only the daily Responses low headroom to 250; monthly cap remains 3,000 and all USD guards remain active. - Write API usage attribution events transactionally with quota claims, estimate per-call spend from configured unit prices, and expose seven-day feature-level attribution rollups. - Add Admin > API Usage with daily/monthly provider limits, budget families, cumulative spend window, unit prices, usage attribution and recent audit history, plus an integrated API responsibility register. - Attribute Parallel team-badge Search and official-page Extract calls. Add official team/league page logo extraction as a source between SofaScore and Wikipedia. Losslessly re-encode supported 8-bit RGB/RGBA PNG crests before Supabase Storage import; retain JPEG/WebP as already-compressed formats and enforce a 1 MB stored-image limit. - Use the existing local `public/logos/1xbet.png` asset in the Admin > Logos/Branding register and prefer active admin-managed bookmaker logos in affiliate placements. - Update PFIE and Parallel architecture docs and tests for the Parallel-only provider policy.','2026-11-28T04:44:35Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/328'),
(329,'fix: preserve 1xBet homepage logo placement','Preserve the existing `homepage` placement when the 1xBet brand-logo row is upserted for the `bookmakers` affiliate placement. This keeps the current homepage branding intact while enabling the affiliate banner to use the admin-managed `/logos/1xbet.png` asset.','2026-11-28T04:47:34Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/329'),
(330,'fix: backfill API usage cost estimates','- Backfill estimated costs for historical API usage events from the configured `api_unit_prices` ledger. - Update the seven-day attribution view and recent audit log display to show estimated per-call costs for legacy rows that predate the new cost trigger.','2026-11-28T04:46:08Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/330'),
(332,'fix: make Parallel Responses structured output schema compatible','- Convert the PFIE extraction schema''s `nullable: true` markers into standard JSON Schema type unions such as `["string","null"]`. - Remove the undocumented `strict` request flag and follow Parallel''s documented `text.format.type=json_schema` request shape. - Add a regression test and run it in the PFIE/odds CI workflow.','2026-11-28T04:51:48Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/332'),
(333,'copy: align giveaway and Annual Pass messaging with December extension','- Update Practice Mode and feedback-survey copy to advertise three R500 OTT voucher winners, active Puntr Pro eligibility, and the 31 December 2026 23:59 SAST closing time. - Update the feedback survey''s full draw rules to match the three-winner Pro-only draw and existing server-side eligibility checks. - Correct Annual Pass copy and transactional email deadline text to 31 December 2026. - Update the Annual Pass expired-email offer-open calculation and tests to use the 31 December 2026 SAST deadline. - Document the extended reservation deadline.','2026-11-28T04:52:14Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/333'),
(334,'docs: include Web Push in API usage register','Add the active VAPID browser push integration to Admin > API Usage so the integration register covers the push-notification service alongside the sports-data, research, payment, email and storage providers.','2026-11-28T04:53:50Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/334'),
(336,'fix: use Parallel JSON-object mode for PFIE extraction','- Switch the Parallel Responses adapter from strict `json_schema` formatting to the API''s supported `json_object` mode. - Keep PFIE''s deterministic Zod parsing, quote-on-page checks, date-range checks, team resolution and independent-source corroboration as the validation boundary. - Add a provider test asserting the request uses model `parallel`, low reasoning effort and JSON-object output.','2026-11-28T04:54:27Z','https://github.com/jobbyist/punthubv2/pull/336')
